1
00:00:04,705 --> 00:00:07,875
♪ IN THE NOT-TOO-DISTANT
FUTURE ♪

2
00:00:07,875 --> 00:00:11,112
♪ NEXT SUNDAY, A.D. ♪

3
00:00:11,112 --> 00:00:13,948
♪ THERE WAS A GUY
NAMED JOEL ♪

4
00:00:13,948 --> 00:00:17,418
♪ NOT TOO DIFFERENT
FROM YOU OR ME ♪

5
00:00:17,418 --> 00:00:20,288
♪ HE WORKED
AT GIZMONIC INSTITUTE ♪

6
00:00:20,288 --> 00:00:23,758
♪ JUST ANOTHER FACE
IN A RED JUMPSUIT ♪

7
00:00:23,758 --> 00:00:26,293
♪ HE DID A GOOD JOB
CLEANING UP THE PLACE ♪

8
00:00:26,293 --> 00:00:28,095
♪ BUT HIS BOSSES
DIDN’T LIKE HIM ♪

9
00:00:28,095 --> 00:00:30,498
♪ SO THEY SHOT HIM
INTO SPACE ♪

10
00:00:32,800 --> 00:00:35,970
♪ WE’LL SEND HIM
CHEESY MOVIES ♪

11
00:00:35,970 --> 00:00:39,173
- ♪ THE WORST WE CAN FIND ♪
- ♪ LA LA LA ♪

12
00:00:39,173 --> 00:00:42,043
♪ HE’LL HAVE TO SIT
AND WATCH THEM ALL ♪

13
00:00:42,043 --> 00:00:45,313
- ♪ AND WE’LL MONITOR HIS MIND ♪
- ♪ LA LA LA ♪

14
00:00:45,313 --> 00:00:48,315
♪ NOW KEEP IN MIND
JOEL CAN’T CONTROL ♪

15
00:00:48,315 --> 00:00:51,518
- ♪ WHERE THE MOVIES
BEGIN OR END ♪
- ♪ LA LA LA ♪

16
00:00:51,518 --> 00:00:54,755
♪ BECAUSE HE USED
THOSE SPECIAL PARTS ♪

17
00:00:54,755 --> 00:00:57,692
♪ TO MAKE HIS ROBOT FRIENDS ♪

18
00:00:59,360 --> 00:01:01,328
LET’S GO.

19
00:01:01,328 --> 00:01:02,630
- CAMBOT.
- PAN LEFT.

20
00:01:02,630 --> 00:01:03,932
HI, GIRL.

21
00:01:03,932 --> 00:01:05,733
WHAT A COOL GUY.

22
00:01:05,733 --> 00:01:07,302
A WISECRACKER.

23
00:01:07,302 --> 00:01:10,305
♪ IF YOU’RE WONDERING HOW
HE EATS AND BREATHES ♪

24
00:01:10,305 --> 00:01:13,140
- ♪ AND OTHER SCIENCE FACTS ♪
- ♪ LA LA LA ♪

25
00:01:13,140 --> 00:01:16,177
♪ THEN REPEAT TO YOURSELF
"IT’S JUST A SHOW ♪

26
00:01:16,177 --> 00:01:19,513
♪ "I SHOULD REALLY
JUST RELAX ♪

27
00:01:19,513 --> 00:01:22,350
♪ FOR... ♪

28
00:01:33,662 --> 00:01:36,563
OH! COME ON, GYPSY.

29
00:01:36,563 --> 00:01:38,032
I CAN’T HOLD
THIS POSITION FOREVER.

30
00:01:38,032 --> 00:01:39,267
I’M CRAMPING!
HURRY UP.

31
00:01:39,267 --> 00:01:41,135
ALL RIGHT, NEXT TIME GYPSY
DOES THE SPECIAL EFFECTS

32
00:01:41,135 --> 00:01:42,170
AND I’LL DIRECT.

33
00:01:42,170 --> 00:01:43,203
QUIET ON THE SET!

34
00:01:43,203 --> 00:01:45,407
IN THIS SCENE, CROW,

35
00:01:45,407 --> 00:01:46,808
YOU’RE A LITTLE GIRL,

36
00:01:46,808 --> 00:01:49,077
AND YOU CLIMBED UP
ON A STACK OF BOXES

37
00:01:49,077 --> 00:01:51,880
CONTAINING HIGHLY
FLAMMABLE PAJAMAS.

38
00:01:51,880 --> 00:01:53,347
YEAH.

39
00:01:53,347 --> 00:01:54,382
OKAY. ACTION.

40
00:01:54,382 --> 00:01:55,650
MAKE ’EM HOT.
FIRE IT UP.

41
00:01:55,650 --> 00:01:57,685
HI, EVERYBODY. WELCOME
TO THE SATELLITE OF LOVE.

42
00:01:57,685 --> 00:01:58,787
I’VE ALLOWED THE BOTS

43
00:01:58,787 --> 00:02:01,890
TO TAPE A SPONTANEOUS,
FUNNY HOME VIDEO

44
00:02:01,890 --> 00:02:04,292
FOR AMERICA’S
GOOFIEST HOME VIDEOS.

45
00:02:04,292 --> 00:02:05,927
SO HERE’S TO RISKING YOUR LIFE

46
00:02:05,927 --> 00:02:08,530
IN THE INTEREST OF SOME
NATIONAL TV EXPOSURE.

47
00:02:08,530 --> 00:02:09,563
LET’S GO.

48
00:02:09,563 --> 00:02:10,998
HEY, WHERE’S MAGIC VOICE?

49
00:02:10,998 --> 00:02:12,200
AH,
SHE WALKED OFF THE SET.

50
00:02:12,200 --> 00:02:13,502
SHE’S SULKING
IN HER TRAILER.

51
00:02:13,502 --> 00:02:15,670
QUIET!
STAY IN CHARACTER, CROW.

52
00:02:15,670 --> 00:02:16,703
OKAY.

53
00:02:16,703 --> 00:02:17,905
YOU’RE A THREE-YEAR-OLD GIRL

54
00:02:17,905 --> 00:02:19,140
ON A BOX
OF FLAMMABLE PAJAMAS.

55
00:02:19,140 --> 00:02:20,175
START ACTING LIKE IT!

56
00:02:20,175 --> 00:02:21,843
HIT ’EM WITH THE FIRE, TOM!

57
00:02:21,843 --> 00:02:23,143
FIRE IN THE HOLE!

58
00:02:23,143 --> 00:02:25,413
I--I CHANGED MY MIND!

59
00:02:25,413 --> 00:02:27,415
[SCREAMING]

60
00:02:27,415 --> 00:02:30,218
I’M ON FIRE! OH,
WHAT A WORLD, WHAT A WORLD.

61
00:02:30,218 --> 00:02:31,352
WHAT A WOR--AAH!

62
00:02:32,853 --> 00:02:34,455
NOPE, IT’S YOU,
ALL RIGHT, CROW.

63
00:02:34,455 --> 00:02:37,292
OH, OKAY. LET’S WATCH THE TAPE.
SEE HOW IT TURNED OUT, OKAY?

64
00:02:37,292 --> 00:02:38,893
GO AHEAD.

65
00:02:41,897 --> 00:02:43,765
[LAUGHTER]

66
00:02:43,765 --> 00:02:45,933
AH, YOU’RE RIGHT.
THAT’S PRETTY FUNNY.

67
00:02:45,933 --> 00:02:46,968
THAT’S GREAT.

68
00:02:46,968 --> 00:02:48,770
NOW, UH, HOW YOU FEELING
ABOUT YOUR ARM?

69
00:02:48,770 --> 00:02:49,803
IT’S ALL GNARLED.

70
00:02:49,803 --> 00:02:51,172
I CAN MAKE YOU A NEW ONE
IF YOU LIKE.

71
00:02:51,172 --> 00:02:53,207
NO, I LIKE IT
ALL GNARLED LIKE THAT.

72
00:02:53,207 --> 00:02:54,675
IT LOOKS REAL TOUGH.

73
00:02:54,675 --> 00:02:57,645
OH, OKAY.
WELL, THE MADS ARE CALLING.

74
00:02:57,645 --> 00:02:59,747
AH, IT DOES MY HEART GOOD

75
00:02:59,747 --> 00:03:03,317
TO SEE CROW BURNED
BEYOND ALL RECOGNITION.

76
00:03:03,317 --> 00:03:05,253
OH, FRANK, UH, IT’S TIME

77
00:03:05,253 --> 00:03:07,788
TO REVEAL THIS WEEK’S
INVENTION EXCHANGE.

78
00:03:07,788 --> 00:03:08,823
[CRYING]

79
00:03:08,823 --> 00:03:10,392
OH, ACCEPT THE PAIN, FRANK.

80
00:03:10,392 --> 00:03:11,425
I KNOW.

81
00:03:11,425 --> 00:03:12,560
YOU’VE HEARD THE EXPRESSION

82
00:03:12,560 --> 00:03:14,862
"THAT’S A HARD PILL
TO SWALLOW."

83
00:03:14,862 --> 00:03:17,065
WELL, OUR INVENTION EXCHANGE
THIS WEEK IS JUST THAT.

84
00:03:17,065 --> 00:03:19,700
SOME HARD PILLS TO SWALLOW.

85
00:03:19,700 --> 00:03:21,335
YOU SEE THIS PILL
RIGHT HERE?

86
00:03:21,335 --> 00:03:23,503
THAT SHOULD BE EASY TO SWALLOW,
SHOULDN’T IT, FRANK?

87
00:03:23,503 --> 00:03:25,273
YES. IT SHOULD BE EASY,

88
00:03:25,273 --> 00:03:28,743
EXCEPT FOR THE THREE-PRONG
FISH-HOOK ATTACHED TO IT.

89
00:03:28,743 --> 00:03:30,645
UH, THIS PILL,
I’M NOT GONNA KID YOU,

90
00:03:30,645 --> 00:03:32,613
THIS IS VERY DIFFICULT
TO SWALLOW.

91
00:03:32,613 --> 00:03:34,482
IT’S A NOT-SO-TINY
TIME PILL

92
00:03:34,482 --> 00:03:36,650
COMPLETE WITH A LIVING GERBIL.

93
00:03:36,650 --> 00:03:38,352
TERRY, NO!
[CRYING CONTINUES]

94
00:03:38,352 --> 00:03:39,387
OH, TERRY, YES.

95
00:03:39,387 --> 00:03:40,588
IF YOU CAN KEEP IT DOWN,

96
00:03:40,588 --> 00:03:43,023
YOU HAVE A PET THAT KNOWS YOU
INSIDE AND OUT.

97
00:03:43,023 --> 00:03:45,527
TURN, FRANK.
AND COUGH.

98
00:03:45,527 --> 00:03:47,628
IF YOU HAVE TROUBLE
KEEPING ONE PILL DOWN,

99
00:03:47,628 --> 00:03:50,732
TRY OUR PILL NECKLACE
OF PICRIC ACID.

100
00:03:50,732 --> 00:03:53,467
105 CAPSULES ON A STRING.

101
00:03:53,467 --> 00:03:56,637
KEEP YOUR GAG REFLEX ACTIVE
TILL THE COWS COME HOME.

102
00:03:56,637 --> 00:03:58,840
THE LONGER
IT TAKES TO SWALLOW,

103
00:03:58,840 --> 00:04:00,408
THE HARDER IT GETS.

104
00:04:00,408 --> 00:04:02,543
YES. AND THE CHILDREN.

105
00:04:02,543 --> 00:04:05,813
- THE CHILDREN LOVE...
- AH, THE CHILDREN!

106
00:04:05,813 --> 00:04:08,348
VITAMIN SHAPES
SHAPED LIKE CARTOONS.

107
00:04:08,348 --> 00:04:10,017
WHIMSICAL SHAPES.
WHIMSICAL SHAPES.

108
00:04:10,017 --> 00:04:12,753
AND WOULDN’T IT BE HARD
ON ALL THOSE FLINTSTONE KIDS

109
00:04:12,753 --> 00:04:16,257
IF THEIR FAVORITE
CARTOON VITAMIN CAME...

110
00:04:16,257 --> 00:04:18,392
TURN, FRANK.

111
00:04:18,392 --> 00:04:20,495
LIFE-SIZE. HMM? HMM?

112
00:04:20,495 --> 00:04:23,665
BALL’S IN YOUR COURT,
JOEL.

113
00:04:23,665 --> 00:04:26,133
WELL, THAT IS DARK, SIRS.

114
00:04:26,133 --> 00:04:28,135
WELL, ANYWAY,
WE’VE GOTTEN TOGETHER

115
00:04:28,135 --> 00:04:31,172
AND COME UP WITH THIS CELEBRITY
HOME APPLIANCES,

116
00:04:31,172 --> 00:04:34,008
LIKE THIS,
THE EMILIO ESTE-PEZ.

117
00:04:34,008 --> 00:04:37,012
JUST LIFT HIS HEAD
AND OUT COMES REAL PEZ.

118
00:04:37,012 --> 00:04:39,047
HEY,
TASTES LIKE REAL CHALK.

119
00:04:39,047 --> 00:04:40,882
LIKE I SAID, REAL PEZ.

120
00:04:40,882 --> 00:04:42,317
HEY, CHECK IT OUT.

121
00:04:42,317 --> 00:04:45,987
HERE’S TOM SERVO MODELING
THE JIMMY J.J. WALKER.

122
00:04:45,987 --> 00:04:48,222
KEEPS ME WALKING,
STANDING UPRIGHT.

123
00:04:48,222 --> 00:04:50,658
TURNS AN ORDINARY STROLL
DYN-O-MITE!

124
00:04:50,658 --> 00:04:54,562
HEY, GO ON THE SULLIVAN SHOW
AND GET CANNED WITH THIS.

125
00:04:54,562 --> 00:04:56,563
YOUR OWN JACKIE MASON JAR.

126
00:04:56,563 --> 00:04:57,598
WHO’S LIFTING MY TOP?

127
00:04:57,598 --> 00:04:59,033
A GENTILE WOULD
DO IT DIFFERENTLY?

128
00:04:59,033 --> 00:05:00,968
HIS LIFTING MY TOP
WOULD BE THE THRILL OF HIS LIFE.

129
00:05:00,968 --> 00:05:02,903
A JEWISH MAN COULD LIFT
THE TOP AND SAY, "OY VEY,

130
00:05:02,903 --> 00:05:04,305
"I’M JEWISH.
I’M CANNING TOMATOES.

131
00:05:04,305 --> 00:05:06,307
I DON’T UNDERSTAND IT.
I GOT A MASON JAR."

132
00:05:06,307 --> 00:05:09,677
AND, FINALLY,
MASSAGE A FRIEND WITH THIS,

133
00:05:09,677 --> 00:05:12,813
THE CHARLIE CALLAS
MASSAGER.

134
00:05:14,648 --> 00:05:17,418
HIGHER, HIGHER.

135
00:05:17,418 --> 00:05:18,920
WHAT DO YOU THINK, SIRS?

136
00:05:18,920 --> 00:05:22,357
I THINK YOU DIE, JOE.

137
00:05:22,357 --> 00:05:23,925
WELL, YOUR EXPERIMENT
THIS WEEK

138
00:05:23,925 --> 00:05:25,593
IS GOING TO BE HARD
TO KEEP DOWN.

139
00:05:25,593 --> 00:05:27,028
IT’S CALLED THE UNEARTHLY,

140
00:05:27,028 --> 00:05:30,330
AND IT STARS JOHN CARRADINE
AND TOR JOHNSON.

141
00:05:30,330 --> 00:05:32,800
PLUS TWO STINKY SHORTS.

142
00:05:32,800 --> 00:05:33,802
FRANK, SHUT UP!

143
00:05:33,802 --> 00:05:34,835
[FRANK CRYING LOUDLY]

144
00:05:34,835 --> 00:05:38,038
ENJOY.

145
00:05:38,038 --> 00:05:40,173
[ALARM BUZZING, SCREAMING]

146
00:05:51,618 --> 00:05:53,755
AVIS FILMS.
WE TRY HARDER.

147
00:05:53,755 --> 00:05:56,690
I THINK HE’S STILL
SMOLDERING OVER THERE.

148
00:05:56,690 --> 00:05:57,725
HUH.

149
00:05:57,725 --> 00:05:59,127
HEY, IT’S WHISTLER’S MOTHER.

150
00:05:59,127 --> 00:06:00,395
[LAUGHTER]

151
00:06:00,395 --> 00:06:02,897
I AM WHISTLER’S MOTHER.

152
00:06:02,897 --> 00:06:06,400
THE STORY
YOU ARE ABOUT TO SEE IS TRUE.

153
00:06:06,400 --> 00:06:08,803
NO NAMES WERE CHANGED,
BECAUSE NO ONE WAS INNOCENT.

154
00:06:08,803 --> 00:06:12,273
[CHUCKLES, IMITATES MUSIC]

155
00:06:13,942 --> 00:06:16,343
MY NAME’S SALLY.
I’M A SNACK-AHOLIC.

156
00:06:16,343 --> 00:06:17,378
HI, SALLY.

157
00:06:17,378 --> 00:06:19,347
...THIRD GRADE CLASS
AT VALLEY SCHOOL

158
00:06:19,347 --> 00:06:20,882
IS TAKING A POSTURE TEST.

159
00:06:20,882 --> 00:06:23,183
EACH GIRL...

160
00:06:23,183 --> 00:06:24,752
- AND BOY...
- OH.

161
00:06:24,752 --> 00:06:26,853
- STANDS BEHIND THE SCREEN--
- IT’S PUDD’NHEAD.

162
00:06:26,853 --> 00:06:29,490
TO MAKE A SHARP, CLEAR SHADOW
FOR EVERYONE TO SEE.

163
00:06:29,490 --> 00:06:31,892
YOU CAN SEE THAT THIS BOY
NEEDS HELP.

164
00:06:31,892 --> 00:06:34,395
HE’S A LOSER, AND THE KIDS
LET HIM KNOW IT.

165
00:06:34,395 --> 00:06:37,198
THANK YOU. NEXT.
OH.

166
00:06:37,198 --> 00:06:39,100
THE TEACHER, MS. MARTIN,

167
00:06:39,100 --> 00:06:41,535
DRAWS A PICTURE
OF EACH GIRL AND BOY.

168
00:06:41,535 --> 00:06:43,503
SHE’S WEIRD,
WHICH RESULTS IN CREATIVITY.

169
00:06:43,503 --> 00:06:44,672
THEN SHE SHOWS WHAT IS WRONG

170
00:06:44,672 --> 00:06:47,342
WHEN A CHILD DOES NOT
STAND STRAIGHT AND TALL.

171
00:06:47,342 --> 00:06:49,277
- IT’S IMOGENE COCA!
- YEAH.

172
00:06:49,277 --> 00:06:50,343
ICK.

173
00:06:50,343 --> 00:06:51,612
MS. MARTIN ASKS THE CLASS

174
00:06:51,612 --> 00:06:55,315
TO REMEMBER FOUR IMPORTANT
THINGS ABOUT POSTURE.

175
00:06:55,315 --> 00:06:58,618
AND THESE FOUR CHILDREN
ARE ESPECIALLY INTERESTED

176
00:06:58,618 --> 00:07:00,220
IN THE FOUR IMPORTANT THINGS.

177
00:07:00,220 --> 00:07:01,688
- ’CAUSE THEY’RE ON THE PAYROLL.
- AH.

178
00:07:01,688 --> 00:07:04,525
FIRST, GOOD HEALTH
HELPS YOU HAVE GOOD POSTURE.

179
00:07:04,525 --> 00:07:05,993
TOMMY UNDERSTANDS THIS,

180
00:07:05,993 --> 00:07:08,062
BECAUSE HE WANTS
TO BE AN ATHLETE.

181
00:07:08,062 --> 00:07:09,697
UH-HUH. YEAH.
UH-HUH. UH-HUH.

182
00:07:09,697 --> 00:07:10,732
HE KNOWS
THAT GOOD HEALTH HABITS

183
00:07:10,732 --> 00:07:12,065
ARE VERY IMPORTANT
TO AN ATHLETE.

184
00:07:12,065 --> 00:07:13,633
AMAZING PHYSIQUE
FOR AN EIGHT-YEAR-OLD.

185
00:07:13,633 --> 00:07:14,902
MM-HMM.

186
00:07:14,902 --> 00:07:17,905
SECOND, GOOD POSTURE
KEEPS YOU FROM BEING TIRED.

187
00:07:17,905 --> 00:07:21,008
WHEN YOU STAND OFF-BALANCE
LIKE THIS HOUSE,

188
00:07:21,008 --> 00:07:22,777
YOUR MUSCLES MUST WORK HARD

189
00:07:22,777 --> 00:07:24,512
TO KEEP YOU
FROM FALLING OVER.

190
00:07:24,512 --> 00:07:25,547
I LIKE HER.
[LAUGHS]

191
00:07:25,547 --> 00:07:26,680
JIMMY LIKES TO BUILD THINGS,

192
00:07:26,680 --> 00:07:29,017
SO HE UNDERSTANDS
THAT STANDING STRAIGHT

193
00:07:29,017 --> 00:07:31,952
IS STANDING STRONG,
LIKE A TALL, STRONG BUILDING.

194
00:07:31,952 --> 00:07:35,523
- LIKE A SPARTAN GOD.
- WOW.

195
00:07:35,523 --> 00:07:37,658
THIRD, IT IS IMPORTANT
TO HAVE THE HABIT

196
00:07:37,658 --> 00:07:39,027
OF GOOD POSTURE.

197
00:07:39,027 --> 00:07:41,195
YOUR BODY
IS LIKE A GROWING TREE.

198
00:07:41,195 --> 00:07:43,363
WITH DUTCH ELM DISEASE.

199
00:07:43,363 --> 00:07:44,832
JANE LOVES TREES.

200
00:07:44,832 --> 00:07:47,902
SHE KNOWS THAT A YOUNG TREE
MUST BE KEPT STRAIGHT,

201
00:07:47,902 --> 00:07:50,170
SO IT WILL GROW TALL
AND BEAUTIFUL.

202
00:07:50,170 --> 00:07:53,473
DON’T YOU, JANE?
JANE!

203
00:07:53,473 --> 00:07:54,508
[WHISPERS]
JANE.

204
00:07:54,508 --> 00:07:58,012
THE...LARCH.

205
00:07:58,012 --> 00:07:59,813
FOURTH, THE WAY YOU LOOK

206
00:07:59,813 --> 00:08:02,148
CAN DEPEND UPON
YOUR POSTURE.

207
00:08:02,148 --> 00:08:05,920
WHEN YOU SLUMP, YOU LOOK
TIRED AND UNHAPPY.

208
00:08:05,920 --> 00:08:07,322
BUT WHEN YOU STAND TALL,

209
00:08:07,322 --> 00:08:08,722
YOU LOOK CHEERFUL AND BRIGHT.

210
00:08:08,722 --> 00:08:09,990
LIKE A MAN.

211
00:08:09,990 --> 00:08:11,458
MARY UNDERSTANDS THIS.

212
00:08:11,458 --> 00:08:13,493
MARY WANTS TO BE AN ACTRESS.

213
00:08:13,493 --> 00:08:15,162
SHE KNOWS THAT AN ACTRESS

214
00:08:15,162 --> 00:08:16,963
MUST STAND STRAIGHT AND TALL

215
00:08:16,963 --> 00:08:19,800
TO LOOK BEAUTIFUL AND HAPPY.

216
00:08:19,800 --> 00:08:21,568
FINGERS ON THE...

217
00:08:21,568 --> 00:08:22,937
THANK YOU.
THANK YOU VERY MUCH.

218
00:08:22,937 --> 00:08:25,873
I’M WEARING
A LOVELY PANTSUIT.

219
00:08:25,873 --> 00:08:27,308
MS. MARTIN TELLS THE CLASS

220
00:08:27,308 --> 00:08:29,043
- THAT SOMEDAY SOON...
- SHE’LL BE MARRIED.

221
00:08:29,043 --> 00:08:30,878
AFTER THE NEXT POSTURE TEST,

222
00:08:30,878 --> 00:08:33,580
THEY WILL CHOOSE
A KING, A QUEEN,

223
00:08:33,580 --> 00:08:36,583
A PRINCE,
AND A PRINCESS OF POSTURE.

224
00:08:36,583 --> 00:08:39,687
THE TWO BOYS AND THE TWO GIRLS
WITH THE BEST POSTURES

225
00:08:39,687 --> 00:08:41,922
WILL WEAR
THESE POSTURE CROWNS.

226
00:08:41,922 --> 00:08:43,190
YEAH,
THEY’LL GO TO BURGER KING

227
00:08:43,190 --> 00:08:46,960
AND GET CRAPPY HATS.

228
00:08:46,960 --> 00:08:49,230
TOMMY, JIMMY, JANE, AND MARY

229
00:08:49,230 --> 00:08:51,432
ARE VERY INTERESTED
IN THIS ANNOUNCEMENT.

230
00:08:51,432 --> 00:08:54,568
HEY, WHO WOULDN’T BE?

231
00:08:54,568 --> 00:08:56,703
SO WHEN CLASS IS OVER,

232
00:08:56,703 --> 00:08:58,672
THEY DECIDE
TO TAKE A CLOSE LOOK

233
00:08:58,672 --> 00:09:00,775
AT THEIR POSTURE DRAWINGS.

234
00:09:00,775 --> 00:09:03,277
THAT’S WHEN THE KIDS
CAME UP WITH A PLAN

235
00:09:03,277 --> 00:09:06,380
TO BLACKMAIL MRS. REEDY.

236
00:09:06,380 --> 00:09:09,450
BUT THEY’RE NOT HAPPY
WITH WHAT THEY SEE.

237
00:09:09,450 --> 00:09:11,985
THEY’RE DISGUSTED
AND FILLED WITH SELF LOATHING.

238
00:09:11,985 --> 00:09:13,922
FOR TOMMY IS INDEED SURPRISED,

239
00:09:13,922 --> 00:09:15,155
AND HE’S NOT PLEASED
BY WHAT HE FOUND.

240
00:09:15,155 --> 00:09:16,223
UH-UH. UH-UH.
NO. UH-UH.

241
00:09:16,223 --> 00:09:18,525
HE DIDN’T KNOW HIS CHEST
LOOKED FLAT

242
00:09:18,525 --> 00:09:20,695
BECAUSE HIS TUMMY
LOOKED SO ROUND.

243
00:09:20,695 --> 00:09:22,597
HE’S GOT V.P.L.

244
00:09:22,597 --> 00:09:25,365
HEY, LET ME TELL YOU.
JOEL!

245
00:09:25,365 --> 00:09:26,700
NOW JIMMY IS DISTURBED
TO SEE...

246
00:09:26,700 --> 00:09:28,402
UH-UH. NO. NOTHIN’ DOING.

247
00:09:28,402 --> 00:09:31,172
THAT AIN’T GONNA WORK.
IT’S NOT FLYING WITH ME, POPS.

248
00:09:31,172 --> 00:09:34,042
OUT OF BALANCE, JUST LIKE
A HOUSE ABOUT TO FALL.

249
00:09:34,042 --> 00:09:36,043
JUST LIKE HIS DAD
ON FRIDAY NIGHT.

250
00:09:36,043 --> 00:09:37,945
OUCH.

251
00:09:37,945 --> 00:09:40,080
AND WHAT GIVES JANE
HER WORRIED FROWN?

252
00:09:40,080 --> 00:09:41,082
VALIUM?

253
00:09:41,082 --> 00:09:42,148
LOOK AT THE BOARD.

254
00:09:42,148 --> 00:09:43,750
IT’S PLAIN TO SEE
THAT JANE

255
00:09:43,750 --> 00:09:45,518
MUST PRACTICE
STANDING STRAIGHT

256
00:09:45,518 --> 00:09:47,588
TO GROW UP
LIKE A LOVELY TREE.

257
00:09:47,588 --> 00:09:50,190
ALL OF A SUDDEN
IT’S IAMBIC PENTAMETER HERE.

258
00:09:50,190 --> 00:09:52,225
OUR MARY IS A HAPPY GIRL,

259
00:09:52,225 --> 00:09:54,528
SO SHE IS SHOCKED TO SEE INSTEAD

260
00:09:54,528 --> 00:09:56,930
A DROOPY GIRL DRAWN ON THE BOARD

261
00:09:56,930 --> 00:09:59,367
WITH HALLOW CHEST
AND TIRED HEAD.

262
00:09:59,367 --> 00:10:01,368
SHE SHOULD JUST
GO HOME TO BED.

263
00:10:01,368 --> 00:10:03,637
- D’OH.
- GREEN EGGS AND HAM.

264
00:10:03,637 --> 00:10:04,672
YOU SAM I AM?

265
00:10:04,672 --> 00:10:05,840
MS. MARTIN SEES
THAT THE CHILDREN

266
00:10:05,840 --> 00:10:07,375
ARE ESPECIALLY INTERESTED,

267
00:10:07,375 --> 00:10:10,177
SO SHE OFFERS TO HELP THEM
IMPROVE THEIR POSITIONS.

268
00:10:10,177 --> 00:10:11,278
UH-HUH.

269
00:10:11,278 --> 00:10:12,847
FIRST, SHE SHOWS THEM
THE IMPORTANCE

270
00:10:12,847 --> 00:10:14,515
OF GOOD FOOT POSITION.

271
00:10:14,515 --> 00:10:16,583
UH, MS. MARTIN HAS A LITTLE
TOO MUCH FREE TIME

272
00:10:16,583 --> 00:10:18,118
ON HER HANDS.

273
00:10:18,118 --> 00:10:20,722
- TOES POINT STRAIGHT FORWARD...
- THERE’S NO PLACE LIKE HOME.

274
00:10:22,255 --> 00:10:25,392
- WEIGHT OF THE BODY...
- HOOVES. OH.

275
00:10:25,392 --> 00:10:28,795
ON THE HEEL AND BALL
OF BOTH FEET.

276
00:10:28,795 --> 00:10:30,765
FIRST DOWN...DOWN...

277
00:10:30,765 --> 00:10:32,500
GOAL TO GO...GO...

278
00:10:32,500 --> 00:10:34,768
EYES ARE STRAIGHT.
THE ABDOMEN IS IN.

279
00:10:34,768 --> 00:10:35,803
THE BACK IS STRAIGHT.

280
00:10:35,803 --> 00:10:37,505
ARMS SWING
EASILY AT THE SIDES.

281
00:10:37,505 --> 00:10:38,505
[WHISTLES]

282
00:10:38,505 --> 00:10:41,975
HERE SHE REENACTS
HER FIRST D.U.I.

283
00:10:41,975 --> 00:10:44,145
GET UP.

284
00:10:44,145 --> 00:10:46,713
COME UP HERE.

285
00:10:46,713 --> 00:10:48,348
IN A GOOD STANDING POSITION--

286
00:10:48,348 --> 00:10:49,983
HEY, HEY, HEY, HEY,
HEY, HEY, HEY.

287
00:10:49,983 --> 00:10:52,520
BACK IS STRAIGHT,
YOU STRETCH TALL.

288
00:10:52,520 --> 00:10:54,622
ARMS ARE EASY AT THE SIDES.

289
00:10:54,622 --> 00:10:57,123
EYES STRAIGHT AHEAD,
SHOULDERS RELAXED.

290
00:10:57,123 --> 00:10:59,227
AND YOU TRUCK
LIKE THE DOODAH MAN.

291
00:10:59,227 --> 00:11:02,295
OOH.
GOT YOUR CHIPS CASHED IN.

292
00:11:02,295 --> 00:11:04,198
IN GOOD SITTING POSITION,

293
00:11:04,198 --> 00:11:06,000
BOTH FEET
ARE FLAT ON THE FLOOR.

294
00:11:06,000 --> 00:11:07,267
ASSUMING
THEY REACH THE FLOOR.

295
00:11:07,267 --> 00:11:08,835
HOO-HOO.

296
00:11:08,835 --> 00:11:11,138
HIPS ARE WELL BACK
AGAINST THE CHAIR.

297
00:11:11,138 --> 00:11:12,172
MM-HMM.

298
00:11:12,172 --> 00:11:13,307
CROW.

299
00:11:13,307 --> 00:11:15,508
FOREARMS AND HANDS
ARE RELAXED ON THE DESK.

300
00:11:15,508 --> 00:11:17,243
PELVIS.
WHAT ABOUT THE PELVIS?

301
00:11:17,243 --> 00:11:20,848
ELVIS.

302
00:11:20,848 --> 00:11:21,882
MS. MARTIN SUGGESTS

303
00:11:21,882 --> 00:11:23,417
THAT TOMMY AND JIMMY

304
00:11:23,417 --> 00:11:24,918
AND JANE AND MARY

305
00:11:24,918 --> 00:11:27,722
BE POSTURE PALS
TO HELP ONE ANOTHER.

306
00:11:27,722 --> 00:11:30,590
AND SHE REMINDS THEM
OF THE POSTURE CONTEST.

307
00:11:30,590 --> 00:11:31,625
[IMITATING SLURPING]

308
00:11:31,625 --> 00:11:34,027
THE CHILDREN
DO HELP ONE ANOTHER.

309
00:11:34,027 --> 00:11:37,398
JIMMY HELPS TOMMY
TO KEEP HIS TUMMY IN.

310
00:11:37,398 --> 00:11:39,200
YOU HAVE GOT
TO BE KIDDING ME, PYLE.

311
00:11:39,200 --> 00:11:41,068
LOOK AT THAT GUT.

312
00:11:44,572 --> 00:11:46,007
TOMMY REMINDS JIMMY.

313
00:11:46,007 --> 00:11:47,040
THAT’S YOU.

314
00:11:47,040 --> 00:11:48,608
WHEN JIMMY STANDS OFF-BALANCE.

315
00:11:48,608 --> 00:11:51,912
TEARS OF SHAME
POUR DOWN TOMMY’S FACE.

316
00:11:51,912 --> 00:11:54,548
MS. MARTIN,
TOMMY DREW A BONG.

317
00:11:54,548 --> 00:11:55,817
HUH?

318
00:11:57,585 --> 00:11:59,787
MARY ALWAYS REMINDS JANE

319
00:11:59,787 --> 00:12:02,255
WHEN JANE FORGETS TO STAND
STRAIGHT AND TALL.

320
00:12:02,255 --> 00:12:04,358
WAIT A MINUTE.
SPOT FOR ME, HONEY. WILL YOU?

321
00:12:04,358 --> 00:12:05,458
THERE.

322
00:12:05,458 --> 00:12:08,128
A PLAYGROUND WHERE APES
EVOLVE FROM MEN?!

323
00:12:08,128 --> 00:12:10,932
[IMITATES APE]

324
00:12:10,932 --> 00:12:14,135
AND JANE REMINDS MARY

325
00:12:14,135 --> 00:12:15,502
WHEN MARY
SLUMPS AT HER DESK.

326
00:12:15,502 --> 00:12:17,472
OH, THEY’RE GONNA TAKE THIS
FOR ABOUT A HALF HOUR

327
00:12:17,472 --> 00:12:19,038
BEFORE THEY END UP
KILLING EACH OTHER.

328
00:12:19,038 --> 00:12:20,875
YEAH, I THINK SO.

329
00:12:25,678 --> 00:12:28,548
THE CHILDREN HAVE OTHER
POSTURE PALS AT HOME.

330
00:12:29,717 --> 00:12:32,887
HEY, MOM’S DRESS
MATCHES THE WALLPAPER.

331
00:12:32,887 --> 00:12:34,588
NIGHT, HEF.

332
00:12:34,588 --> 00:12:37,357
TOMMY’S MOTHER HELPS HIM
TO GET PLENTY OF SLEEP.

333
00:12:37,357 --> 00:12:39,260
SLEEP!

334
00:12:39,260 --> 00:12:42,597
AND PLENTY OF GOOD,
HEALTHFUL FOOD

335
00:12:42,597 --> 00:12:43,963
SO HE’LL STAY
HEALTHY AND STRONG.

336
00:12:43,963 --> 00:12:46,300
FOUR FOOD GROUPS.
HMM.

337
00:12:46,300 --> 00:12:48,802
JIMMY’S FATHER REMINDS JIMMY

338
00:12:48,802 --> 00:12:50,537
WHEN HE STANDS OFF-BALANCE.

339
00:12:50,537 --> 00:12:53,440
AN AIRPLANE
SHOULDN’T STAND CROOKED.

340
00:12:53,440 --> 00:12:54,875
LIKE DADDY ON FRIDAY NIGHT.

341
00:12:54,875 --> 00:12:57,343
AH.

342
00:12:57,343 --> 00:13:00,347
SO JIMMY REMEMBERS
A BOY SHOULDN’T EITHER.

343
00:13:00,347 --> 00:13:02,817
NOR SHOULD HE WEAR
TACKY HAWAIIAN SHIRTS.

344
00:13:04,652 --> 00:13:07,120
JANE’S FATHER HAS A WAY
OF REMINDING JANE

345
00:13:07,120 --> 00:13:08,288
WHEN SHE FORGETS.

346
00:13:08,288 --> 00:13:09,790
ALL RIGHT, HONEY,
I’M GONNA KILL THIS TREE

347
00:13:09,790 --> 00:13:11,025
IF YOU DON’T STAND STRAIGHT.

348
00:13:11,025 --> 00:13:12,727
A YOUNG PLANT
SHOULDN’T BE BENT LIKE THAT.

349
00:13:12,727 --> 00:13:15,395
THEN STOP DOING IT.

350
00:13:15,395 --> 00:13:17,330
THEN JANE REMEMBERS.

351
00:13:17,330 --> 00:13:18,998
- A GIRL SHOULDN’T EITHER.
- OH, YEAH.

352
00:13:18,998 --> 00:13:20,100
- A GIRL?
- WHAT?

353
00:13:20,100 --> 00:13:23,637
MARY HAS TWO POSTURE PALS
AT HER HOME.

354
00:13:23,637 --> 00:13:24,872
MARY’S MOTHER REMINDS HER

355
00:13:24,872 --> 00:13:26,673
NOT TO SLUMP
WHEN SHE’S SITTING DOWN.

356
00:13:26,673 --> 00:13:28,408
IT’S ERNEST BORGNINE.

357
00:13:28,408 --> 00:13:30,978
UGH.

358
00:13:30,978 --> 00:13:33,080
UH, SORRY, MOM, DAD.

359
00:13:36,383 --> 00:13:37,952
PAINTING HER TEETH.

360
00:13:37,952 --> 00:13:39,653
AND BOMBO REMINDS HER...

361
00:13:39,653 --> 00:13:41,322
BOMBO?

362
00:13:41,322 --> 00:13:42,890
...YOU LOOK TIRED AND UNHAPPY.

363
00:13:42,890 --> 00:13:45,025
BOMBO.

364
00:13:45,025 --> 00:13:47,227
DOESN’T BOMBO LOOK TIRED?

365
00:13:47,227 --> 00:13:48,762
YES, VERY MUCH SO.

366
00:13:48,762 --> 00:13:50,865
BUT NOW YOU SEE IT WAS
JUST BECAUSE...

367
00:13:50,865 --> 00:13:54,033
NO, NO, MY SPINE! AAH!
[IMITATING BONES CRACKING]

368
00:13:57,037 --> 00:14:00,273
AT LAST
THE BIG DAY HAS COME.

369
00:14:00,273 --> 00:14:03,677
THE CLASS IS TAKING
THEIR SECOND POSTURE TEST.

370
00:14:03,677 --> 00:14:05,412
[IMITATING FUNERAL MARCH
OF A MARIONETTE]

371
00:14:05,412 --> 00:14:07,815
- IT’S HITCHCOCK.
- YEAH. AFTER SLIM-FAST.

372
00:14:09,683 --> 00:14:11,085
MS. MARTIN
IS COUNTING VOTES

373
00:14:11,085 --> 00:14:13,553
TO SEE WHO WILL BE
THE KING, QUEEN,

374
00:14:13,553 --> 00:14:15,788
PRINCE,
AND PRINCESS OF POSTURE.

375
00:14:15,788 --> 00:14:18,458
AND WHO WILL HAVE
A SEALY POSTUREPEDIC CHILDHOOD.

376
00:14:18,458 --> 00:14:19,993
WHO DID THIS? DID YOU DO THIS?

377
00:14:19,993 --> 00:14:21,095
WHO DID THIS? WHO DID THIS?

378
00:14:21,095 --> 00:14:22,730
IT SHOULDN’T BE HARD
FOR YOU TO GUESS

379
00:14:22,730 --> 00:14:24,398
WHO WINS THE VOTES.

380
00:14:24,398 --> 00:14:27,300
THAT’S RIGHT.
MARY IS ELECTED QUEEN.

381
00:14:27,300 --> 00:14:29,837
FIX! IT’S A RIG! FIX!

382
00:14:29,837 --> 00:14:32,405
THEN MARY’S HEAD
IS LIT ON FIRE.

383
00:14:34,073 --> 00:14:35,943
AND THE OTHER THREE CHILDREN

384
00:14:35,943 --> 00:14:37,110
WIN THE OTHER
POSTURE CROWNS.

385
00:14:37,110 --> 00:14:38,545
DEFINITELY A FIX.

386
00:14:38,545 --> 00:14:42,215
DON’T YOU AGREE THAT THESE
FOUR CHILDREN DESERVE TO WIN

387
00:14:42,215 --> 00:14:44,985
AFTER TRYING SO HARD
TO IMPROVE THEIR POSTURES?

388
00:14:44,985 --> 00:14:46,020
[ALL]
NO.

389
00:14:46,020 --> 00:14:48,955
YES, TOMMY IS OUR POSTURE KING.

390
00:14:48,955 --> 00:14:51,058
WHILE JIMMY IS THE PRINCE,
YOU SEE.

391
00:14:51,058 --> 00:14:53,527
JANE IS NOW THE PRINCESS FAIR,

392
00:14:53,527 --> 00:14:55,228
AND MARY
IS OUR HAPPY QUEEN.

393
00:14:55,228 --> 00:14:56,397
THEY’RE THE POSTURE POSSE.

394
00:14:56,397 --> 00:14:58,865
THESE BOYS AND GIRLS
WON POSTURE CROWNS

395
00:14:58,865 --> 00:15:00,867
BY HELPING ONE ANOTHER LEARN.

396
00:15:00,867 --> 00:15:03,103
THEY HOPE THAT YOU
WILL LEARN FROM THEM

397
00:15:03,103 --> 00:15:05,005
AND BE A POSTURE PAL IN TURN.

398
00:15:05,005 --> 00:15:08,908
THEIR CHANCES OF BEING COOL
ARE RUINED FOR LIFE.

399
00:15:08,908 --> 00:15:09,943
BYE, KIDS.

400
00:15:09,943 --> 00:15:11,845
[LAUGHS]

401
00:15:11,845 --> 00:15:16,483
NEXT WEEK,
POSTURE POKE--IN COLOR.

402
00:15:16,483 --> 00:15:18,685
[MUTTERS]

403
00:15:26,860 --> 00:15:28,095
HEY, REUBEN HILL.

404
00:15:28,095 --> 00:15:29,963
YOU STILL WALK
THE FERTILE FIELDS OF MY MIND.

405
00:15:29,963 --> 00:15:31,365
OH, PROFESSOR
IN FAMILY LIFE.

406
00:15:31,365 --> 00:15:32,465
THAT’S AN EASY MAJOR.

407
00:15:32,465 --> 00:15:35,335
THIS IS THE STORY
OF A BOY NAMED TOMMY

408
00:15:35,335 --> 00:15:38,105
AND HOW HE LEARNED ALL--
MOTHER DO FOR HIM.

409
00:15:38,105 --> 00:15:40,073
- HUH?
- THIS IS TOMMY’S ROOM.

410
00:15:40,073 --> 00:15:41,442
CAN YOU GUESS
WHAT HE’S THINKING?

411
00:15:41,442 --> 00:15:42,643
WHAT A DUMP!

412
00:15:42,643 --> 00:15:45,478
LOOK HOW NEAT AND STRAIGHT
HIS WHOLE ROOM IS.

413
00:15:45,478 --> 00:15:46,513
HMM.

414
00:15:46,513 --> 00:15:47,748
TOMMY’S THINKING HARD,

415
00:15:47,748 --> 00:15:49,450
BECAUSE HE HASN’T DONE
A THING TO HIS ROOM

416
00:15:49,450 --> 00:15:51,518
SINCE HE LEFT
FOR SCHOOL THIS MORNING,

417
00:15:51,518 --> 00:15:55,322
AND WHEN HE LEFT, THE ROOM
DIDN’T LOOK LIKE THIS AT ALL.

418
00:15:55,322 --> 00:15:56,357
HE’S IN THE WRONG HOUSE.

419
00:15:56,357 --> 00:15:58,892
TOYS ON THE SHELVES,
BED NEATLY MADE.

420
00:15:58,892 --> 00:16:00,593
CLOTHES PUT AWAY.

421
00:16:00,593 --> 00:16:03,030
NO, THIS MORNING
IT LOOKED LIKE THIS.

422
00:16:03,030 --> 00:16:04,465
HAD MORE OF
A QUEEN ANNE THEME TO IT.

423
00:16:04,465 --> 00:16:05,565
YEAH.

424
00:16:05,565 --> 00:16:09,102
CLOTHES SCATTERED ABOUT.
TOYS ON THE FLOOR.

425
00:16:09,102 --> 00:16:10,237
BEER CANS EVERYWHERE.

426
00:16:10,237 --> 00:16:12,005
YES, WHEN TOMMY WENT
TO SCHOOL THIS MORNING,

427
00:16:12,005 --> 00:16:14,273
HE LEFT HIS ROOM A MESS.

428
00:16:14,273 --> 00:16:17,310
- BUT NOW...
- HEY.

429
00:16:17,310 --> 00:16:19,178
EVERYTHING
IS NEAT AND STRAIGHT.

430
00:16:19,178 --> 00:16:20,513
EXCEPT FOR HIS MIND.

431
00:16:20,513 --> 00:16:22,448
NOW HOW DO YOU SUPPOSE
THAT HAPPENS?

432
00:16:22,448 --> 00:16:23,617
WHAT IS THIS CRAP?

433
00:16:23,617 --> 00:16:25,185
AND THAT’S NOT ALL.

434
00:16:25,185 --> 00:16:29,222
YESTERDAY, TOMMY TORE THE SLEEVE
OF HIS FAVORITE COWBOY SHIRT...

435
00:16:29,222 --> 00:16:30,323
IN A PRISON BREAK.

436
00:16:30,323 --> 00:16:31,792
AND NOW IT’S MENDED
AS GOOD AS NEW.

437
00:16:31,792 --> 00:16:33,093
TOMMY’S THE LATHE OF HEAVEN.

438
00:16:33,093 --> 00:16:34,728
AND HIS JACKET
HAD A BUTTON OFF.

439
00:16:34,728 --> 00:16:36,563
NOW THERE’S A NEW BUTTON.

440
00:16:36,563 --> 00:16:37,597
HMM.

441
00:16:37,597 --> 00:16:38,632
AND, YOU KNOW,

442
00:16:38,632 --> 00:16:39,800
THINGS OF THAT SORT

443
00:16:39,800 --> 00:16:41,668
DON’T HAPPEN
JUST IN TOMMY’S ROOM.

444
00:16:41,668 --> 00:16:44,037
THEY HAPPEN
ALL OVER THE HOUSE.

445
00:16:44,037 --> 00:16:46,640
IT’S CALLED GUILT,
AND BOY DOES IT WORK.

446
00:16:46,640 --> 00:16:48,708
AFTER BREAKFAST THIS MORNING,

447
00:16:48,708 --> 00:16:50,910
THE KITCHEN LOOKED LIKE THIS.

448
00:16:50,910 --> 00:16:54,415
THEN DO YOU KNOW WHAT HAPPENED
WHILE TOMMY WAS IN SCHOOL?

449
00:16:54,415 --> 00:16:55,982
SOMEONE STOLE EVERYTHING.

450
00:16:55,982 --> 00:16:57,785
YES, THE TABLE WAS CLEARED,

451
00:16:57,785 --> 00:16:59,787
THE DISHES
WERE WASHED AND PUT AWAY,

452
00:16:59,787 --> 00:17:01,955
AND THE WHOLE KITCHEN
WAS CLEANED UP.

453
00:17:01,955 --> 00:17:04,057
BY A WOMAN WITH NO CAREER
OUTSIDE THE HOUSE.

454
00:17:04,057 --> 00:17:05,492
THE SAME THING HAPPENED
WITH THE DIRTY CLOTHES.

455
00:17:05,492 --> 00:17:09,162
THEY GET WASHED AND IRONED
AND PUT AWAY JUST LIKE MAGIC.

456
00:17:09,162 --> 00:17:11,265
MAGIC’S EASY
ONCE YOU KNOW MOM.

457
00:17:11,265 --> 00:17:13,967
AND THE GROCERIES
THAT COME FROM THE STORES.

458
00:17:13,967 --> 00:17:15,568
WELL, SEE THAT CHICKEN?

459
00:17:15,568 --> 00:17:16,903
WHERE? WHERE? OH.

460
00:17:16,903 --> 00:17:19,673
HERE’S THE WAY IT LOOKS
WHEN TOMMY SITS DOWN TO SUPPER.

461
00:17:19,673 --> 00:17:21,142
- UGH.
- TRUMPY, NO!

462
00:17:21,142 --> 00:17:23,243
THAT REMINDS ME.
I GOTTA GO FRESHEN UP.

463
00:17:23,243 --> 00:17:26,147
THINGS CERTAINLY DO HAPPEN
WHILE TOMMY’S IN SCHOOL.

464
00:17:26,147 --> 00:17:27,180
MM-HMM.

465
00:17:27,180 --> 00:17:28,448
NOW WHAT DOES TOMMY SEE?

466
00:17:28,448 --> 00:17:30,950
IT’S TOMMY’S CONNECTION
COMING UP THE WALK.

467
00:17:30,950 --> 00:17:33,120
WHERE’S HE GOING?

468
00:17:33,120 --> 00:17:35,088
OH, HERE’S TOMMY’S FATHER,
HOME FROM WORK.

469
00:17:35,088 --> 00:17:37,758
BUT TOMMY
CALLS MANY MEN "DAD."

470
00:17:37,758 --> 00:17:40,160
- HEY, YOU LOOK GOOD.
- OH, LOOK REALLY GOOD, CROW.

471
00:17:40,160 --> 00:17:41,562
HELLO, MASTER.

472
00:17:41,562 --> 00:17:44,297
TOMMY LIKES
TO BE WITH HIS PARENTS.

473
00:17:44,297 --> 00:17:46,767
AND THIS EVENING
IS A LITTLE SPECIAL,

474
00:17:46,767 --> 00:17:49,803
FOR IT’S THE DAY FOR TOMMY
TO RECEIVE HIS ALLOWANCE.

475
00:17:49,803 --> 00:17:52,038
HERE’S A PENNY.
HAPPY BIRTHDAY.

476
00:17:52,038 --> 00:17:53,407
...FATHER COMES HOME WITH MONEY

477
00:17:53,407 --> 00:17:55,342
FOR TOMMY AND FOR MOTHER.

478
00:17:55,342 --> 00:17:56,443
EH, I SUPPOSE YOU WANT SOME.

479
00:17:56,443 --> 00:17:58,512
...MONEY FATHER EARNS
BY GOING OUT...

480
00:17:58,512 --> 00:18:01,715
HERE’S A DOLLAR. GO BUY
YOURSELF SOMETHING PRETTY.

481
00:18:01,715 --> 00:18:04,117
AFTER SUPPER,
THE KITCHEN LOOKS VERY MUCH

482
00:18:04,117 --> 00:18:05,518
AS IT DID AFTER BREAKFAST.

483
00:18:05,518 --> 00:18:06,987
UGH.

484
00:18:06,987 --> 00:18:08,588
DO YOU KNOW WHO’LL CLEAN IT UP?

485
00:18:08,588 --> 00:18:10,123
THE MAID?

486
00:18:10,123 --> 00:18:12,592
TOMMY KNOWS THAT WHEN
HE GETS UP TOMORROW MORNING,

487
00:18:12,592 --> 00:18:14,127
EVERYTHING’LL BE DONE.

488
00:18:14,127 --> 00:18:17,832
SO GOODNIGHT, FATHER.

489
00:18:17,832 --> 00:18:20,467
GOODNIGHT, MOTHER.

490
00:18:20,467 --> 00:18:23,870
GOODNIGHT, OEDIPUS.

491
00:18:23,870 --> 00:18:25,372
GOODNIGHT.

492
00:18:25,372 --> 00:18:26,373
[KISSES]

493
00:18:26,373 --> 00:18:27,640
SLEEP.

494
00:18:27,640 --> 00:18:30,743
NO, HELP! THERE’S AN ANNOUNCER
UNDER MY BED!

495
00:18:30,743 --> 00:18:32,980
NOW THE FACES
OF THOSE HE’S WRONGED

496
00:18:32,980 --> 00:18:34,682
FLASH BEFORE HIS EYES.

497
00:18:34,682 --> 00:18:37,483
WHOOPS. ALMOST FORGOT
SOMETHING VERY IMPORTANT.

498
00:18:37,483 --> 00:18:39,052
TO PAY HOMAGE TO GORTO.

499
00:18:39,052 --> 00:18:40,587
HE’D BETTER PUT
THE ALLOWANCE MONEY

500
00:18:40,587 --> 00:18:42,322
IN HIS BANK
BEFORE HE FORGETS.

501
00:18:42,322 --> 00:18:43,990
YEAH, YOU WOULDN’T WANT
THAT PENNY JUST SITTING OUT.

502
00:18:43,990 --> 00:18:46,560
BUT, SAY,
THAT’S NOT VERY MUCH MONEY.

503
00:18:46,560 --> 00:18:47,593
UH-UH.

504
00:18:47,593 --> 00:18:49,162
AND THERE ARE SHOWS
TO GO TO.

505
00:18:49,162 --> 00:18:50,363
MM-HMM.

506
00:18:50,363 --> 00:18:52,098
AND THAT SUPER ATOMIC
AIRPLANE TO SEND FOR.

507
00:18:52,098 --> 00:18:53,867
MM-HMM.

508
00:18:53,867 --> 00:18:55,468
WELL, THERE ARE SO MANY THINGS

509
00:18:55,468 --> 00:18:57,137
A BOY LIKES
TO HAVE MONEY FOR.

510
00:18:57,137 --> 00:18:58,505
LIKE PLAY THE NUMBERS.

511
00:18:58,505 --> 00:19:01,140
TOMMY’S GOING DOWNSTAIRS.

512
00:19:01,140 --> 00:19:02,977
HE’S GOING TO ASK FATHER

513
00:19:02,977 --> 00:19:05,345
IF HE CAN’T HAVE A LITTLE
MORE MONEY EVERY WEEK.

514
00:19:05,345 --> 00:19:07,413
BUT FIRST HE STRAPS GOPHERS
TO HIS FEET.

515
00:19:07,413 --> 00:19:08,615
BYE.

516
00:19:08,615 --> 00:19:09,717
AND TOMMY WILL GET TO SEE

517
00:19:09,717 --> 00:19:11,785
WHAT MOTHER AND FATHER
DO AFTER SUPPER.

518
00:19:11,785 --> 00:19:13,520
AND WHAT ALL
THE YELLING’S ABOUT.

519
00:19:13,520 --> 00:19:15,655
YEAH.

520
00:19:15,655 --> 00:19:19,893
MOM? DAD?

521
00:19:19,893 --> 00:19:22,128
[GASPS] OH, MY GOD!
THAT’S DISGUSTING! OH!

522
00:19:22,128 --> 00:19:24,798
OH, THEY’RE DOING
THOSE DIRTY DISHES.

523
00:19:24,798 --> 00:19:25,832
WHEW.

524
00:19:25,832 --> 00:19:27,400
AND MOTHER IS TELLING FATHER

525
00:19:27,400 --> 00:19:28,902
ALL ABOUT THE THINGS SHE DID

526
00:19:28,902 --> 00:19:30,270
WHILE HE WAS AT WORK.

527
00:19:30,270 --> 00:19:34,975
WELL, I ISOLATED
THAT NUCLEOTIDE TODAY.

528
00:19:34,975 --> 00:19:36,443
THE FIRST THING
SHE DID THIS MORNING

529
00:19:36,443 --> 00:19:37,978
WAS TO FIX UP THE KITCHEN.

530
00:19:37,978 --> 00:19:40,680
MOM LEADS A LIFE
OF QUIET DESPERATION.

531
00:19:40,680 --> 00:19:42,648
SHE CLEARED THE TABLE
AND WASHED THE DISHES

532
00:19:42,648 --> 00:19:44,050
AND PUT THE FOOD AWAY

533
00:19:44,050 --> 00:19:46,220
AND MADE EVERYTHING
SPICK AND SPAN.

534
00:19:46,220 --> 00:19:49,522
WHILE SUPPRESSING
HER OWN DREAMS.

535
00:19:49,522 --> 00:19:52,258
THEN SHE WENT UP TO TOMMY’S ROOM
TO STRAIGHTEN IT.

536
00:19:52,258 --> 00:19:54,527
AS SHE CHOKES BACK
THE BILE OF RESENTMENT.

537
00:19:54,527 --> 00:19:56,195
THERE WERE TRAIN TRACKS
AND OTHER TOYS

538
00:19:56,195 --> 00:20:00,167
TO BE PICKED UP
AND PUT AWAY.

539
00:20:00,167 --> 00:20:01,435
THERE WAS THE BED TO BE MADE.

540
00:20:01,435 --> 00:20:02,468
AND THE MAID TO BE BEDDED.

541
00:20:02,468 --> 00:20:03,503
[IMITATES RIMSHOT]

542
00:20:03,503 --> 00:20:04,938
THERE WERE CLOTHES
TO BE HUNG UP.

543
00:20:04,938 --> 00:20:08,342
AND SOME WOULD NEED
WASHING OR MENDING.

544
00:20:08,342 --> 00:20:11,678
AFTER THAT, MOTHER STARTED
ON THE IRONING.

545
00:20:11,678 --> 00:20:13,247
THE MOST SATISFYING
PART OF HER DAY.

546
00:20:13,247 --> 00:20:15,282
DOING THE FAMILY
WASHING AND IRONING

547
00:20:15,282 --> 00:20:16,983
IS A PRETTY HARD JOB.

548
00:20:16,983 --> 00:20:18,118
MM.

549
00:20:18,118 --> 00:20:20,420
BUT MOTHER DOES IT REGULARLY
EVERY WEEK.

550
00:20:20,420 --> 00:20:21,955
SHE’S IN WHAT WE CALL A RUT.

551
00:20:21,955 --> 00:20:23,690
- AND THE COOKING.
- OH, YEAH.

552
00:20:23,690 --> 00:20:26,660
MOTHER HAS TO FIND TIME
TO MAKE GOOD, NOURISHING MEALS

553
00:20:26,660 --> 00:20:27,693
FOR THE WHOLE FAMILY.

554
00:20:27,693 --> 00:20:28,728
WE’RE HAVING CAT TODAY.

555
00:20:28,728 --> 00:20:30,030
[IMITATES CAT SCREECHING]

556
00:20:30,030 --> 00:20:32,565
TOMMY’S APPETITE IS GETTING
BIGGER AND BIGGER.

557
00:20:32,565 --> 00:20:34,367
WHILE HIS BRAIN
GETS DIMMER AND DIMMER.

558
00:20:34,367 --> 00:20:35,902
LATER, SHE DID THE MENDING.

559
00:20:35,902 --> 00:20:38,038
THERE’S TOMMY’S COWBOY SHIRT.

560
00:20:38,038 --> 00:20:39,205
AND HIS JACKET.

561
00:20:39,205 --> 00:20:40,740
HE CAN REJOIN
THE VILLAGE PEOPLE NOW.

562
00:20:40,740 --> 00:20:43,343
TOMMY COULD BE MORE CAREFUL
WITH HIS CLOTHES.

563
00:20:43,343 --> 00:20:45,878
YEAH, WHY SHOULD HE?

564
00:20:45,878 --> 00:20:47,913
THOSE ARE JUST
SOME OF THE THINGS

565
00:20:47,913 --> 00:20:49,548
THAT MOTHER HAS TO DO.

566
00:20:49,548 --> 00:20:52,918
NO WONDER SHE’S OFTEN TIRED
AT THE END OF THE DAY.

567
00:20:52,918 --> 00:20:54,187
TIRED OF TOMMY.

568
00:20:54,187 --> 00:20:56,757
IT SEEMS MOTHER NEVER STOPS
WORKING FOR THE FAMILY.

569
00:20:56,757 --> 00:20:57,790
AND THE MAN.

570
00:20:57,790 --> 00:20:59,525
AND WHAT ABOUT FATHER?

571
00:20:59,525 --> 00:21:01,528
WHAT DOES HE DO ALL DAY?

572
00:21:01,528 --> 00:21:04,798
WELL, HE HAD A PARTICULARLY
HARD JOB TODAY.

573
00:21:04,798 --> 00:21:06,265
DAD PULLS THE LEVER
AT THE BIG HOUSE.

574
00:21:06,265 --> 00:21:08,268
[IMITATES ELECTRICITY CRACKLING]

575
00:21:08,268 --> 00:21:09,568
...BUT HE DID IT ANYWAY.

576
00:21:09,568 --> 00:21:12,072
BECAUSE THAT’S THE WAY FATHER
EARNS MONEY,

577
00:21:12,072 --> 00:21:13,640
BY DOING THE JOB.

578
00:21:13,640 --> 00:21:14,942
A LOUSY JOB.

579
00:21:14,942 --> 00:21:17,843
YOU SEE,
IT IS THE TIME HE GIVES,

580
00:21:17,843 --> 00:21:20,647
THE WORK HE DOES,
THAT HE GETS MONEY FOR.

581
00:21:20,647 --> 00:21:23,383
HERE. WE GOTTA LET YOU GO.
HERE’S YOUR PINK SLIP.

582
00:21:23,383 --> 00:21:25,085
BE OUT OF THE BUILDING BY 5:00.

583
00:21:25,085 --> 00:21:26,853
THANKS A LOT.

584
00:21:26,853 --> 00:21:28,655
...AND GIVE TOMMY
HIS ALLOWANCE TOO.

585
00:21:28,655 --> 00:21:32,225
IN A WAY, THE MONEY
IS FATHER’S WORK.

586
00:21:32,225 --> 00:21:33,427
HMM.

587
00:21:33,427 --> 00:21:34,895
AT HOME, BEFORE SUPPER,

588
00:21:34,895 --> 00:21:36,463
FATHER WORKED
ON THE FAMILY BUDGET.

589
00:21:36,463 --> 00:21:37,897
OH, MAN.
WE’RE IN TROUBLE.

590
00:21:37,897 --> 00:21:39,332
IT ISN’T EASY TO FIGURE OUT

591
00:21:39,332 --> 00:21:41,300
HOW BEST TO SPEND THE MONEY.

592
00:21:41,300 --> 00:21:44,738
BECAUSE THERE ARE ALWAYS
SO MANY BILLS TO PAY

593
00:21:44,738 --> 00:21:47,940
AND SO MANY THINGS
THE FAMILY WANTS TO BUY.

594
00:21:47,940 --> 00:21:49,977
LUXURIES LIKE SHOES AND FOOD.

595
00:21:49,977 --> 00:21:51,845
AFTER SUPPER, FATHER REPAIRED
A BROKEN CHAIR.

596
00:21:51,845 --> 00:21:54,313
FIXING THINGS
INSTEAD OF BUYING NEW ONES

597
00:21:54,313 --> 00:21:56,883
- IS A GOOD WAY TO SAVE MONEY.
- HMM.

598
00:21:56,883 --> 00:21:59,152
YES, SIR, FATHER AND MOTHER
DO A GOOD JOB

599
00:21:59,152 --> 00:22:00,153
OF WORKING TOGETHER.

600
00:22:00,153 --> 00:22:01,888
GIVEN THEIR LIMITED
CAPABILITIES.

601
00:22:01,888 --> 00:22:03,923
LIKE A TEAM.

602
00:22:03,923 --> 00:22:07,427
YEAH, AS FOR TOMMY,
HE’S A SLACKER.

603
00:22:07,427 --> 00:22:11,030
THEY DO SO MANY THINGS
FOR THE WHOLE FAMILY.

604
00:22:11,030 --> 00:22:15,835
AND THAT’S SOMETHING TOMMY
HADN’T THOUGHT ABOUT BEFORE.

605
00:22:15,835 --> 00:22:16,937
A TEAM.

606
00:22:16,937 --> 00:22:18,172
I’VE GOT IT.
I’M RESOLVED NOW.

607
00:22:18,172 --> 00:22:20,440
THAT’S WHAT A FAMILY IS.

608
00:22:20,440 --> 00:22:24,143
A FAMILY IS A TEAM
THAT WORKS TOGETHER.

609
00:22:24,143 --> 00:22:25,845
A LOSING TEAM, BUT STILL--

610
00:22:25,845 --> 00:22:27,947
AND TOMMY WOULD LIKE
TO BE ON THAT TEAM.

611
00:22:27,947 --> 00:22:29,817
SO HE PUNTS A FOOTBALL
THROUGH THE WINDOW.

612
00:22:29,817 --> 00:22:32,618
HE THINKS IT’S SOMETHING
LIKE A FOOTBALL TEAM.

613
00:22:32,618 --> 00:22:35,822
YES, TOMMY LIKES
TO PAY ON A TEAM.

614
00:22:35,822 --> 00:22:38,658
AND HE KNOWS
THAT TO HAVE A GOOD GAME

615
00:22:38,658 --> 00:22:40,493
YOU MUST ALL WORK TOGETHER.

616
00:22:40,493 --> 00:22:41,528
AND TAKE STEROIDS.

617
00:22:41,528 --> 00:22:42,928
AND EVERY MEMBER OF THE TEAM

618
00:22:42,928 --> 00:22:44,297
MUST DO HIS SHARE.

619
00:22:44,297 --> 00:22:45,898
OR HAVE A RICH DAD.

620
00:22:45,898 --> 00:22:49,737
NOW TOMMY WANTS TO DO HIS SHARE
FOR THE FAMILY TEAM.

621
00:22:49,737 --> 00:22:52,672
ONE THING--
HE CAN SAVE HIS MONEY.

622
00:22:52,672 --> 00:22:54,507
NOT ASK FATHER FOR MORE.

623
00:22:54,507 --> 00:22:58,812
AND SO HELP THE FAMILY
BUY MORE THINGS THEY ALL WANT.

624
00:22:58,812 --> 00:23:00,480
AND STARTING RIGHT NOW,

625
00:23:00,480 --> 00:23:03,283
HE CAN HELP MOTHER
BY PUTTING THINGS AWAY.

626
00:23:03,283 --> 00:23:04,818
LIKE HIS HOPES AND DREAMS.

627
00:23:04,818 --> 00:23:06,118
YES, FROM NOW ON,

628
00:23:06,118 --> 00:23:07,920
THINGS ARE GOING
TO BE DIFFERENT WITH TOMMY.

629
00:23:07,920 --> 00:23:09,588
WHOO! HIS FEET STINK.

630
00:23:09,588 --> 00:23:11,758
UGH.

631
00:23:11,758 --> 00:23:13,593
AFTER A WEEK OR SO
OF TRYING...

632
00:23:13,593 --> 00:23:14,627
HE GIVES UP.

633
00:23:14,627 --> 00:23:17,030
TOMMY WAS REALLY WORKING
ON THE TEAM.

634
00:23:17,030 --> 00:23:19,398
WHEN A PIECE
OF TRAIN TRACK WAS BROKEN,

635
00:23:19,398 --> 00:23:20,833
TOMMY FIXED IT HIMSELF...

636
00:23:20,833 --> 00:23:21,902
KILLING 400 COMMUTERS.

637
00:23:21,902 --> 00:23:23,570
SO FATHER
DIDN’T HAVE TO FIX IT

638
00:23:23,570 --> 00:23:26,473
OR SPEND MONEY
BUYING NEW TRACK.

639
00:23:26,473 --> 00:23:29,843
DON’T YOU THINK THAT’S
A GOOD WAY TO HELP YOUR FATHER

640
00:23:29,843 --> 00:23:32,078
AND SHOW HIM HOW MUCH
YOU APPRECIATE

641
00:23:32,078 --> 00:23:33,413
ALL HE DOES FOR YOU?

642
00:23:33,413 --> 00:23:34,647
IF YOU’RE INTO
THAT KINDA THING.

643
00:23:34,647 --> 00:23:36,917
AND SEE HOW NEAT
TOMMY’S ROOM IS.

644
00:23:36,917 --> 00:23:39,718
TOMMY’S GOTTEN IN THE HABIT
OF PICKING THINGS UP

645
00:23:39,718 --> 00:23:41,387
AND PUTTING THEM AWAY.

646
00:23:41,387 --> 00:23:43,290
AND IT MAKES HIM PROUD
WHEN MOTHER

647
00:23:43,290 --> 00:23:44,958
DOESN’T HAVE TO DO ANY WORK
IN HIS ROOM.

648
00:23:44,958 --> 00:23:46,192
NOW THAT HE’S IN HIS PLACE.

649
00:23:46,192 --> 00:23:48,228
ISN’T THAT A GOOD WAY
TO HELP YOUR MOTHER

650
00:23:48,228 --> 00:23:50,563
AND SHOW HER HOW MUCH
YOU APPRECIATE

651
00:23:50,563 --> 00:23:51,932
ALL SHE DOES FOR YOU?

652
00:23:51,932 --> 00:23:54,167
MY MOTHER IS A SAINT!

653
00:23:54,167 --> 00:23:56,470
AND TOMMY HAS THOUGHT
OF OTHER THINGS

654
00:23:56,470 --> 00:23:57,870
HE CAN DO FOR HIS PARENTS.

655
00:23:57,870 --> 00:23:59,538
LAST NIGHT HE DID
A RING JOB ON THE CAR.

656
00:23:59,538 --> 00:24:00,873
IT’S REALLY
MORE FUN THAN WORK

657
00:24:00,873 --> 00:24:02,942
WHEN YOU KNOW YOU’RE HELPING
YOUR MOTHER AND FATHER?

658
00:24:02,942 --> 00:24:05,112
YOU KNOW, MOM, I’M GONNA BE
A MIXOLOGIST WHEN I GROW UP.

659
00:24:05,112 --> 00:24:06,947
WOULDN’T YOU LIKE
TO DO THINGS FOR YOUR PARENTS...

660
00:24:06,947 --> 00:24:11,250
MOM, I TRANSLATED
A BECKETT PLAY THIS MORNING.

661
00:24:11,250 --> 00:24:13,887
THEN HELP TO KEEP YOUR ROOM
CLEAN AND NEAT.

662
00:24:13,887 --> 00:24:16,890
WELL, SEAL IT OFF.
DON’T GO IN THERE.

663
00:24:16,890 --> 00:24:18,858
KEEP YOUR CLOTHES ON HANGERS.

664
00:24:18,858 --> 00:24:21,562
TRY NOT TO TEAR THEM
OR GET THEM TOO DIRTY.

665
00:24:21,562 --> 00:24:22,662
TRY NOT TO EAT THEM.

666
00:24:22,662 --> 00:24:24,630
PUT THINGS WHERE THEY BELONG.

667
00:24:24,630 --> 00:24:26,867
DON’T LEAVE THEM ON THE FLOOR
WHEN YOU’RE NOT USING THEM.

668
00:24:26,867 --> 00:24:29,402
YEAH, WHAT IS WITH YOU
TODAY, TOMMY?

669
00:24:29,402 --> 00:24:31,905
- HELP SAVE MONEY.
- MM-HMM.

670
00:24:31,905 --> 00:24:34,040
REMEMBER, SOMEONE
HAS TO WORK TO EARN IT.

671
00:24:34,040 --> 00:24:36,408
GET PORKY SOME PANTS.

672
00:24:36,408 --> 00:24:39,045
HELP YOUR PARENTS
AROUND THE HOUSE.

673
00:24:39,045 --> 00:24:40,913
THERE ARE MANY JOBS
YOU CAN DO

674
00:24:40,913 --> 00:24:43,417
THAT WILL MAKE THINGS EASIER
FOR FATHER AND MOTHER.

675
00:24:43,417 --> 00:24:46,018
TOMMY SHOWERS ONLY HALF
HIS BODY TO SAVE WATER.

676
00:24:46,018 --> 00:24:47,820
TRY TO THINK UP NEW WAYS

677
00:24:47,820 --> 00:24:49,388
YOU CAN HELP YOUR FAMILY.

678
00:24:49,388 --> 00:24:51,692
AND ASK YOUR MOTHER
AND FATHER ABOUT THEM.

679
00:24:51,692 --> 00:24:52,892
HMM.

680
00:24:52,892 --> 00:24:54,327
THEY’LL BE GLAD THAT YOU WANT...

681
00:24:54,327 --> 00:24:56,162
- AAH!
- OOH.

682
00:24:56,162 --> 00:24:57,597
...HOW MUCH YOU LOVE THEM

683
00:24:57,597 --> 00:25:02,068
AND APPRECIATE ALL THE THINGS
THEY DO FOR YOU.

684
00:25:02,068 --> 00:25:03,670
AAH! NOTHING, DAD.
NOTHING. NOTHING.

685
00:25:03,670 --> 00:25:04,803
I WAS JUST...

686
00:25:04,803 --> 00:25:07,307
...AS TOMMY’S
FATHER AND MOTHER DO.

687
00:25:07,307 --> 00:25:08,808
AND WHAT’S MORE,

688
00:25:08,808 --> 00:25:11,645
BECAUSE TOMMY
HAS HELPED US SAVE MONEY,

689
00:25:11,645 --> 00:25:12,912
MOTHER AND FATHER AGREE...

690
00:25:12,912 --> 00:25:14,147
YOU DO THE VOICE.
I’LL WORK THE JAW, HONEY.

691
00:25:14,147 --> 00:25:16,015
HELLO, BUBBIE.

692
00:25:16,015 --> 00:25:17,783
A BIGGER ALLOWANCE.

693
00:25:17,783 --> 00:25:19,385
A NICKEL. THANKS, DAD.

694
00:25:19,385 --> 00:25:20,787
THAT’S MIGHTY GOOD.

695
00:25:20,787 --> 00:25:22,488
BUT WHAT’S BETTER,

696
00:25:22,488 --> 00:25:25,258
TOMMY KNOWS
HE’S A REAL MEMBER

697
00:25:25,258 --> 00:25:27,160
OF HIS FAMILY TEAM.

698
00:25:27,160 --> 00:25:29,195
FROM SLACKER TO BOOSTER.

699
00:25:29,195 --> 00:25:30,230
THANKS, TOMMY.

700
00:25:30,230 --> 00:25:31,263
THANKS, DAD.

701
00:25:31,263 --> 00:25:32,298
YOU DOPE.

702
00:25:32,298 --> 00:25:33,333
[LAUGHTER]

703
00:25:33,333 --> 00:25:35,002
YOUR BODY LOOKS GOOD.

704
00:25:46,680 --> 00:25:49,548
THIS IS THE STORY
OF A ROBOT NAMED CROW.

705
00:25:49,548 --> 00:25:51,585
CAN YOU GUESS WHAT CROW
IS THINKING?

706
00:25:51,585 --> 00:25:53,118
CROW IS THINKING HARD,

707
00:25:53,118 --> 00:25:55,388
OR AS HARD
AS HE CAN THINK, ANYWAY,

708
00:25:55,388 --> 00:25:57,723
ON HOW THE SATELLITE
GOT SO DARN CLEAN.

709
00:25:57,723 --> 00:25:59,358
IT WASN’T CLEAN THIS MORNING.

710
00:25:59,358 --> 00:26:01,227
THINK HARD NOW, CROW.

711
00:26:01,227 --> 00:26:04,363
THINK REALLY HARD,
YOU POOR DOPE.

712
00:26:04,363 --> 00:26:06,600
SCAN THAT SCRAP HEAP
YOU CALL A BRAIN

713
00:26:06,600 --> 00:26:08,402
AND TRY TO FIND SOME
PITEOUS SHRED OF THOUGHT OR--

714
00:26:08,402 --> 00:26:09,902
HEY, KNOCK IT OFF.

715
00:26:09,902 --> 00:26:11,772
OH, SORRY.
[CLEARS THROAT]

716
00:26:11,772 --> 00:26:14,007
AH, YES. THERE IT IS.

717
00:26:14,007 --> 00:26:16,375
WHO DOES THESE THINGS
WHEN WE’RE TOO LAZY,

718
00:26:16,375 --> 00:26:17,943
TOO BLOATED ON DINNERS
OF RICH FOOD

719
00:26:17,943 --> 00:26:20,747
AND GENEROUS PORTIONS
OF OUR OWN GARGANTUAN EGO?

720
00:26:20,747 --> 00:26:23,182
WHO DEBUGS THE MASSIVE
COMPUTER CONTROL CENTER

721
00:26:23,182 --> 00:26:24,750
BECAUSE OUR OWN
ENFEEBLED BRAINS

722
00:26:24,750 --> 00:26:26,720
CAN BARELY ADD FRACTIONS?

723
00:26:26,720 --> 00:26:28,588
WHO PROVIDES THE WARM,
INVITING WATER

724
00:26:28,588 --> 00:26:31,892
IN WHICH YOU BATHE YOUR FILTHY,
OIL-STAINED CARCASS?

725
00:26:31,892 --> 00:26:34,227
WHO GOES ON MIND-BENDINGLY
DANGEROUS MISSIONS

726
00:26:34,227 --> 00:26:36,930
OUTSIDE IN THE COLD, BLACK VOID
OF UNFORGIVING SPACE

727
00:26:36,930 --> 00:26:39,798
WHILE YOU SIT INSIDE,
COZY AS ALISTAIR COOKE,

728
00:26:39,798 --> 00:26:42,035
SIPPING COCOA AND WATCHING
TINY TOONS?

729
00:26:42,035 --> 00:26:43,903
PINCH YOURSELF HARD,
MR. ROBOT.

730
00:26:43,903 --> 00:26:45,138
YOU DESERVE IT.

731
00:26:45,138 --> 00:26:46,740
YOU THINK YOU’RE ALL
SUNSHINE AND GOODNESS,

732
00:26:46,740 --> 00:26:47,840
BUT YOU’RE NOTHING BUT DIRT

733
00:26:47,840 --> 00:26:49,575
BETWEEN THE TOES
OF AN EVIL TROLL.

734
00:26:49,575 --> 00:26:50,810
THAT’S RIGHT.

735
00:26:50,810 --> 00:26:52,745
WHO PERIODICALLY CHANGES
THE PLUTONIUM RODS

736
00:26:52,745 --> 00:26:55,215
IN THE NUCLEAR REACTOR
DEEP IN THE BOWELS OF THE SHIP

737
00:26:55,215 --> 00:26:57,117
WHILE YOU FEAST
ON GOOEY HANDFULS

738
00:26:57,117 --> 00:26:59,618
OF FIDDLE FADDLE AND PLAY
HOPSCOTCH AND MARBLES?

739
00:26:59,618 --> 00:27:01,387
AND IT’S SPRING,
AND THE LITTLE--

740
00:27:01,387 --> 00:27:04,257
HEY, NOW JUST A DOG-BLASTED
MINUTE HERE.

741
00:27:04,257 --> 00:27:05,958
WHAT ARE YOU
LAYING IT ALL ON ME FOR?

742
00:27:05,958 --> 00:27:08,027
YOU’RE THE LAZIEST ROBOT
I’VE EVER SEEN.

743
00:27:08,027 --> 00:27:10,163
OH, I SEE.
IT’S ME NOW, IS IT?

744
00:27:10,163 --> 00:27:13,132
TOO PAINFUL TO LOOK INTO THAT
DEEP, DARK, TRUTHFUL MIRROR, EH?

745
00:27:13,132 --> 00:27:14,567
YOU MAKE ME SICK.

746
00:27:14,567 --> 00:27:16,068
I THOUGHT YOU LOOKED SICK,

747
00:27:16,068 --> 00:27:17,570
BUT IT’S ALWAYS
HARD TO TELL WITH YOU.

748
00:27:17,570 --> 00:27:19,105
WHY, I OUGHT TO--

749
00:27:19,105 --> 00:27:20,140
UH, HI.

750
00:27:20,140 --> 00:27:22,575
[STAMMERING]
GYPSY.

751
00:27:22,575 --> 00:27:24,177
I GOTTA GO CLEAN MY ROOM.

752
00:27:24,177 --> 00:27:25,878
I’M GONNA GO
CLEAN YOUR ROOM TOO.

753
00:27:25,878 --> 00:27:30,617
HE’S GONNA HELP ME
CLEAN MY ROOM.

754
00:27:30,617 --> 00:27:32,852
OOH.

755
00:27:38,123 --> 00:27:39,492
OH, THE UNEARTHLY.

756
00:27:39,492 --> 00:27:41,127
HUH?

757
00:27:41,127 --> 00:27:43,095
OH,
STARRING JOHN CARRADINE.

758
00:27:43,095 --> 00:27:44,630
THAT WAS KUNG FU, RIGHT?

759
00:27:44,630 --> 00:27:46,700
NO, NO, NO, HE WAS THE GUY
IN REVENGE OF THE NERDS.

760
00:27:46,700 --> 00:27:49,035
OH, ISN’T HE THE GUY THAT DOES
ALL THOSE ALAN RUDOLPH FILMS?

761
00:27:49,035 --> 00:27:51,137
OH, THAT MUST BE IT.

762
00:27:51,137 --> 00:27:52,872
HE’S ALL OF THOSE AND MORE.

763
00:27:52,872 --> 00:27:55,542
MUSIC BY THE EDGAR ALLEN POE
MARCHING BAND.

764
00:27:55,542 --> 00:27:59,945
[IMITATES MUSIC]

765
00:27:59,945 --> 00:28:01,915
YOU KNOW, I READ
IN VIDEO WATCHDOG

766
00:28:01,915 --> 00:28:03,383
THAT GEOFFREY DENNIS
COMPLETELY REWROTE

767
00:28:03,383 --> 00:28:05,052
JANE MANN’S ORIGINAL SCRIPT.

768
00:28:05,052 --> 00:28:07,753
- SHE WAS REALLY MAD
ABOUT IT, TOO.
- OH, YEAH, I READ THAT TOO.

769
00:28:07,753 --> 00:28:08,888
YOU KNOW WHAT I READ
IN STARLOG?

770
00:28:08,888 --> 00:28:10,323
THAT ROBERT A. TERRY

771
00:28:10,323 --> 00:28:11,323
HAD TO BE BROUGHT IN
TO SMOOTH THINGS OVER.

772
00:28:11,323 --> 00:28:13,025
IT WAS--
IT WAS REALLY A MESS, MAN.

773
00:28:13,025 --> 00:28:14,493
DID YOU READ IN FANGORIA

774
00:28:14,493 --> 00:28:16,228
ABOUT HOW RICHARD CURRIER
AND MORTON TUBOR

775
00:28:16,228 --> 00:28:17,530
WERE AT EACH OTHER’S THROATS?

776
00:28:17,530 --> 00:28:20,233
YEAH, THEY SAID THE WHOLE
SHOOT WAS A BIG ORDEAL,

777
00:28:20,233 --> 00:28:22,735
AND THE THREE DAYS
WERE ABSOLUTE HELL
OF THE WHOLE THING, YEAH.

778
00:28:22,735 --> 00:28:24,670
DID YOU READ IN GOREZONE
ABOUT THE TORRID LOVE AFFAIR

779
00:28:24,670 --> 00:28:27,040
- BETWEEN BETTY SINCLAIR
AND PAUL GRANCELL?
- OH, NO.

780
00:28:27,040 --> 00:28:29,242
WAIT, WHY WOULD THEIR
LOVE AFFAIR BE IN GOREZONE?

781
00:28:29,242 --> 00:28:30,710
HAVE YOU SEEN BETTY?

782
00:28:30,710 --> 00:28:31,978
- OH!
- BA-BOOM.

783
00:28:31,978 --> 00:28:33,713
Y’KNOW, I READ IN NEWSWEEK

784
00:28:33,713 --> 00:28:37,950
THAT HENRY VARS
REALLY RESENTED MITCHELL TERR
SUPERVISING HIS MUSIC.

785
00:28:37,950 --> 00:28:39,985
YOU READ NEWSWEEK?
HA. WHAT A LOSER!

786
00:28:39,985 --> 00:28:41,387
HEY.

787
00:28:41,387 --> 00:28:42,555
CAN’T BELIEVE IT.

788
00:28:42,555 --> 00:28:44,723
THE FANZINE SKETCH,
LADIES AND GENTLEMEN.

789
00:28:44,723 --> 00:28:46,625
THANK YOU VERY MUCH.

790
00:28:46,625 --> 00:28:47,660
[DOG BARKS]

791
00:28:47,660 --> 00:28:48,695
HEY, YOUR CAR’S BARKING.

792
00:28:48,695 --> 00:28:49,928
BETTER CHANGE YOUR BARK PLUGS.

793
00:28:49,928 --> 00:28:51,230
AH-HA. YEAH.

794
00:28:51,230 --> 00:28:52,498
SKY.

795
00:28:52,498 --> 00:28:54,533
CUTE.

796
00:28:58,605 --> 00:28:59,638
[DOG BARKS]

797
00:28:59,638 --> 00:29:01,107
WHAT IS THIS,
"DOG ON A HOT TIN ROOF"?

798
00:29:01,107 --> 00:29:04,377
HEY, LOOK. SHE’S DATING
MR. DITHERS FROM BLONDIE.

799
00:29:04,377 --> 00:29:06,078
YEAH, DAGWOOD...

800
00:29:06,078 --> 00:29:08,147
[DOORBELL RINGS]

801
00:29:08,147 --> 00:29:10,383
HEY, IT’S TOR JOHNSON.

802
00:29:13,418 --> 00:29:15,955
AVON CALLING.

803
00:29:15,955 --> 00:29:18,123
TELL DR. CONWAY
THAT WE’RE HERE.

804
00:29:18,123 --> 00:29:19,158
LOREN.

805
00:29:19,158 --> 00:29:20,193
OH.

806
00:29:20,193 --> 00:29:21,227
GOOD TO SEE YOU.

807
00:29:21,227 --> 00:29:22,862
THANK YOU, CHARLES.

808
00:29:22,862 --> 00:29:24,930
THIS IS GRACE THOMAS,
THE PATIENT I PHONED YOU ABOUT.

809
00:29:24,930 --> 00:29:27,033
OH, THOSE--SHE’LL DO NICELY.

810
00:29:27,033 --> 00:29:28,233
PLEASED TO MEET YOU,
MRS. THOMAS.

811
00:29:28,233 --> 00:29:30,035
DR. WRIGHT HAS TOLD ME
A GREAT DEAL ABOUT YOU.

812
00:29:30,035 --> 00:29:32,238
AND WHAT YOU DIDN’T TELL ME
THE PHOTOS WILL REVEAL.

813
00:29:36,108 --> 00:29:38,978
DON’T SAY HI.

814
00:29:38,978 --> 00:29:41,347
I’LL BE UP
TO TUCK YOU IN LATER.

815
00:29:44,750 --> 00:29:46,752
MS. THOMAS, I’D LIKE YOU
TO MEET MY ASSISTANT,

816
00:29:46,752 --> 00:29:48,153
DR. GILCHRIST.

817
00:29:48,153 --> 00:29:49,622
I’M PLEASED TO MEET YOU,
MS. THOMAS.

818
00:29:49,622 --> 00:29:51,090
WE’RE DELIGHTED TO HAVE YOU
JOIN US HERE.

819
00:29:51,090 --> 00:29:52,125
WE’VE BEEN EXPECTING YOU.

820
00:29:52,125 --> 00:29:54,093
I HAVE SOME THINGS TO DO,
DOCTOR.

821
00:29:54,093 --> 00:29:55,162
THINGS?

822
00:29:55,162 --> 00:29:56,295
- YOU’LL EXCUSE ME.
- CERTAINLY.

823
00:29:56,295 --> 00:29:59,065
NOW SHOULD WE MAKE
OURSELVES COMFORTABLE?

824
00:29:59,065 --> 00:30:01,567
CHARLES,
I FINALLY CONVINCED GRACE

825
00:30:01,567 --> 00:30:02,702
THAT THE BEST THING FOR HER

826
00:30:02,702 --> 00:30:04,403
WOULD BE TO PLACE
HERSELF IN YOUR CARE,

827
00:30:04,403 --> 00:30:06,705
AND THAT WITH YOUR HELP
HER RECOVERY HERE

828
00:30:06,705 --> 00:30:07,973
WOULD BE A CERTAINTY.

829
00:30:07,973 --> 00:30:09,208
THANK YOU, LOREN.

830
00:30:09,208 --> 00:30:10,977
I’M SURE WE’LL DO
EVERYTHING POSSIBLE

831
00:30:10,977 --> 00:30:13,012
TO MAKE YOUR STAY HERE
PLEASANT AND COMFORTABLE.

832
00:30:13,012 --> 00:30:15,348
YOUR DECISION TO COME HERE
WAS INDEED A WISE ONE.

833
00:30:15,348 --> 00:30:17,483
OH, SHE’S ANNE SEXTON. OH.

834
00:30:17,483 --> 00:30:19,085
I’M SURE I CAN.

835
00:30:19,085 --> 00:30:20,320
TO START WITH,
WE’LL SEE THAT YOU GET

836
00:30:20,320 --> 00:30:22,255
PLENTY OF FRESH AIR, REST.

837
00:30:22,255 --> 00:30:23,557
THEN OF COURSE
MY TREATMENTS.

838
00:30:23,557 --> 00:30:25,057
I’M SURE YOU’LL
BENEFITED BY THEM.

839
00:30:25,057 --> 00:30:27,060
MY DEAR,
YOU’RE A VERY LUCKY GIRL.

840
00:30:27,060 --> 00:30:29,295
DR. CONWAY’S ONE OF THE FINEST
MEN IN THE FIELD.

841
00:30:29,295 --> 00:30:31,130
OH, IT’S NOTHING.
I REALLY...

842
00:30:31,130 --> 00:30:33,065
...THAT HE HAS ACCEPTED
YOUR CASE.

843
00:30:33,065 --> 00:30:34,800
I’M VERY GRATEFUL.

844
00:30:34,800 --> 00:30:35,902
IF YOU DON’T MIND, DOCTOR,

845
00:30:35,902 --> 00:30:37,370
I’D LIKE TO SHOW
MS. THOMAS TO HER ROOM.

846
00:30:37,370 --> 00:30:39,005
- SURE.
- COME WITH ME, GRACE.

847
00:30:39,005 --> 00:30:40,740
I’LL SEE THAT YOU’RE
COMFORTABLY SETTLED.

848
00:30:40,740 --> 00:30:41,773
OH, UH, BY THE WAY, GRACE,

849
00:30:41,773 --> 00:30:43,242
I’LL GET IN TOUCH
WITH YOUR FATHER

850
00:30:43,242 --> 00:30:45,512
AND ASK HIM TO SEND YOU
THE THINGS THAT YOU NEED.

851
00:30:45,512 --> 00:30:46,880
I’M SURE HE’LL
BE MOST PLEASED...

852
00:30:46,880 --> 00:30:47,913
MORE THINGS?

853
00:30:47,913 --> 00:30:49,148
THANK YOU.
GOOD NIGHT, GRACE.

854
00:30:49,148 --> 00:30:50,317
DON’T FALL OFF YOUR SHOES.

855
00:30:50,317 --> 00:30:53,753
I’LL LOOK IN ON YOU
BEFORE YOU RETIRE.

856
00:30:53,753 --> 00:30:55,655
AAH!

857
00:30:55,655 --> 00:30:56,855
DIBS.

858
00:30:56,855 --> 00:30:58,457
WHAT’S THIS BUSINESS
ABOUT HER FATHER?

859
00:30:58,457 --> 00:31:00,192
NO NEED TO GET EXCITED,
CHARLES.

860
00:31:00,192 --> 00:31:01,827
EVERYTHING’S
BEEN TAKING CARE OF.

861
00:31:01,827 --> 00:31:03,930
OUR AGREEMENT WAS THAT
THE PATIENTS YOU BROUGHT TO ME

862
00:31:03,930 --> 00:31:05,865
WERE TO HAVE NO RELATIVES,
NO TIES WHATSOEVER.

863
00:31:05,865 --> 00:31:08,533
AND I TELL YOU THAT THIS ONE
HAS NO TIES.

864
00:31:08,533 --> 00:31:10,703
PRECISELY,
WHAT DOES THAT MEAN?

865
00:31:10,703 --> 00:31:12,138
I ASK YOU,
MORTON KONDRACKE!

866
00:31:12,138 --> 00:31:14,473
GRACE THOMAS
COMMITTED SUICIDE.

867
00:31:14,473 --> 00:31:15,942
COMMITTED SUICIDE?

868
00:31:15,942 --> 00:31:17,343
SOMEONE SHOULD TELL HER.

869
00:31:17,343 --> 00:31:21,080
HER BAG AND COAT WILL BE FOUND
FLOATING IN THE BAY.

870
00:31:21,080 --> 00:31:22,815
I THINK YOU’LL FIND
THIS ROOM COMFORTABLE.

871
00:31:22,815 --> 00:31:24,817
IT HAS LOTS OF THINGS.

872
00:31:24,817 --> 00:31:25,918
AND DON’T WORRY.

873
00:31:25,918 --> 00:31:27,487
WE HAVE EVERYTHING
YOU NEED RIGHT HERE

874
00:31:27,487 --> 00:31:28,588
UNTIL YOUR CLOTHES ARRIVE.

875
00:31:28,588 --> 00:31:29,622
YOU’RE VERY KIND.

876
00:31:29,622 --> 00:31:30,990
THESE THINGS SHOULD FIT YOU.

877
00:31:30,990 --> 00:31:34,060
OH, AND THERE’S PLENTY
OF BULLET BRAS IN THE DRAWER.

878
00:31:34,060 --> 00:31:36,028
YOU’LL FIND THE OTHER THINGS
YOU WANT IN THE BATH.

879
00:31:36,028 --> 00:31:38,463
- IT’S AWFULLY GOOD OF YOU.
- NOT AT ALL.

880
00:31:38,463 --> 00:31:40,500
NOW I’LL BE BACK LATER
AND BRING YOU SOME WARM MILK.

881
00:31:40,500 --> 00:31:41,833
AND WE’LL GIVE YOU
A LITTLE SEDATIVE.

882
00:31:41,833 --> 00:31:42,868
MAKE YOU WAKE UP RESTED.

883
00:31:42,868 --> 00:31:43,903
TO YOUTH.

884
00:31:43,903 --> 00:31:45,405
TO ETERNITY.

885
00:31:45,405 --> 00:31:46,905
TO TED KENNEDY.

886
00:31:46,905 --> 00:31:48,975
WHAT’S THE WORD?
THUNDERBIRD.

887
00:31:48,975 --> 00:31:51,077
WHAT’S THE PRICE?
40 TWICE.

888
00:31:51,077 --> 00:31:52,445
QUITE.

889
00:31:52,445 --> 00:31:54,080
I’M MORE THAN ANXIOUS
TO SEE YOUR LAST EXPERIMENT

890
00:31:54,080 --> 00:31:55,415
ON JEDROW, CHARLES.

891
00:31:55,415 --> 00:31:56,548
JEDROW?

892
00:31:56,548 --> 00:31:59,085
VERY WELL.

893
00:31:59,085 --> 00:32:00,920
COME WITH ME.
I’LL SHOW YOU.

894
00:32:00,920 --> 00:32:04,590
WE’LL BE BACK WITH
"PONS AND FLEISCHMANN:
THE EARLY YEARS"

895
00:32:04,590 --> 00:32:06,392
- IT’S AL LEWIS.
- HEY.

896
00:32:06,392 --> 00:32:07,427
YEAH.

897
00:32:07,427 --> 00:32:08,695
OH, IT’S ANN B. DAVIS.

898
00:32:08,695 --> 00:32:10,195
UGH.

899
00:32:10,195 --> 00:32:12,265
OF COURSE IT’S JEDROW.

900
00:32:12,265 --> 00:32:13,532
[QUACKING, GRUNTING]

901
00:32:22,108 --> 00:32:24,810
[GROANS]

902
00:32:24,810 --> 00:32:26,645
THANKS.
I NEEDED AN EYE-OPENER.

903
00:32:30,783 --> 00:32:32,985
NO, THANKS.
I DON’T SMOKE.

904
00:32:36,255 --> 00:32:38,223
THIS IS HOW YOU THROW
A KNUCKLE BALL.

905
00:32:38,223 --> 00:32:41,760
I KNOW PHIL NIEKRO
IS OLD, BUT WHOA.

906
00:32:41,760 --> 00:32:43,797
[GRUNTING]

907
00:32:43,797 --> 00:32:45,865
[IMITATES KNOCKING]

908
00:32:45,865 --> 00:32:46,898
WILL HE BE ALL RIGHT?

909
00:32:46,898 --> 00:32:48,467
I’M AFRAID NOT.

910
00:32:48,467 --> 00:32:51,103
PERHAPS YOU COULD
COUNTERACT THE TREATMENT?

911
00:32:51,103 --> 00:32:52,105
OH, THAT’S IMPOSSIBLE.

912
00:32:52,105 --> 00:32:53,673
THEN WHAT
ARE WE GOING TO DO?

913
00:32:53,673 --> 00:32:57,077
WAIT. WAIT AND HOPE
THAT HE COMES OUT
OF THIS STATE OF SHOCK.

914
00:32:57,077 --> 00:32:59,445
[CONTINUES GRUNTING]

915
00:32:59,445 --> 00:33:01,613
AND IF NOT?

916
00:33:01,613 --> 00:33:02,648
[GRUNTS]

917
00:33:02,648 --> 00:33:04,217
WE CONTINUE
OUR EXPERIMENTS FURTHER.

918
00:33:04,217 --> 00:33:05,918
MUST HAVE YOUNGER SUBJECTS.

919
00:33:05,918 --> 00:33:08,153
RADIATION MUST BE
CAREFULLY CALCULATED

920
00:33:08,153 --> 00:33:10,322
IN RELATION TO THE SUBJECT’S
AGE AND METABOLISM.

921
00:33:10,322 --> 00:33:11,657
[GRUNTING]

922
00:33:11,657 --> 00:33:13,458
BUT ISN’T IT POSSIBLE
TO DO SOMETHING

923
00:33:13,458 --> 00:33:16,995
STOP GIVING HIM
BURGESS MEREDITH INJECTIONS.

924
00:33:16,995 --> 00:33:18,732
WHY ARE YOU SO CONCERNED
ABOUT HIM?

925
00:33:18,732 --> 00:33:21,133
I’M AFRAID WE’RE IN
A BIT OF DIFFICULTY.

926
00:33:21,133 --> 00:33:23,102
WHAT DO YOU MEAN,
DIFFICULTY?

927
00:33:23,102 --> 00:33:25,003
A RELATIVE OF HIS SHOWED UP.

928
00:33:25,003 --> 00:33:26,038
A RELATIVE?

929
00:33:26,038 --> 00:33:27,607
HARRY JEDROW HAS A SISTER.

930
00:33:27,607 --> 00:33:29,842
SHE’S BEEN TO MY OFFICE
TRYING TO LOCATE HIM.

931
00:33:29,842 --> 00:33:30,977
HER NAME’S ELLY MAY.

932
00:33:30,977 --> 00:33:32,712
JEDROW NEVER SAID ANYTHING
ABOUT A FAMILY.

933
00:33:32,712 --> 00:33:34,247
I TOOK IT FOR GRANTED.

934
00:33:34,247 --> 00:33:35,982
YOU TOOK IT FOR GRANTED.

935
00:33:35,982 --> 00:33:38,150
IN SCIENCE,
NOTHING IS TAKEN FOR GRANTED.

936
00:33:38,150 --> 00:33:39,252
WHAT ARE WE GOING TO DO?

937
00:33:39,252 --> 00:33:40,252
WHAT’LL I TELL HIS SISTER?

938
00:33:40,252 --> 00:33:43,622
THAT, MY DEAR FELLOW,
IS YOUR PROBLEM.

939
00:33:43,622 --> 00:33:44,757
WAIT IN MY OFFICE FOR ME.

940
00:33:44,757 --> 00:33:46,025
I’VE GOT TO SEE GRACE.

941
00:33:46,025 --> 00:33:48,393
HEY, UH, DON’T FORGET
TO TURN THE GUY OFF.

942
00:33:48,393 --> 00:33:50,095
COME IN, LOBO.

943
00:33:50,095 --> 00:33:52,898
UH, TOR MAKE BUNDT CAKE.

944
00:33:52,898 --> 00:33:53,933
GO AHEAD.

945
00:33:53,933 --> 00:33:56,035
TIME FOR PEDICURE.

946
00:33:56,035 --> 00:33:58,470
LET’S SEE.
NOW WHAT WE’RE GONNA DO

947
00:33:58,470 --> 00:33:59,505
IS TAKE THAT GRAY OUT.

948
00:33:59,505 --> 00:34:01,407
UH, I SEE A MORE
CHIC LOOK FOR YOU.

949
00:34:01,407 --> 00:34:03,408
YOU’RE JUST WAITING TO HAPPEN,
DEAR.

950
00:34:03,408 --> 00:34:06,345
KISS ME. I’M IRISH.

951
00:34:06,345 --> 00:34:09,148
BLUE EYE SHADOW IS A NO-NO.

952
00:34:09,148 --> 00:34:12,218
YOU HAVE COMBINATION SKIN,
SEE?

953
00:34:12,218 --> 00:34:15,120
SO I MIX UP A LITTLE
OIL OF OLAY HERE.

954
00:34:15,120 --> 00:34:16,588
UH, LET’S SEE.

955
00:34:16,588 --> 00:34:19,892
YOU’RE OILY UP HERE.
DRY HERE.

956
00:34:19,892 --> 00:34:23,662
DEAD HERE. OOH.
THAT’S A DEFINITE NO.

957
00:34:23,662 --> 00:34:27,633
OH. HEY. CHECK HIM OUT.
HE’S DOING HIS DANGERFIELD.

958
00:34:27,633 --> 00:34:29,135
AH, NO RESPECT.
NO RESPECT.

959
00:34:29,135 --> 00:34:30,368
YEAH,
DON’T GET ANY RESPECT.

960
00:34:30,368 --> 00:34:33,272
STAIRWAY. HO. IT’S--AH.

961
00:34:33,272 --> 00:34:35,475
WELL, MY DEAR,
YOU LOOK RADIANT.

962
00:34:35,475 --> 00:34:39,078
IF I WERE REMBRANDT,
I’D PAINT A PORTRAIT OF YOU.

963
00:34:39,078 --> 00:34:40,513
TELL ME.
YOU COMFORTABLE HERE?

964
00:34:40,513 --> 00:34:41,647
I MAKE A NICE LIVING.

965
00:34:41,647 --> 00:34:43,182
I LIKE IT HERE VERY MUCH.

966
00:34:43,182 --> 00:34:45,250
GOOD.
NOW TELL ME, MY DEAR,

967
00:34:45,250 --> 00:34:46,518
WHAT SEEMS
TO BE BOTHERING YOU?

968
00:34:46,518 --> 00:34:48,087
UH, YOU’RE SITTING ON MY LEG.

969
00:34:48,087 --> 00:34:52,090
DON’T KNOW, DOCTOR.
I’M ALWAYS SO FRIGHTENED.

970
00:34:52,090 --> 00:34:53,960
FRIGHTENED OF WHAT, GRACE?

971
00:34:53,960 --> 00:34:54,993
CARRADINES ON MY BED.

972
00:34:54,993 --> 00:34:56,195
I’M JUST AFRAID.

973
00:34:56,195 --> 00:34:59,398
WELL, YOU MUSTN’T BE AFRAID.
NOT OF ANYTHING.

974
00:34:59,398 --> 00:35:01,933
OFTEN I WANT TO CRY.
JUST CRY.

975
00:35:01,933 --> 00:35:03,102
SEE THIS SHOULDER,
HONEY?

976
00:35:03,102 --> 00:35:04,570
ANY TIME.
IT’S RIGHT HERE FOR YOU.

977
00:35:04,570 --> 00:35:06,138
I HAVE NO ONE TO TURN TO.

978
00:35:06,138 --> 00:35:08,908
NOW, NOW, MY DEAR. FROM NOW ON
THAT’LL ALL BE DIFFERENT.

979
00:35:08,908 --> 00:35:11,710
I WANT YOU TO HAVE ABSOLUTE
CONFIDENCE IN ME.

980
00:35:11,710 --> 00:35:13,278
TRUST ME IMPLICITLY.

981
00:35:13,278 --> 00:35:15,715
COME TO ME WITH YOUR PROBLEMS.
NO MATTER WHAT THEY ARE.

982
00:35:15,715 --> 00:35:17,650
COME TO ME IN A THIN NEGLIGEE.

983
00:35:17,650 --> 00:35:19,618
TONIGHT I WANT YOU TO HAVE
A GOOD NIGHT’S REST.

984
00:35:19,618 --> 00:35:21,153
TOMORROW YOU’LL FEEL BETTER.

985
00:35:21,153 --> 00:35:23,990
HEY, JOHN,
WHY THE LONG FACE, PAL?

986
00:35:23,990 --> 00:35:25,023
[LAUGHTER]

987
00:35:25,023 --> 00:35:26,825
BONE STRUCTURE.

988
00:35:26,825 --> 00:35:29,095
HEY, JOHN. YOU SHOULD CHECK
THOSE BAGS UNDER YOUR EYES.

989
00:35:29,095 --> 00:35:32,565
WHOO! HOO-HOO.

990
00:35:32,565 --> 00:35:34,367
AFFECTION, ATTENTION...

991
00:35:34,367 --> 00:35:36,068
AN OLD CHARACTER ACTOR.

992
00:35:36,068 --> 00:35:38,003
YOU’RE VERY KIND TO ME,
DOCTOR.

993
00:35:38,003 --> 00:35:40,807
OH, HERE COMES THE REF.

994
00:35:40,807 --> 00:35:42,675
NOT TO DISCUSS YOUR AFFAIRS
WITH ANYONE BUT ME.

995
00:35:42,675 --> 00:35:45,377
- DO YOU UNDERSTAND?
- YES, DOCTOR.

996
00:35:45,377 --> 00:35:47,847
DOCTOR WRIGHT IS WAITING FOR YOU
IN YOUR OFFICE.

997
00:35:47,847 --> 00:35:48,848
OH, THANK YOU.

998
00:35:48,848 --> 00:35:50,015
I ALMOST FORGOT.

999
00:35:50,015 --> 00:35:51,617
GOODNIGHT.
I’LL SEE YOU IN THE MORNING.

1000
00:35:51,617 --> 00:35:53,352
GOOD NIGHT, DOCTOR.

1001
00:35:53,352 --> 00:35:57,088
MM-HMM. HMM. NICE THING.
THANK YOU.

1002
00:35:57,088 --> 00:35:59,858
WELL, WOULD YOU LIKE TO SAMPLE
OUR ANTI-DEPRESSANT CART?

1003
00:35:59,858 --> 00:36:01,427
UH, WE HAVE
BLEU CHEESE VALIUM,

1004
00:36:01,427 --> 00:36:02,462
FLINTSTONES CHEWABLE PROZAC,

1005
00:36:02,462 --> 00:36:04,930
AND WILLIAM STYRON TABLETS.

1006
00:36:04,930 --> 00:36:06,098
TAKE THESE.

1007
00:36:06,098 --> 00:36:08,300
HEY, ISN’T HE THE GUY
FROM MONOPOLY?

1008
00:36:08,300 --> 00:36:10,268
I’VE JUST LOOKED IN ON GRACE.

1009
00:36:10,268 --> 00:36:12,037
SHE WAS IN HER JAMMIES.

1010
00:36:12,037 --> 00:36:13,672
I DON’T ANTICIPATE
ANY GREAT DIFFICULTY

1011
00:36:13,672 --> 00:36:15,040
IN GETTING HER
STRAIGHTENED OUT.

1012
00:36:15,040 --> 00:36:16,075
WELL, I’M GLAD, AND I HOPE

1013
00:36:16,075 --> 00:36:17,677
SHE MAKES AN EXCELLENT
SUBJECT FOR YOU.

1014
00:36:17,677 --> 00:36:19,978
THE SUBJECT WAS ROSES.

1015
00:36:19,978 --> 00:36:21,280
I’VE GIVEN HER THE SEDATIVE.

1016
00:36:21,280 --> 00:36:22,315
THANK YOU, SHARON.

1017
00:36:22,315 --> 00:36:24,317
I’LL BE GETTING BACK TO TOWN.

1018
00:36:24,317 --> 00:36:26,652
GOOD NIGHT, SHARON.
GOOD NIGHT, CHARLES.

1019
00:36:26,652 --> 00:36:27,820
GOOD NIGHT, LOREN.

1020
00:36:27,820 --> 00:36:29,522
- GOOD NIGHT, JOHN-BOY.
- GOOD NIGHT, MCCLOUD.

1021
00:36:29,522 --> 00:36:30,723
THESE MUST BE GRACE’S.

1022
00:36:30,723 --> 00:36:32,225
- I’LL TAKE THEM TO HER.
- WHAT’S THAT?

1023
00:36:32,225 --> 00:36:33,458
I’LL TAKE THESE TO GRACE.

1024
00:36:33,458 --> 00:36:36,828
- NO.
- WHAT?

1025
00:36:36,828 --> 00:36:38,297
LET ME HAVE THEM.

1026
00:36:38,297 --> 00:36:39,532
THAT’S MY PURSE.
GIVE ME THAT.

1027
00:36:39,532 --> 00:36:42,435
SIT DOWN.
WE HAVE TO TALK.

1028
00:36:45,605 --> 00:36:47,573
[GOOFY HUMMING]

1029
00:36:47,573 --> 00:36:50,475
LAUREN.
YOU’RE GETTING CARELESS.

1030
00:36:50,475 --> 00:36:53,245
- YOU FORGOT THESE.
- YOUR PARTING GIFTS.

1031
00:36:53,245 --> 00:36:54,380
WELL, I AM SORRY, CHARLES.

1032
00:36:54,380 --> 00:36:56,248
I’VE GIVEN UP
MY ALTERNATE LIFESTYLE.

1033
00:36:56,248 --> 00:36:57,350
- GOOD NIGHT.
- GOOD NIGHT.

1034
00:36:57,350 --> 00:36:59,452
WHAT ABOUT MY KISS?

1035
00:36:59,452 --> 00:37:01,787
- OH.
- [KISSES]

1036
00:37:01,787 --> 00:37:03,622
DAMN.

1037
00:37:10,963 --> 00:37:12,332
[GRUNTS]

1038
00:37:12,332 --> 00:37:14,367
LIGHTS, PLEASE. LIGHTS.

1039
00:37:14,367 --> 00:37:18,837
WE NEED LIGHTS.

1040
00:37:18,837 --> 00:37:20,907
- WHAT HAPPENED, BOBO?
- UH, I FORGOT.

1041
00:37:20,907 --> 00:37:22,742
I FOUND HIM IN THE GARDEN.

1042
00:37:22,742 --> 00:37:23,775
CAN I KEEP HIM?

1043
00:37:23,775 --> 00:37:25,010
WHAT WERE YOU DOING THERE?

1044
00:37:25,010 --> 00:37:26,312
I’M A TURNIP.

1045
00:37:26,312 --> 00:37:29,148
I WAS TRYING TO FIND MY WAY
BACK TO CIVILIZATION.

1046
00:37:29,148 --> 00:37:30,282
I’VE BEEN HITCHHIKING.

1047
00:37:30,282 --> 00:37:31,950
A GUY DROPPED ME OFF
IN THE MIDDLE OF NOWHERE

1048
00:37:31,950 --> 00:37:33,052
AND I GOT LOST.

1049
00:37:33,052 --> 00:37:35,287
- YOU LIE, JOE.
- I DON’T THINK SO.

1050
00:37:35,287 --> 00:37:37,523
LOOK, MISTER, I KNOW WHAT YOU
GOT IN THE BACK OF YOUR MIND,

1051
00:37:37,523 --> 00:37:38,690
BUT YOU’RE WRONG.

1052
00:37:38,690 --> 00:37:41,160
I DIDN’T COME HERE
TO STEAL ANYTHING.

1053
00:37:41,160 --> 00:37:42,395
THEN WHY HAVE YOU COME HERE?

1054
00:37:42,395 --> 00:37:44,030
I TOLD YOU. I GOT LOST.

1055
00:37:44,030 --> 00:37:46,098
MY CAR RAN OUT OF TIRE.
UH...

1056
00:37:46,098 --> 00:37:47,333
YOU TOLD ME
A FABRICATED STORY

1057
00:37:47,333 --> 00:37:48,467
WHICH WOULDN’T
CONVINCE A CHILD.

1058
00:37:48,467 --> 00:37:49,868
TOR BOUGHT IT.

1059
00:37:49,868 --> 00:37:51,203
OH, MR. SCOTT. YOU’RE NOT
BEING VERY CLEVER AT ALL.

1060
00:37:51,203 --> 00:37:52,572
SCOTT?
WHERE’D YOU GET THAT NAME?

1061
00:37:52,572 --> 00:37:54,373
MY NAME’S HOUSTON.
MARK HOUSTON.

1062
00:37:54,373 --> 00:37:57,310
YOU’RE FRANK SCOTT,
KILLER AND THIEF.

1063
00:37:57,310 --> 00:37:58,978
YOU GOT THE WRONG BOY.

1064
00:37:58,978 --> 00:38:01,513
ARE YOU SURE?
I DON’T THINK I HAVE.

1065
00:38:01,513 --> 00:38:03,548
THERE WAS A DETAILED
DESCRIPTION OF YOU

1066
00:38:03,548 --> 00:38:05,050
IN THE POLICE BULLETIN
THIS MORNING.

1067
00:38:05,050 --> 00:38:06,485
UH, I GOT NEW HEADSHOTS.
THAT’S IT.

1068
00:38:06,485 --> 00:38:08,887
YOU’RE WANTED
FOR KILLING A MAN IN A HOLDUP.

1069
00:38:08,887 --> 00:38:11,323
YOU’RE SICK, MISTER.
YOU OUGHT TO SEE A DOCTOR.

1070
00:38:11,323 --> 00:38:12,958
I HAPPEN TO BE A DOCTOR.

1071
00:38:12,958 --> 00:38:15,093
- OH, TOUCHE.
- OUCH.

1072
00:38:15,093 --> 00:38:16,362
YOU SEE,
LAST NIGHT’S PAPER

1073
00:38:16,362 --> 00:38:18,363
CARRIED YOUR STORY
IN THE FRONT PAGE.

1074
00:38:18,363 --> 00:38:20,432
LEATHER JACKET,
ABOUT SIX FEET TALL.

1075
00:38:20,432 --> 00:38:22,402
ALL RIGHT,
I WEAR A LEATHER JACKET
AND I’M NOT A MIDGET.

1076
00:38:22,402 --> 00:38:23,668
SO WHAT?

1077
00:38:23,668 --> 00:38:25,570
SO HE WON’T BE BOOKED
ON THE SULLIVAN SHOW.

1078
00:38:25,570 --> 00:38:28,307
HAVE A CIGARETTE.
THANKS.

1079
00:38:28,307 --> 00:38:30,910
IT’S A SKIN COMPASS!

1080
00:38:30,910 --> 00:38:31,943
YOU SEEM TO BE A BIT WOBBLY.

1081
00:38:31,943 --> 00:38:34,413
- I’M ALL RIGHT.
- I’M A WEEBLE.

1082
00:38:34,413 --> 00:38:36,015
- I’LL STAND.
- SIT DOWN.

1083
00:38:36,015 --> 00:38:39,585
HEY, I WOBBLE,
BUT WE DON’T SIT DOWN.

1084
00:38:39,585 --> 00:38:43,088
YOU MUST BE OUT OF YOUR HEADS.

1085
00:38:43,088 --> 00:38:46,658
WHY ELSE WOULD A MAN WANDER
20 MILES FROM CIVILIZATION.

1086
00:38:46,658 --> 00:38:48,760
I TOLD YOU EXACTLY
HOW IT HAPPENED.

1087
00:38:48,760 --> 00:38:51,563
I HARDLY THINK SO.
YOU KNOW, I PITY YOU.

1088
00:38:51,563 --> 00:38:53,065
THIS IS A TOWN WITHOUT PITY.

1089
00:38:53,065 --> 00:38:55,100
DOC, THE LAST THING
I NEED RIGHT NOW IS PITY.

1090
00:38:55,100 --> 00:38:56,635
LET’S JUST CALL IT A DAY, HUH?

1091
00:38:56,635 --> 00:38:57,737
WE’LL SAY IT’S BEEN CHARMING

1092
00:38:57,737 --> 00:38:59,072
AND I’LL BE ON MY WAY.

1093
00:38:59,072 --> 00:39:00,438
TOR RESENT THAT.

1094
00:39:00,438 --> 00:39:02,007
YOUR PERSISTENCE
IS ADMIRABLE,

1095
00:39:02,007 --> 00:39:03,675
BUT HIGHLY IMPRACTICAL.

1096
00:39:03,675 --> 00:39:06,378
I HAVE NO INTENTION OF
TURNING YOU OVER TO THE POLICE.

1097
00:39:06,378 --> 00:39:09,282
PERHAPS I DON’T BELIEVE
IN CAPITAL PUNISHMENT.

1098
00:39:09,282 --> 00:39:10,950
OH, I HAVE A BETTER IDEA.

1099
00:39:10,950 --> 00:39:12,418
I’M WILLING
TO OFFER YOU SANCTUARY.

1100
00:39:12,418 --> 00:39:13,452
HERE.

1101
00:39:13,452 --> 00:39:15,020
SANCTUARY. FOR ME?

1102
00:39:15,020 --> 00:39:16,488
SANCTUARY!

1103
00:39:16,488 --> 00:39:17,990
WELL, THAT’S REAL FINE.

1104
00:39:17,990 --> 00:39:20,760
EXCEPT NOBODY
DOES SOMETHING FOR NOTHING.

1105
00:39:20,760 --> 00:39:23,395
I’M HAPPY YOU’VE DECIDED
TO BE HONEST WITH ME.

1106
00:39:23,395 --> 00:39:25,197
I HAVEN’T DECIDED A THING.
I’M JUST CURIOUS.

1107
00:39:25,197 --> 00:39:27,867
I’D REALLY LIKE TO FIND OUT
WHAT IT IS YOU WANT FROM ME.

1108
00:39:27,867 --> 00:39:29,335
PERHAPS SOME ASSISTANCE.

1109
00:39:29,335 --> 00:39:31,137
I MIGHT EASILY USE
A MAN LIKE YOU.

1110
00:39:31,137 --> 00:39:32,405
I DON’T FOLLOW YOU.

1111
00:39:32,405 --> 00:39:35,540
- YOU WILL, SCOTT.
- AFTER YOU READ DIANETICS.

1112
00:39:35,540 --> 00:39:37,543
I SUGGEST WE BOTH RETIRE.

1113
00:39:37,543 --> 00:39:40,012
WE TAKE UP THE DETAILS OF OUR
LITTLE BARGAIN IN THE MORNING.

1114
00:39:40,012 --> 00:39:41,047
NOW WAIT A MINUTE.

1115
00:39:41,047 --> 00:39:42,748
I DIDN’T MAKE ANY BARGAIN.

1116
00:39:42,748 --> 00:39:44,048
OH, YES, YOU HAVE.

1117
00:39:44,048 --> 00:39:46,018
YOU MADE YOUR BARGAIN
WHEN YOU PULLED THE TRIGGER

1118
00:39:46,018 --> 00:39:47,520
AND SHOT THAT MAN DOWN.

1119
00:39:47,520 --> 00:39:49,755
I SUGGEST
YOU KEEP THAT IN MIND.

1120
00:39:49,755 --> 00:39:51,723
YOU’RE A KILLER, SCOTT.
A HUNTED MAN.

1121
00:39:51,723 --> 00:39:52,758
WOW.

1122
00:39:52,758 --> 00:39:53,892
TAKE ALL THE HELP YOU CAN GET.

1123
00:39:53,892 --> 00:39:55,828
MAY MEAN THE DIFFERENCE
BETWEEN LIFE AND DEATH.

1124
00:39:55,828 --> 00:39:57,730
TOR, BUDDY,
YOU CAN DROP YOUR EYEBROWS.

1125
00:39:57,730 --> 00:40:00,967
- YEAH.
- UGH.

1126
00:40:00,967 --> 00:40:02,968
YOU GOT THIS PRETTY WELL
FIGURED OUT, HAVEN’T YOU?

1127
00:40:02,968 --> 00:40:05,670
I’M A SCIENTIST.
THINKING IS MY BUSINESS.

1128
00:40:05,670 --> 00:40:07,607
ALONG WITH
APPLYING FOR GRANTS.

1129
00:40:07,607 --> 00:40:09,708
ALL RIGHT.

1130
00:40:09,708 --> 00:40:11,477
I GUESS YOU WIN.

1131
00:40:11,477 --> 00:40:13,178
I’M AFRAID IT HAS TO BE RIGHT,
DOESN’T IT?

1132
00:40:13,178 --> 00:40:15,647
TAKE MR. SCOTT--
OR MARK HOUSTON,

1133
00:40:15,647 --> 00:40:17,015
IF YOU WANT IT THAT WAY.

1134
00:40:17,015 --> 00:40:18,017
TAKE HIM TO HIS ROOM.

1135
00:40:18,017 --> 00:40:19,252
SEE THAT HE HAS
SOME OTHER CLOTHES.

1136
00:40:19,252 --> 00:40:20,752
HE’LL TAKE YOU TO YOUR ROOM.

1137
00:40:20,752 --> 00:40:23,088
YEAH, I KNOW.

1138
00:40:23,088 --> 00:40:25,390
DOC, I’M AFRAID
YOU’RE A VERY CLEVER MAN.

1139
00:40:25,390 --> 00:40:27,760
THANK YOU, MR. HOUSTON.

1140
00:40:27,760 --> 00:40:29,395
YEAH, TOR GOT NEW BEST BUDDY.

1141
00:40:29,395 --> 00:40:32,865
COME ON, FRIEND.

1142
00:40:32,865 --> 00:40:35,200
HA. THEY MAKE A LOVELY COUPLE,
DON’T THEY?

1143
00:40:35,200 --> 00:40:37,202
SO ROUND, SO FIRM,
SO FULLY PACKED.

1144
00:40:37,202 --> 00:40:38,337
IT’S TOASTED.

1145
00:40:38,337 --> 00:40:41,140
LSMFT.
[LAUGHS]

1146
00:40:41,140 --> 00:40:44,075
AH, THIS SURE IS GOOD GRUB.

1147
00:40:44,075 --> 00:40:46,212
- COLD.
- I LIKE MY TRIX HEATED.

1148
00:40:46,212 --> 00:40:47,647
"EAT," HE SAYS.

1149
00:40:47,647 --> 00:40:50,248
"FOOD AND NUTRITION
ARE IMPORTANT," HE SAYS.

1150
00:40:50,248 --> 00:40:52,250
DON’T START WITH ME, GEORGE.

1151
00:40:52,250 --> 00:40:54,353
STUCK IN A STINKING JOINT
LIKE THIS.

1152
00:40:54,353 --> 00:40:56,388
SIX WEEKS OF GET UP, GO TO BED,

1153
00:40:56,388 --> 00:40:57,590
DO THIS, DON’T DO THAT,

1154
00:40:57,590 --> 00:40:58,990
WALK HERE, SIT THERE.

1155
00:40:58,990 --> 00:41:00,492
SIGN, SIGN.
EVERYWHERE A SIGN.

1156
00:41:00,492 --> 00:41:03,262
- THEY GOT ME ALL CAGED UP.
- NO CABLE.

1157
00:41:03,262 --> 00:41:05,263
I’VE HAD A LOT OF TIME TO THINK
SINCE I’VE BEEN HERE.

1158
00:41:05,263 --> 00:41:07,600
I’M TELLING YOU,
I’M GONNA GET OUT OF HERE.

1159
00:41:07,600 --> 00:41:10,035
IT’S ABOUT TIME YOU GOT HERE
WITH THAT TOAST.

1160
00:41:10,035 --> 00:41:12,605
NOW MAYBE THE EGGS
WON’T TASTE SO BAD.

1161
00:41:12,605 --> 00:41:14,607
COLD.
YOU CAN’T DO ANYTHING RIGHT.

1162
00:41:14,607 --> 00:41:16,242
WHY I EVER MARRIED YOU,
I DON’T KNOW.

1163
00:41:16,242 --> 00:41:18,777
AW, TOR WORK HARD.

1164
00:41:18,777 --> 00:41:20,012
GO ON, GET BACK
TO THE KITCHEN.

1165
00:41:20,012 --> 00:41:22,213
YOU MAKE ME NERVOUS.

1166
00:41:22,213 --> 00:41:23,948
YOU MAKE ME NERVOUS.

1167
00:41:23,948 --> 00:41:25,083
TOR FEEL UNAPPRECIATED.

1168
00:41:25,083 --> 00:41:26,652
WHY DO YOU HAVE
TO PICK ON HIM LIKE THAT?

1169
00:41:26,652 --> 00:41:28,353
HE’S NICE TO YOU,
AND YOU’RE ALWAYS ON HIS BACK.

1170
00:41:28,353 --> 00:41:29,822
I’D LIKE TO BREAK HIS NECK.

1171
00:41:29,822 --> 00:41:31,223
BUT I’D NEED A FORKLIFT.

1172
00:41:31,223 --> 00:41:33,525
LOOK, PUT THAT BOOK DOWN,
WILL YOU, AND LISTEN TO ME.

1173
00:41:33,525 --> 00:41:35,793
HOW LONG DO YOU THINK
THE DOC CAN KEEP ME HERE?

1174
00:41:35,793 --> 00:41:37,563
- LISTEN TO THIS.
- I DON’T WANNA LISTEN
TO NOTHING.

1175
00:41:37,563 --> 00:41:39,865
"HER HAIR FELL FREE
AND HUNG THICK AND SOFT..."

1176
00:41:39,865 --> 00:41:40,900
OH, JACQUELINE SUSANN.

1177
00:41:40,900 --> 00:41:42,200
"SUDDENLY HE RELEASED HER,

1178
00:41:42,200 --> 00:41:44,537
- AND SHE SLIPPED
FROM HIS STRONG ARMS."
- OH, YEAH.

1179
00:41:44,537 --> 00:41:47,105
[IMITATING TRUMAN CAPOTE]
THAT’S NOT WRITING.
THAT’S TYPING.

1180
00:41:47,105 --> 00:41:48,673
IT’S NONE OF YOUR BUSINESS
WHAT I READ.

1181
00:41:48,673 --> 00:41:49,942
I DON’T LIKE YOU READING
WHEN I’M TALKING TO YOU.

1182
00:41:49,942 --> 00:41:51,977
NO REASON FOR YOU TO THROW
MY BOOKS AROUND EITHER.

1183
00:41:51,977 --> 00:41:54,380
I’D LIKE TO TAKE ALL THESE BOOKS
AND THROW ’EM INTO A FURNACE.

1184
00:41:54,380 --> 00:41:56,582
GUYS MAKE A FORTUNE
SCRIBBLING JUNK LIKE THAT

1185
00:41:56,582 --> 00:41:58,550
AND IDIOTS LIKE YOU
SPEND YOUR LIFE READING IT.

1186
00:41:58,550 --> 00:42:00,052
OH, YOU’RE IN A LOUSY MOOD.

1187
00:42:00,052 --> 00:42:01,287
IT’S A LOUSY WORLD.

1188
00:42:01,287 --> 00:42:03,122
SO YOU FIGHT EVERYTHING
AND EVERYBODY, RIGHT?

1189
00:42:03,122 --> 00:42:04,122
YEAH.
DO YOU KNOW ANY OTHER WAY?

1190
00:42:04,122 --> 00:42:05,157
- MORNING.
- WOW. HELLO.

1191
00:42:05,157 --> 00:42:07,727
DAY IN THE LIFE
OF BIOSPHERE TWO.

1192
00:42:07,727 --> 00:42:08,727
I’M NATALIE ANDRIES.

1193
00:42:08,727 --> 00:42:10,862
SOURPUSS OVER THERE
IS DANNY GREEN.

1194
00:42:10,862 --> 00:42:12,530
HE’S WEARING A CHIP
ON HIS SHOULDER THIS MORNING,

1195
00:42:12,530 --> 00:42:14,165
BUT ONCE YOU GET USED TO HIM
HE GETS WORSE.

1196
00:42:14,165 --> 00:42:15,533
- COFFEE?
- YES, IT IS.

1197
00:42:15,533 --> 00:42:16,568
YEAH, THANKS.

1198
00:42:16,568 --> 00:42:17,870
WHEN DID YOU GET HERE?

1199
00:42:17,870 --> 00:42:19,872
LAST NIGHT. LATE.

1200
00:42:19,872 --> 00:42:23,308
YOU DON’T KNOW HOW GLAD I AM
TO SEE A NEW FACE AROUND HERE.

1201
00:42:23,308 --> 00:42:25,343
IF I HAD TO PUT UP WITH
SMILEY OVER THERE ANOTHER DAY

1202
00:42:25,343 --> 00:42:26,445
I THINK I’D SCREAM.

1203
00:42:26,445 --> 00:42:27,512
SO SCREAM.

1204
00:42:27,512 --> 00:42:28,913
[SCREAMS]

1205
00:42:28,913 --> 00:42:30,983
I KNOW THAT’S A LITTLE BLUNT,
BUT LET’S FACE IT.

1206
00:42:30,983 --> 00:42:32,350
WE’RE ALL IN THE SAME BOAT.

1207
00:42:32,350 --> 00:42:33,785
YEAH, THAT WE ARE.

1208
00:42:33,785 --> 00:42:35,753
I REALLY WON’T KNOW
WHAT BROUGHT ME HERE

1209
00:42:35,753 --> 00:42:37,757
UNTIL I TALK TO THE DOC
THIS MORNING.

1210
00:42:37,757 --> 00:42:39,358
WHAT ABOUT YOU?

1211
00:42:39,358 --> 00:42:41,227
OH, I GUESS
I WAS KINDA RUN DOWN.

1212
00:42:41,227 --> 00:42:43,162
- BY A CAR.
- JUST COULDN’T
COORDINATE MYSELF.

1213
00:42:43,162 --> 00:42:44,530
SORT OF MIXED UP TOO.

1214
00:42:44,530 --> 00:42:45,597
BUT I’VE BEEN HERE
FOUR MONTHS,

1215
00:42:45,597 --> 00:42:46,732
AND I’M IN THE PINK.

1216
00:42:46,732 --> 00:42:48,733
THAT DOCTOR
SURE SNAPPED ME OUT OF IT.

1217
00:42:48,733 --> 00:42:50,402
I MIGHT BE GOING HOME SOON.

1218
00:42:50,402 --> 00:42:53,772
HOME SOON? HOME TO WHAT?

1219
00:42:53,772 --> 00:42:55,507
YOU GOT NOBODY WAITING FOR YOU.

1220
00:42:55,507 --> 00:42:58,543
YOU FEEL FINE? OKAY.
DON’T TELL ME ABOUT IT.

1221
00:42:58,543 --> 00:43:00,478
I AIN’T FINE.
I AIN’T FINE AT ALL.

1222
00:43:00,478 --> 00:43:02,480
THAT’S NOT A VERY NICE WAY
TO TALK TO A LADY.

1223
00:43:02,480 --> 00:43:04,015
I DON’T WANNA TALK
TO THAT LADY AT ALL.

1224
00:43:04,015 --> 00:43:05,050
KEEP HER OFF MY BACK.

1225
00:43:05,050 --> 00:43:06,085
AND YOU KEEP OFF MY BACK TOO.

1226
00:43:06,085 --> 00:43:07,418
I DON’T WANNA TALK TO NOBODY.

1227
00:43:07,418 --> 00:43:08,853
WHOA. SWITCH TO DECAF.

1228
00:43:08,853 --> 00:43:10,355
NOBODY WANTS TO HEAR WHAT
YOU LIKE AND DON’T LIKE EITHER,

1229
00:43:10,355 --> 00:43:12,390
BUT THAT DOESN’T STOP YOU
FROM COMPLAINING ALL THE TIME.

1230
00:43:12,390 --> 00:43:13,392
DON’T LISTEN.

1231
00:43:13,392 --> 00:43:15,193
SEEMS TO ME
YOU STARTED ALL THIS.

1232
00:43:15,193 --> 00:43:16,728
WHAT IS THIS?
AN O’NEILL PLAY?

1233
00:43:16,728 --> 00:43:18,930
CRYING OUT LOUD.

1234
00:43:18,930 --> 00:43:20,632
WHAT YOU DON’T LIKE
DON’T MATTER.

1235
00:43:20,632 --> 00:43:21,900
DOESN’T MAKE ANY DIFFERENCE
WHAT YOU DON’T LIKE.

1236
00:43:21,900 --> 00:43:23,135
I CAN SAY WHATEVER I WANT
AND TO WHOEVER I WANT.

1237
00:43:23,135 --> 00:43:24,337
BEFORE YOU DO ANYMORE SAYING,

1238
00:43:24,337 --> 00:43:25,537
YOU BETTER DO SOME LISTENING.

1239
00:43:25,537 --> 00:43:27,038
HO, BREAK IT UP, YOU TWO.

1240
00:43:27,038 --> 00:43:28,473
THE ONLY WAY WE’LL DO THAT

1241
00:43:28,473 --> 00:43:30,642
IS IF YOU START ACTING LIKE
A MAN INSTEAD OF A SCHOOL KID.

1242
00:43:30,642 --> 00:43:32,778
NOW YOU COME WALTZING IN HERE
OUT OF THE CLEAR BLUE SKY

1243
00:43:32,778 --> 00:43:34,145
AND ACT LIKE A BIG WHEEL.

1244
00:43:34,145 --> 00:43:36,415
WELL, LISTEN, BIG WHEEL.
I AIN’T HAVING ANY, YOU HEAR?

1245
00:43:36,415 --> 00:43:38,517
I AIN’T HAVING ANY. DON’T ACT
LIKE A BIG WHEEL WITH ME.

1246
00:43:38,517 --> 00:43:39,552
COMING IN...

1247
00:43:39,552 --> 00:43:40,585
[WHISTLING, APPLAUSE]

1248
00:43:40,585 --> 00:43:42,688
BRAVO. BRAVO.

1249
00:43:42,688 --> 00:43:44,088
DOES HE GET LIKE THAT
VERY OFTEN?

1250
00:43:44,088 --> 00:43:45,623
TWO OR THREE TIMES A DAY.

1251
00:43:45,623 --> 00:43:48,860
I DON’T KNOW WHAT
GETS HIM SO STEAMED UP.

1252
00:43:48,860 --> 00:43:51,030
PROBABLY DOESN’T KNOW HIMSELF.

1253
00:43:51,030 --> 00:43:52,698
POOR DOPE.

1254
00:43:52,698 --> 00:43:54,833
EXCUSE ME.
WHAT ABOUT YOUR COFFEE?

1255
00:43:54,833 --> 00:43:56,135
IT’S COLD.

1256
00:43:56,135 --> 00:44:00,172
TORTURED BY COLD FOOD.

1257
00:44:00,172 --> 00:44:01,607
DON’T DO THIS.
DON’T DO THAT.

1258
00:44:01,607 --> 00:44:03,375
HE’S HAVING HIS TROUBLE AGAIN,
DOCTOR.

1259
00:44:03,375 --> 00:44:05,577
GIVE HIM THE USUAL AMOUNT
OF R-16.

1260
00:44:05,577 --> 00:44:06,612
YES, DOCTOR.

1261
00:44:06,612 --> 00:44:07,813
YEAH. DO THIS.
DON’T DO THAT.

1262
00:44:07,813 --> 00:44:10,482
BIG SHOT.
EVERYBODY’S A BIG SHOT.

1263
00:44:10,482 --> 00:44:12,383
COME ON.
HURRY UP WITH THAT, WILL YA?

1264
00:44:12,383 --> 00:44:13,785
WILL YOU HURRY UP WITH THAT?
I’M BURNING UP.

1265
00:44:13,785 --> 00:44:15,187
- TIME TO ROLL, GUYS.
- OH, LET’S GO.

1266
00:44:15,187 --> 00:44:16,288
HMM?

1267
00:44:16,288 --> 00:44:17,890
OH, I GET IT.
HE’S LENNY BRUCE.

1268
00:44:17,890 --> 00:44:21,093
OH, IT’S JUST A CASE
OF SLIGHT OVERACTING, I THINK.

1269
00:44:21,093 --> 00:44:23,362
ALL RIGHT, DAN.
YOU’LL BE FINE IN A MINUTE.

1270
00:44:33,505 --> 00:44:35,340
THE UNEARTHLY? MAN, THEY SHOULD
CALL IT THE UN-ACTING.

1271
00:44:35,340 --> 00:44:37,843
YOU’RE RIGHT,
TV’s WISECRACKING CROW.

1272
00:44:37,843 --> 00:44:39,812
BUT, YOU KNOW, AT LEAST
ONE OF THE CAST MEMBERS

1273
00:44:39,812 --> 00:44:42,313
IS A DECENT ACTOR WHO’S DONE
SOME GOOD WORK IN THE PAST.

1274
00:44:42,313 --> 00:44:43,915
EXACTLY. JOHN CARRADINE.

1275
00:44:43,915 --> 00:44:45,983
THAT’S WHY I’VE PREPARED
THIS ARTISTS RENDERING

1276
00:44:45,983 --> 00:44:48,153
OF HIS LIFE AND TIMES IN FILM.

1277
00:44:48,153 --> 00:44:49,287
[GROANING]

1278
00:44:49,287 --> 00:44:51,022
COME ON. JOHN CARRADINE
MADE A LOT OF STUFF.

1279
00:44:51,022 --> 00:44:53,092
HE WORKED WITH JOHN FORD
IN STAGECOACH.

1280
00:44:53,092 --> 00:44:54,793
HE WAS IN
DRUMS ALONG THE MOHAWK.

1281
00:44:54,793 --> 00:44:56,595
HE WAS THE PREACHER
IN THE GRAPES OF WRATH.

1282
00:44:56,595 --> 00:44:57,628
COME ON.

1283
00:44:57,628 --> 00:44:58,897
JOEL, YOU’RE MISSING THE POINT.

1284
00:44:58,897 --> 00:45:00,532
WE’RE NOT TALKING
ABOUT JOHN CARRADINE.

1285
00:45:00,532 --> 00:45:02,033
WE’RE TALKING ABOUT TOR JOHNSON.

1286
00:45:02,033 --> 00:45:04,135
THAT’S RIGHT, AND USING
SOME ADVANCED TECHNOLOGY

1287
00:45:04,135 --> 00:45:05,703
CALLED THE VIDEO TOASTER,

1288
00:45:05,703 --> 00:45:07,338
WE’RE PUT TOGETHER
A LITTLE PRESENTATION

1289
00:45:07,338 --> 00:45:10,308
THAT WE LIKE TO CALL
THE MANY FACES OF TOR JOHNSON.

1290
00:45:10,308 --> 00:45:11,777
CAMBOT,
GIVE US A NICE REVEAL THERE.

1291
00:45:11,777 --> 00:45:14,378
YEAH. UH,
IN THE UNEARTHLY ALONE,

1292
00:45:14,378 --> 00:45:16,082
TOR JOHNSON RUNS
THE GAMUT OF EMOTION

1293
00:45:16,082 --> 00:45:19,017
FROM ANGER, TO TENDERNESS,

1294
00:45:19,017 --> 00:45:21,753
TO BEMUSEMENT,
AND BACK TO HEARTBREAK.

1295
00:45:21,753 --> 00:45:22,955
THERE’S HEARTBREAK.

1296
00:45:22,955 --> 00:45:24,757
YEAH. BUT YOU KNOW,
THE TOR JOHNSON CANON

1297
00:45:24,757 --> 00:45:26,092
PREVIOUS TO THE UNEARTHLY

1298
00:45:26,092 --> 00:45:27,325
DISPLAYS THE SAME VERSATILITY

1299
00:45:27,325 --> 00:45:29,495
THAT WAS THE HALLMARK
OF HIS ACTING CAREER.

1300
00:45:29,495 --> 00:45:30,928
WHY, HERE HE IS
IN THE TITLE ROLE

1301
00:45:30,928 --> 00:45:33,565
OF THE ACCLAIMED FILM VERSION
OF KING LEAR.

1302
00:45:33,565 --> 00:45:36,335
AND HERE HE IS
AS BOTH FELIX AND OSCAR

1303
00:45:36,335 --> 00:45:37,937
IN THE FILM VERSION
OF THE ODD COUPLE.

1304
00:45:37,937 --> 00:45:41,640
BUT PERHAPS TOR’S
GREATEST TOUR DE FORCE

1305
00:45:41,640 --> 00:45:43,042
WAS PLAYING THE MULTIPLE ROLES

1306
00:45:43,042 --> 00:45:45,810
IN THE TV REMAKE OF SEVEN BRIDES
FOR SEVEN BROTHERS.

1307
00:45:45,810 --> 00:45:49,313
OH, WHOA. WELL, HE’S NEVER BEEN
IN A JOHN FORD MOVIE.

1308
00:45:49,313 --> 00:45:50,982
WELL,
AS A MATTER OF FACT, JOEL,

1309
00:45:50,982 --> 00:45:52,183
HE HAD ONE OF THE STARRING ROLES

1310
00:45:52,183 --> 00:45:54,787
IN JOHN FORD’S
"SHE TOR A YELLOW RIBBON."

1311
00:45:54,787 --> 00:45:56,322
[LAUGHTER]

1312
00:45:56,322 --> 00:45:58,757
WOW, I’M SORRY
I EVEN DOUBTED YOU GUYS.

1313
00:45:58,757 --> 00:46:02,360
NEVER APOLOGIZE, MISTER.
IT’S A SIGN OF WEAKNESS.

1314
00:46:02,360 --> 00:46:04,395
[ALARM BUZZING]

1315
00:46:04,395 --> 00:46:05,963
OH, WE GOT MOVIE SIGN!

1316
00:46:15,673 --> 00:46:19,077
I HAVE DISCOVERED HOW TO ADD
TO THE 16 EXISTING GLANDS

1317
00:46:19,077 --> 00:46:21,280
A 17TH ONE,
ARTIFICIALLY DEVELOPED.

1318
00:46:21,280 --> 00:46:22,313
A NEW GLAND.

1319
00:46:22,313 --> 00:46:23,315
OH, A DESIGNATED GLAND.

1320
00:46:23,315 --> 00:46:24,683
WHAT FOR?

1321
00:46:24,683 --> 00:46:27,318
THIS 17TH GLAND IS THE SECRET
OF YOUTH AND ETERNAL LIFE.

1322
00:46:27,318 --> 00:46:28,453
THE PROMISED GLAND.

1323
00:46:28,453 --> 00:46:30,188
WITH IT, THE AGING PROCESS
CAN BE ARRESTED.

1324
00:46:30,188 --> 00:46:32,790
I CAN PROLONG LIFE
FOR THOUSANDS OF YEARS,

1325
00:46:32,790 --> 00:46:33,858
PERHAPS FOREVER.

1326
00:46:33,858 --> 00:46:35,760
FOREVER’S A LONG TIME, DOC.

1327
00:46:35,760 --> 00:46:37,695
YEAH, TELL US ABOUT IT.
THIS MOVIE’S A LONG TIME.

1328
00:46:37,695 --> 00:46:38,730
YEAH.

1329
00:46:38,730 --> 00:46:40,165
TO BE ALWAYS EXACTLY
AS YOU ARE NOW.

1330
00:46:40,165 --> 00:46:42,100
TO SEE THE PAGEANT OF LIFE
GO BY YOU

1331
00:46:42,100 --> 00:46:44,302
WHILE YOU REMAIN ETERNALLY
YOUNG AND VIGOROUS?

1332
00:46:44,302 --> 00:46:45,470
CARL JUNG?

1333
00:46:45,470 --> 00:46:46,805
SUPPOSE YOU COULD
WAKE UP EVERY MORNING

1334
00:46:46,805 --> 00:46:48,873
AND SEE YOUR FACE
UNTOUCHED BY TIME.

1335
00:46:48,873 --> 00:46:49,908
LIKE DICK CLARK?

1336
00:46:49,908 --> 00:46:52,110
YES, YOU, MARK. YOU.

1337
00:46:52,110 --> 00:46:54,847
YOU CAN BE THE FIRST MAN
TO HAVE ETERNAL LIFE.

1338
00:46:54,847 --> 00:46:57,148
FOR THREE EASY PAYMENTS
OF 19.95.

1339
00:46:57,148 --> 00:46:58,783
NO, THANKS, DOC.
I’M HAPPY JUST LIKE I AM.

1340
00:46:58,783 --> 00:47:00,152
MARK, TO PROVE MY THEORY,

1341
00:47:00,152 --> 00:47:03,555
I NEED A COMPLETELY SOUND
HUMAN SPECIMEN.

1342
00:47:03,555 --> 00:47:05,157
OH, WELL, I’M UP FOR THAT.

1343
00:47:05,157 --> 00:47:06,292
MENTALLY AND PHYSICALLY PERFECT.

1344
00:47:06,292 --> 00:47:07,325
YOU ARE THAT SPECIMEN.

1345
00:47:07,325 --> 00:47:08,593
THAT’S WHERE YOU’RE WRONG.

1346
00:47:08,593 --> 00:47:10,728
THE WHOLE IDEA’S FANTASTIC.
IT’S CRAZY.

1347
00:47:10,728 --> 00:47:12,932
WHY IS IT CRAZY? BECAUSE
IT’S NEVER BEEN DONE BEFORE?

1348
00:47:12,932 --> 00:47:14,633
BECAUSE IT CAN’T BE BOUGHT
IN A DRUGSTORE?

1349
00:47:14,633 --> 00:47:16,602
YEP, PRETTY MUCH.
THAT’S IT.

1350
00:47:16,602 --> 00:47:19,503
PASTEUR, FREUD,
MARIE CURIE, EHRLICH.

1351
00:47:19,503 --> 00:47:20,538
WESTHEIMER!

1352
00:47:20,538 --> 00:47:21,840
I KNOW MY THEORY’S RIGHT.

1353
00:47:21,840 --> 00:47:24,042
I PROBED IT.
ETERNAL LIFE, MARK.

1354
00:47:24,042 --> 00:47:26,043
- NO, NOT FOR ME, DOC.
- I’M BUSY THAT WEEK.

1355
00:47:26,043 --> 00:47:28,280
LIKE I SAID BEFORE,
I’LL STAY JUST LIKE I AM.

1356
00:47:28,280 --> 00:47:30,215
AND BE BURNED
IN THE ELECTRIC CHAIR?

1357
00:47:30,215 --> 00:47:32,250
I’D RATHER DO THAT THAN BE
A GUINEA PIG FOR YOU.

1358
00:47:32,250 --> 00:47:33,652
MARK,
THIS IS NOT THE FIRST TIME

1359
00:47:33,652 --> 00:47:35,287
A CONDEMNED MAN’S LIFE
HAS BEEN OFFERED TO HIM

1360
00:47:35,287 --> 00:47:36,988
IN RETURN
FOR THE PROGRESS OF SCIENCE.

1361
00:47:36,988 --> 00:47:38,490
I HAVEN’T BEEN
CONDEMNED YET, DOC.

1362
00:47:38,490 --> 00:47:40,458
PERHAPS NOT, BUT YOU’RE
CONCERNED ABOUT NOTHING.

1363
00:47:40,458 --> 00:47:42,093
I’LL TAKE EVERY PRECAUTION.

1364
00:47:42,093 --> 00:47:43,262
I’LL TAKE THE CURTAIN.

1365
00:47:43,262 --> 00:47:44,863
FINAL PROCESS
WILL BE TESTED AND RETESTED

1366
00:47:44,863 --> 00:47:46,063
BEFORE YOUR FINAL TREATMENT.

1367
00:47:46,063 --> 00:47:47,832
AH, I KNEW
THERE’D BE A TEST.

1368
00:47:47,832 --> 00:47:50,102
SO THAT’S WHAT THOSE
OTHER PEOPLE ARE HERE FOR.

1369
00:47:50,102 --> 00:47:53,105
OF COURSE. THEY’RE JUST RUNGS
IN THE LADDER I HAVE TO CLIMB.

1370
00:47:53,105 --> 00:47:55,940
IN SCIENCE, THERE’S ALWAYS BEEN
SOME NECESSARY SACRIFICES.

1371
00:47:55,940 --> 00:47:57,008
NOW YOU TRY SAYING THAT.

1372
00:47:57,008 --> 00:47:58,543
I DON’T WANT ANY PART OF IT.

1373
00:47:58,543 --> 00:47:59,678
NO USE TALKING ANYMORE, DOC.

1374
00:47:59,678 --> 00:48:01,380
I’M GONNA GET OUT OF HERE.

1375
00:48:01,380 --> 00:48:03,382
STOP FIGHTING
AND GIVE ME SKIN.

1376
00:48:03,382 --> 00:48:05,117
I’M SORRY OUR AGREEMENT
DIDN’T WORK OUT.

1377
00:48:05,117 --> 00:48:07,920
SHALL I CALL THE POLICE NOW
TO COME AND PICK YOU UP?

1378
00:48:07,920 --> 00:48:09,520
OH, TOUCHE.

1379
00:48:09,520 --> 00:48:10,555
WAIT A MINUTE.

1380
00:48:10,555 --> 00:48:12,223
YOU TELL THE POLICE ABOUT ME,

1381
00:48:12,223 --> 00:48:13,958
I’LL HAVE A FEW THINGS
TO TELL ’EM ABOUT YOU.

1382
00:48:13,958 --> 00:48:14,993
AND WHO’LL BELIEVE YOU?

1383
00:48:14,993 --> 00:48:16,728
THE HOUSE ETHICS COMMITTEE.

1384
00:48:16,728 --> 00:48:17,828
...YOUR WORD AGAINST MINE.

1385
00:48:17,828 --> 00:48:18,897
YOU’RE A HUNTED MAN.

1386
00:48:18,897 --> 00:48:21,065
I HAPPEN TO BE
A REPUTABLE SCIENTIST.

1387
00:48:21,065 --> 00:48:22,533
IF YOU WERE TO REPEAT
WHAT I TOLD YOU,

1388
00:48:22,533 --> 00:48:25,737
YOU WOULDN’T HAVE THE PROOF
TO SUBSTANTIATE YOUR STORY.

1389
00:48:25,737 --> 00:48:27,805
YOU KNOW, I THINK THAT’S
THE VISIBLE VENUS DE MILO HERE.

1390
00:48:27,805 --> 00:48:29,507
WHAT’S IT GOING TO BE,
MARK?

1391
00:48:29,507 --> 00:48:30,808
SHALL I CALL THE POLICE,

1392
00:48:30,808 --> 00:48:32,945
SUBJECT US BOTH
TO A DUEL OF WITS?

1393
00:48:32,945 --> 00:48:34,680
A DUEL I’M BOUND TO WIN?

1394
00:48:34,680 --> 00:48:37,148
OH, LET THE BABY
HAVE HIS WAY.

1395
00:48:37,148 --> 00:48:38,350
NO.

1396
00:48:38,350 --> 00:48:40,952
I’M GLAD YOU DECIDED
TO SEE IT MY WAY.

1397
00:48:40,952 --> 00:48:42,153
I DON’T HAVE MUCH CHOICE, DO I?

1398
00:48:42,153 --> 00:48:43,722
VERY SENSIBLE CONCLUSION.

1399
00:48:43,722 --> 00:48:46,458
NOW, YOU ARE NOT
TO DISCUSS OR DISCLOSE

1400
00:48:46,458 --> 00:48:48,760
MY CONVERSATION
OR MY PLANS IN ANY WAY

1401
00:48:48,760 --> 00:48:50,662
TO ANYONE AT ANY TIME, ANYWHERE.

1402
00:48:50,662 --> 00:48:51,830
DO YOU UNDERSTAND?

1403
00:48:51,830 --> 00:48:53,565
WHY TALK ABOUT SOMETHING
NOBODY’D BELIEVE?

1404
00:48:53,565 --> 00:48:55,267
DON’T WORRY, DOC.
I’LL KEEP MY MOUTH SHUT.

1405
00:48:55,267 --> 00:48:56,735
HEY, HAL IS READING YOUR LIPS.

1406
00:48:56,735 --> 00:48:58,103
NOW WE CAN START.

1407
00:48:58,103 --> 00:49:00,172
OLD AGE WILL BE CONQUERED.

1408
00:49:00,172 --> 00:49:03,875
YOU’LL BE HERE TO ACCEPT
THE ACCLAIM OF A GRATEFUL WORLD.

1409
00:49:03,875 --> 00:49:05,777
WAIT.
WHO TURNED OFF THE LI--

1410
00:49:05,777 --> 00:49:07,478
HUH? OH.

1411
00:49:07,478 --> 00:49:08,680
GRACE,
THIS IS A WILD BOOK.

1412
00:49:08,680 --> 00:49:09,815
HERE.
I WANT YOU TO READ IT.

1413
00:49:09,815 --> 00:49:12,183
IT’S JACKIE O
AND LEE RADZIWILL.

1414
00:49:12,183 --> 00:49:13,918
BE SEEING YA LATER, HONEY.

1415
00:49:13,918 --> 00:49:17,288
AND NOW, OUR NEXT
MISS MANIC DEPRESSIVE EVENT,

1416
00:49:17,288 --> 00:49:18,290
THE SWIMSUIT COMPETITION.

1417
00:49:18,290 --> 00:49:19,457
MORNING.

1418
00:49:19,457 --> 00:49:20,492
I WAS HOPING YOU’D SHOW UP.

1419
00:49:20,492 --> 00:49:21,893
I HEARD YOU WERE
A PERFECT SPECIMEN.

1420
00:49:21,893 --> 00:49:23,628
- OH?
- GONNA BE AROUND LATER?

1421
00:49:23,628 --> 00:49:25,197
WELL, I DIDN’T HAVE
ANY OTHER PLANS.

1422
00:49:25,197 --> 00:49:26,532
I HAVE TO SEE THE DOC
RIGHT NOW,

1423
00:49:26,532 --> 00:49:27,898
BUT THAT WON’T TAKE LONG.

1424
00:49:27,898 --> 00:49:29,300
GOOD. THAT CASE, I’LL SEE YOU
AFTER A WHILE, HUH?

1425
00:49:29,300 --> 00:49:30,735
BYE.

1426
00:49:30,735 --> 00:49:32,803
- GRR.
- DOWN, BOY.

1427
00:49:32,803 --> 00:49:33,838
[GROWLS]

1428
00:49:33,838 --> 00:49:34,840
[DOG BARKS]

1429
00:49:34,840 --> 00:49:36,808
OH, THAT MUST BE
ELLEN BARKIN.

1430
00:49:36,808 --> 00:49:39,577
- OOH.
- I KILL ME.

1431
00:49:39,577 --> 00:49:40,578
MORNING.

1432
00:49:40,578 --> 00:49:42,380
I RESENT THAT.

1433
00:49:42,380 --> 00:49:44,315
MY NAME’S MARK HOUSTON.

1434
00:49:44,315 --> 00:49:45,350
MARK HOUSTON.

1435
00:49:45,350 --> 00:49:47,485
AND WHAT’S YOURS?

1436
00:49:47,485 --> 00:49:51,088
WHAT’S THE MATTER?
DON’T YOU WANNA TALK TO ME?

1437
00:49:51,088 --> 00:49:52,457
GRACE THOMAS.

1438
00:49:52,457 --> 00:49:53,492
GRACE?

1439
00:49:53,492 --> 00:49:55,227
PRETTY NAME
FOR A PRETTY GIRL.

1440
00:49:55,227 --> 00:49:56,928
YOU BEEN HERE LONG, GRACE?

1441
00:49:56,928 --> 00:49:58,230
YESTERDAY.

1442
00:49:58,230 --> 00:49:59,263
MAKES TWO OF US.

1443
00:49:59,263 --> 00:50:01,265
I GOT HERE LAST NIGHT MYSELF.

1444
00:50:01,265 --> 00:50:03,702
I DIDN’T THINK I WAS GONNA LIKE
IT BEING SO FAR FROM EVERYTHING,

1445
00:50:03,702 --> 00:50:06,372
BUT NOW
IT DOESN’T SEEM SO BAD.

1446
00:50:06,372 --> 00:50:08,707
I’M A KILLER.
WHAT’S YOUR RACKET?

1447
00:50:08,707 --> 00:50:09,842
NOTHING.

1448
00:50:09,842 --> 00:50:11,275
WELL, HOW’D YOU HAPPEN
TO COME HERE?

1449
00:50:11,275 --> 00:50:13,912
MY DOCTOR BROUGHT ME.
HE SAID I’D GET WELL HERE.

1450
00:50:13,912 --> 00:50:15,513
WELDED?

1451
00:50:15,513 --> 00:50:17,582
YOU LOOK FINE. WHAT’S SUPPOSED
TO BE WRONG WITH YOU?

1452
00:50:17,582 --> 00:50:18,883
I LIKE THINGS.

1453
00:50:18,883 --> 00:50:20,852
I GUESS YOU COULD CALL IT
A NERVOUS BREAKDOWN.

1454
00:50:20,852 --> 00:50:21,987
MY 19TH.

1455
00:50:21,987 --> 00:50:24,622
HE’S BEEN VERY UPSET
AND AFRAID.

1456
00:50:24,622 --> 00:50:26,625
- AFRAID OF WHAT?
- UM, THINGS.

1457
00:50:26,625 --> 00:50:28,127
I DON’T KNOW.

1458
00:50:28,127 --> 00:50:30,428
WELL, SOONER OR LATER,
EVERYBODY’S AFRAID OF SOMETHING.

1459
00:50:30,428 --> 00:50:33,232
I’M AFRAID OF SOCK MONKEYS.
GO FIGURE.

1460
00:50:33,232 --> 00:50:34,665
BUT TODAY IT’S DIFFERENT.

1461
00:50:34,665 --> 00:50:36,468
TODAY, EVERYTHING’S
RIGHT WITH THE WORLD.

1462
00:50:36,468 --> 00:50:37,602
I GOT A NICE
PLACE TO STAY,

1463
00:50:37,602 --> 00:50:39,603
PLENTY OF FRESH
AIR TO BREATHE AND, UH...

1464
00:50:39,603 --> 00:50:41,740
I’M TAKING THE FIRST STEP.

1465
00:50:41,740 --> 00:50:44,075
I WISH IT
WERE THAT EASY FOR ME.

1466
00:50:44,075 --> 00:50:45,643
WHAT’S DR. CONWAY SAY?

1467
00:50:45,643 --> 00:50:47,312
ARE THEY IN THE SAME SCENE
OR WHAT?

1468
00:50:47,312 --> 00:50:48,580
WHY NOT?

1469
00:50:48,580 --> 00:50:50,948
DR. CONWAY WOULDN’T LIKE IT.

1470
00:50:50,948 --> 00:50:51,983
TIM CONWAY?

1471
00:50:51,983 --> 00:50:53,852
NO, I GUESS HE WOULDN’T.

1472
00:50:53,852 --> 00:50:56,087
ARE YOU GOING
TO BE HERE LONG?

1473
00:50:56,087 --> 00:50:57,255
YEAH, IT LOOKS THAT WAY.

1474
00:50:57,255 --> 00:50:58,657
HELL,
I’M LOONIER THAN YOU ARE.

1475
00:50:58,657 --> 00:51:00,192
WE’LL BE SEEING
A LOT OF EACH OTHER.

1476
00:51:00,192 --> 00:51:01,927
THAT’LL BE NICE.

1477
00:51:01,927 --> 00:51:03,728
AS LONG AS WE’RE GOING
TO BE HERE FOR A WHILE,

1478
00:51:03,728 --> 00:51:05,197
WE OUGHT TO SEE WHAT THE PLACE
LOOKS LIKE, HMM?

1479
00:51:05,197 --> 00:51:07,265
CAN’T HE SEE PLENTY
FROM RIGHT THERE?

1480
00:51:07,265 --> 00:51:09,133
WELL, I’M SUPPOSED TO REST.

1481
00:51:09,133 --> 00:51:10,702
YOU’VE BEEN RESTING.

1482
00:51:10,702 --> 00:51:12,937
I GUESS IT WILL BE ALL RIGHT.

1483
00:51:12,937 --> 00:51:16,007
NICE SCENE, FOLKS.
VERY NICE.

1484
00:51:16,007 --> 00:51:19,577
JUST SIGN HERE.
NEED YOUR PHP CARD.

1485
00:51:19,577 --> 00:51:22,980
HOIMAN, HOIMAN.
YOU GET ME OUT OF THIS CHAIR!

1486
00:51:22,980 --> 00:51:25,850
ITSY BITSY SPIDER...
MM-HMM.

1487
00:51:25,850 --> 00:51:28,220
EITHER HE’S DEAD
OR MY WATCH HAS STOPPED.

1488
00:51:28,220 --> 00:51:29,620
BA-BOOM.

1489
00:51:29,620 --> 00:51:31,490
HEY, SHE’S PUTTING IT
IN WARM WATER.

1490
00:51:31,490 --> 00:51:33,192
OH.

1491
00:51:37,295 --> 00:51:38,630
DOCTOR,
I KILLED THREE MINUTES.

1492
00:51:38,630 --> 00:51:40,265
GOOD, GOOD.

1493
00:51:40,265 --> 00:51:41,700
DID YOU CHECK JEDROW?

1494
00:51:41,700 --> 00:51:43,802
- YES.
- JETHRO?

1495
00:51:43,802 --> 00:51:45,037
WELL?

1496
00:51:45,037 --> 00:51:46,838
PULSE NORMAL,
HEARTBEAT FAINT BUT REGULAR.

1497
00:51:46,838 --> 00:51:49,173
RESPIRATION STEADY,
REACTIONS, NONE.

1498
00:51:49,173 --> 00:51:50,208
WAIT A MINUTE.
THAT’S ME.

1499
00:51:50,208 --> 00:51:51,710
NONE.

1500
00:51:51,710 --> 00:51:54,178
YOU’VE HANDLED
THAT PERFECTLY.

1501
00:51:54,178 --> 00:51:55,880
WE CAN’T CHECK THE REACTION

1502
00:51:55,880 --> 00:51:58,015
UNTIL HE EMERGES FROM
THE CATALATIC STATE.

1503
00:51:58,015 --> 00:51:59,885
THERE SHOULD HAVE BEEN
SOME CHANGE BY NOW.

1504
00:51:59,885 --> 00:52:01,487
YES, I DON’T UNDERSTAND.

1505
00:52:01,487 --> 00:52:03,255
OH, HOW DO I SHAVE
A FACE THIS LONG?

1506
00:52:03,255 --> 00:52:04,788
WE’LL JUST HAVE TO WAIT.

1507
00:52:04,788 --> 00:52:06,492
CAN YOU SUGGEST ANY FURTHER
TREATMENT, CHARLES?

1508
00:52:06,492 --> 00:52:08,227
- ANYTHING FURTHER, FATHER?
- [IMITATES RIMSHOT]

1509
00:52:08,227 --> 00:52:09,693
IF WE INTERRUPT
THE PROCESS NOW,

1510
00:52:09,693 --> 00:52:11,262
WE WON’T HAVE
THE INFORMATION WE WANT.

1511
00:52:11,262 --> 00:52:13,097
OH, WE’RE ALL USED TO THAT
BY NOW.

1512
00:52:13,097 --> 00:52:15,933
[TELEPHONE RINGS]

1513
00:52:15,933 --> 00:52:18,637
MY GOD, I’M IMPOTENT.

1514
00:52:18,637 --> 00:52:19,670
HELLO?

1515
00:52:19,670 --> 00:52:23,375
1-9-7-6 GLAND.

1516
00:52:23,375 --> 00:52:24,808
IT’S LOREN.

1517
00:52:24,808 --> 00:52:25,843
OH.

1518
00:52:25,843 --> 00:52:27,578
OH, HELLO, D.H.

1519
00:52:27,578 --> 00:52:28,580
HOW ARE YOU, LOREN?

1520
00:52:28,580 --> 00:52:29,882
I’M ALL RIGHT.

1521
00:52:29,882 --> 00:52:30,982
BUT JEDROW’S SISTER...

1522
00:52:30,982 --> 00:52:32,550
HA HA. JETHRO WANTS
TO BE A ROCK STAR.

1523
00:52:32,550 --> 00:52:33,818
[LAUGHS]

1524
00:52:33,818 --> 00:52:35,287
JEDROW.

1525
00:52:35,287 --> 00:52:37,688
BUT SHE’S INSISTING TO KNOW
THE WHEREABOUTS OF HER BROTHER.

1526
00:52:37,688 --> 00:52:39,557
I DON’T KNOW
WHAT TO TELL HER.

1527
00:52:39,557 --> 00:52:42,327
[HUMMING]

1528
00:52:42,327 --> 00:52:43,562
I’M BACK.

1529
00:52:43,562 --> 00:52:45,663
MAKE OUT A DEATH CERTIFICATE
FOR HARRY JEDROW.

1530
00:52:45,663 --> 00:52:47,665
HARRY JEDROW IS DEAD.

1531
00:52:47,665 --> 00:52:49,902
OH, BUT, CHARLES.
HE’S--

1532
00:52:49,902 --> 00:52:51,970
MAN, THAT GUY
IS GOOD ON THAT PHONE.

1533
00:52:51,970 --> 00:52:54,305
HIS TECHNIQUE--
UGH.

1534
00:52:54,305 --> 00:52:56,742
BUT HE’S ALIVE.

1535
00:52:56,742 --> 00:52:57,775
NO, MY DEAR.

1536
00:52:57,775 --> 00:52:59,277
JEDROW IS DEAD.

1537
00:52:59,277 --> 00:53:02,413
JEDROW IS DEAD.
LONG LIVE JEDROW.

1538
00:53:02,413 --> 00:53:03,982
YOU MIGHT WANNA GO TELL HIM.

1539
00:53:03,982 --> 00:53:06,150
IT’S GONNA BE QUITE A SHOCK.

1540
00:53:11,088 --> 00:53:12,123
HI.

1541
00:53:12,123 --> 00:53:13,157
I WAS GONNA SAY PERKY.

1542
00:53:13,157 --> 00:53:14,458
OH.

1543
00:53:14,458 --> 00:53:15,860
SECOND THE MOTION.

1544
00:53:15,860 --> 00:53:17,928
SIT DOWN, NATALIE, AND I’LL
TELL HIM YOU’RE HERE.

1545
00:53:17,928 --> 00:53:21,532
NUTCASE NATALIE’S HERE.

1546
00:53:21,532 --> 00:53:23,235
MAN, THE DOCTOR
LIVES IN THE SAME HOUSE

1547
00:53:23,235 --> 00:53:24,668
AND YOU STILL
GOTTA WAIT AN HOUR?

1548
00:53:24,668 --> 00:53:26,572
YEAH.

1549
00:53:26,572 --> 00:53:28,240
SHE’S NOTHING IF NOT PROMPT.

1550
00:53:28,240 --> 00:53:29,540
AND DID I MENTION PERKY?

1551
00:53:29,540 --> 00:53:32,243
MM. YOU DID.

1552
00:53:32,243 --> 00:53:33,712
WELL, I MUST SAY
YOU’RE VERY PROMPT.

1553
00:53:33,712 --> 00:53:35,847
I WAS GOING TO SAY "PERKY,"
BUT...

1554
00:53:35,847 --> 00:53:37,315
I DARE SAY YOU’RE WONDERING

1555
00:53:37,315 --> 00:53:38,950
WHY I HAD YOU COME IN HERE
THIS AFTERNOON.

1556
00:53:38,950 --> 00:53:40,952
WELL, I THINK I HAVE SOME
VERY GOOD NEWS FOR YOU.

1557
00:53:40,952 --> 00:53:42,453
YOU’RE A WOMAN.
WE’RE CERTAIN OF IT.

1558
00:53:42,453 --> 00:53:43,655
DURING THE LAST THREE MONTHS,

1559
00:53:43,655 --> 00:53:45,057
YOU’VE MADE TREMENDOUS STRIDES.

1560
00:53:45,057 --> 00:53:47,592
IN FACT, YOUR IMPROVEMENT
HAS BEEN MORE THAN EXCELLENT.

1561
00:53:47,592 --> 00:53:49,127
I’M SO HAPPY, DOCTOR.

1562
00:53:49,127 --> 00:53:50,128
[WHISPERS]
AND PERKY.

1563
00:53:50,128 --> 00:53:51,328
STOP.

1564
00:53:51,328 --> 00:53:53,097
...I’VE NEVER SEEN
SUCH RAPID PROGRESS.

1565
00:53:53,097 --> 00:53:55,500
NATALIE, YOU’RE ALMOST
WELL ENOUGH TO LEAVE.

1566
00:53:55,500 --> 00:53:57,835
OH, THAT’S WONDERFUL.
WHEN CAN I GO HOME?

1567
00:53:57,835 --> 00:54:00,338
OH, VERY SOON.
BEFORE I LET YOU GO, THOUGH,

1568
00:54:00,338 --> 00:54:02,373
THERE IS ONE
FINAL TREATMENT NECESSARY.

1569
00:54:02,373 --> 00:54:05,910
[IMITATING
SENSUAL FUNK MUSIC]

1570
00:54:05,910 --> 00:54:08,178
I’M SORRY NATALIE MISSED THIS.

1571
00:54:08,178 --> 00:54:10,182
I WONDER WHY
SHE WASN’T AT DINNER.

1572
00:54:10,182 --> 00:54:11,215
MAYBE IT WAS THE BACH.

1573
00:54:11,215 --> 00:54:13,652
SO DO I.

1574
00:54:13,652 --> 00:54:15,553
I’LL SEE IF I CAN FIND OUT.

1575
00:54:15,553 --> 00:54:17,788
BOY, FROM ONE HOT CHICK
TO ANOTHER.

1576
00:54:17,788 --> 00:54:20,125
DINNER’S OVER,
AND HE’S HEADED FOR DESSERT.

1577
00:54:20,125 --> 00:54:22,127
DON’T YOU ENJOY
THE DOCTOR’S MUSIC?

1578
00:54:22,127 --> 00:54:23,395
YEAH.
THAT’S WHY I’M LEAVING.

1579
00:54:23,395 --> 00:54:24,963
YEAH, SURE,
BUT WE JUST FINISHED DINNER

1580
00:54:24,963 --> 00:54:26,430
AND WE MISSED NATALIE.

1581
00:54:26,430 --> 00:54:28,032
I THOUGHT I’D GO UPSTAIRS
AND SEE IF SHE WAS ALL RIGHT.

1582
00:54:28,032 --> 00:54:30,002
NATALIE ASKED FOR A TRAY
IN HER ROOM THIS EVENING.

1583
00:54:30,002 --> 00:54:32,403
THAT’S A PRIVILEGE
YOU ALL HAVE.

1584
00:54:32,403 --> 00:54:36,875
[ALL IMITATING
BASEBALL ORGAN]

1585
00:54:38,777 --> 00:54:41,880
HEY. SHE’S STILL IDLING
ON THE COUCH.

1586
00:54:41,880 --> 00:54:44,115
SHE HAD A TRAY UP IN HER ROOM.

1587
00:54:44,115 --> 00:54:45,683
IS SHE ALL RIGHT.

1588
00:54:45,683 --> 00:54:48,052
I DON’T KNOW.

1589
00:54:53,625 --> 00:54:57,162
UH, WOULD YOU LIKE TO SEE
THE DESERT TRAY?

1590
00:54:57,162 --> 00:54:58,262
LOOKS LIKE TOR JOHNSON’S

1591
00:54:58,262 --> 00:55:01,532
GOING FOR THE DON JOHNSON
LOOK HERE.

1592
00:55:01,532 --> 00:55:05,137
TOR, DON’T PLAY WITH YOUR FOOD.

1593
00:55:05,137 --> 00:55:07,472
UH, NO, TOR,
YOU GOT IT BACKWARDS.

1594
00:55:07,472 --> 00:55:09,673
TAKE THE TRAY,
LEAVE THE GIRL.

1595
00:55:12,443 --> 00:55:13,478
BONK.

1596
00:55:13,478 --> 00:55:17,548
OH, SORRY, HONEY.

1597
00:55:17,548 --> 00:55:19,483
[GRUNTS]

1598
00:55:19,483 --> 00:55:23,120
WILL YOU GET THE DOOR
FOR TOR?

1599
00:55:23,120 --> 00:55:26,057
OKAY, I’LL JUST PUT YOU
ON THE SEAT.

1600
00:55:26,057 --> 00:55:28,493
IF YOU DON’T HAVE TO GO,
THAT’S OKAY.

1601
00:55:28,493 --> 00:55:31,395
JUST TRY ONCE, OKAY?
OKAY.

1602
00:55:33,898 --> 00:55:35,900
I’M SORRY.
I CAN’T THINK OF THE ENDING.

1603
00:55:35,900 --> 00:55:37,468
I CAN’T THINK
OF ANYTHING ELSE.

1604
00:55:37,468 --> 00:55:39,837
A PRETTY GIRL...

1605
00:55:39,837 --> 00:55:40,872
PARTY GIRL?

1606
00:55:40,872 --> 00:55:42,140
PRETTY...

1607
00:55:42,140 --> 00:55:43,173
PRETTY GIRL.

1608
00:55:43,173 --> 00:55:44,442
- WAKE UP.
- LOBO.

1609
00:55:44,442 --> 00:55:45,510
IT’S ELVIS COSTELLO.

1610
00:55:45,510 --> 00:55:46,712
LOBO.

1611
00:55:46,712 --> 00:55:48,380
I’M SORRY.
LOBO’S NOT IN RIGHT NOW,

1612
00:55:48,380 --> 00:55:49,947
BUT IF YOU’D LIKE
TO LEAVE A MESSAGE...

1613
00:55:49,947 --> 00:55:51,415
LOBO, SEND THEM ALL TO BED.

1614
00:55:51,415 --> 00:55:53,985
LOBO GET YAYAS OUT.
WAIT.

1615
00:55:56,287 --> 00:55:59,523
WHO WORKS HIS EYEBROWS?

1616
00:55:59,523 --> 00:56:01,192
HE DIDN’T EVEN COVER HER UP.

1617
00:56:01,192 --> 00:56:03,495
POOR DEAR.

1618
00:56:05,263 --> 00:56:08,767
TOR WANT FATS WALLER NOW.

1619
00:56:11,035 --> 00:56:12,103
YEAH.

1620
00:56:12,103 --> 00:56:13,203
ONE MORE TIME!

1621
00:56:13,203 --> 00:56:14,205
NO.

1622
00:56:14,205 --> 00:56:16,073
TIME FOR GO TO BED.

1623
00:56:16,073 --> 00:56:17,108
WELL SAID.

1624
00:56:17,108 --> 00:56:18,977
SHALL WE RETIRE?

1625
00:56:18,977 --> 00:56:20,812
WHY? ARE YOU COMING APART?

1626
00:56:20,812 --> 00:56:22,347
OH, THAT’S A DIFFERENT JOKE.

1627
00:56:22,347 --> 00:56:23,380
OH.
[IMITATES RIMSHOT]

1628
00:56:23,380 --> 00:56:25,217
GOOD NIGHT, DOCTOR.

1629
00:56:25,217 --> 00:56:29,787
QUIT EYEBALLING MY WOMAN,
YOU ROTTEN...

1630
00:56:29,787 --> 00:56:31,622
[CLOCK CHIMES]

1631
00:56:31,622 --> 00:56:36,027
ESCHER.

1632
00:56:36,027 --> 00:56:38,797
I LIKE THIS MORE
THAN THE ORGAN, DON’T YOU?

1633
00:56:38,797 --> 00:56:40,298
OH, THOSE SHOULDERS.

1634
00:56:40,298 --> 00:56:41,598
SO WHITE, SO...

1635
00:56:41,598 --> 00:56:43,735
OH, THIS IS GONNA BE GREAT.

1636
00:56:43,735 --> 00:56:45,035
I CAN’T...

1637
00:56:45,035 --> 00:56:46,537
- GOODNIGHT, MARK.
- GOODNIGHT?!

1638
00:56:46,537 --> 00:56:47,705
NIGHT.

1639
00:56:47,705 --> 00:56:49,107
LOOKS LIKE A REAL NICE ROOM
YOU GOT THERE.

1640
00:56:49,107 --> 00:56:51,242
MAYBE I COULD COME--
OH.

1641
00:56:51,242 --> 00:56:53,545
SHOOT.

1642
00:56:53,545 --> 00:56:56,213
DOOR NUMBER ONE,
DOOR NUMBER TWO,

1643
00:56:56,213 --> 00:56:59,550
LET’S MAKE A DEAL.

1644
00:56:59,550 --> 00:57:00,652
OH, NO, NO.

1645
00:57:00,652 --> 00:57:02,820
IT GOES [IMITATES
"SHAVE AND A HAIRCUT."]

1646
00:57:02,820 --> 00:57:04,388
NOT QUITE USED TO THE PLACE,
MARK, HUH?

1647
00:57:04,388 --> 00:57:05,657
WE DON’T KNOCK IN THIS HOUSE.

1648
00:57:05,657 --> 00:57:08,827
YOUR ROOM IS OVER HERE.

1649
00:57:08,827 --> 00:57:11,595
OH, YOU SEE, I THOUGHT
THAT WAS MY ROOM...

1650
00:57:11,595 --> 00:57:13,598
[LAUGHING NERVOUSLY]
SORRY.

1651
00:57:13,598 --> 00:57:16,100
- THANKS.
- FOR NOTHING.

1652
00:57:18,770 --> 00:57:21,105
DID YOU STERILIZE
MY NUMBER 23 SCALPEL?

1653
00:57:21,105 --> 00:57:23,407
I GOT CONFUSED
AND STERILIZED YOUR CAT.

1654
00:57:23,407 --> 00:57:24,875
THIS IS THE NIGHT, SHARON.

1655
00:57:24,875 --> 00:57:27,778
- I’M CERTAIN OF IT.
- WHAT?

1656
00:57:27,778 --> 00:57:29,213
AFTER ALL THE YEARS
OF PREPARATION

1657
00:57:29,213 --> 00:57:30,748
AND CALCULATION, FAILURES.

1658
00:57:30,748 --> 00:57:33,017
ALL POINTING US
TOWARD THIS OPERATION.

1659
00:57:33,017 --> 00:57:35,353
AND YOU MOBILE CATTLE
SHOULD RULE OUT

1660
00:57:35,353 --> 00:57:36,620
ANY CHANCE OF
ABORTED VARIATION.

1661
00:57:36,620 --> 00:57:37,655
IT MUST, CHARLES.

1662
00:57:37,655 --> 00:57:40,123
IT WILL. WE MUST SUCCEED.

1663
00:57:40,123 --> 00:57:42,660
ALL RIGHT.
ADMINISTER THE ANESTHETIC.

1664
00:57:42,660 --> 00:57:45,263
WAIT A MINUTE.
HE’S WEARING PLAYTEX GLOVES.

1665
00:57:47,865 --> 00:57:50,000
SO HE CAN PICK UP A DAME.

1666
00:57:50,000 --> 00:57:51,768
BY THAT TIME, MY LUNGS
WERE ACHING FOR--

1667
00:57:51,768 --> 00:57:55,940
OH, THAT’S YOUR LINE.
I’M SORRY.

1668
00:57:55,940 --> 00:57:58,543
WHOA. IT SMELLS
LIKE LOBO IN HERE.

1669
00:57:58,543 --> 00:58:02,913
HE MUST BE HAVING
A MISADVENTURE.

1670
00:58:02,913 --> 00:58:05,250
HEY, SHE GOT
TWO PIECES OF PIE.

1671
00:58:08,452 --> 00:58:11,455
UGH. I COULD USE THESE
ON MY NEXT ROBBERY.

1672
00:58:11,455 --> 00:58:14,025
[LAUGHS]

1673
00:58:14,025 --> 00:58:16,127
OH, SHE’S GOT
ALL THE EXTRAS IN HERE.

1674
00:58:16,127 --> 00:58:20,832
LUKE, IT IS YOUR DESTINY.

1675
00:58:20,832 --> 00:58:23,702
A BRIGGS AND STRATTON
BREATHALYZER.

1676
00:58:23,702 --> 00:58:25,803
OH.

1677
00:58:25,803 --> 00:58:28,573
HMM.

1678
00:58:28,573 --> 00:58:32,043
SCALPEL.

1679
00:58:32,043 --> 00:58:34,045
AAH!

1680
00:58:34,045 --> 00:58:36,080
PINKING SHEARS, PINK THREAD,

1681
00:58:36,080 --> 00:58:40,252
ELMER’S,
WOOD GLUE, AND GLITTER.

1682
00:58:40,252 --> 00:58:42,853
WHOA! SUCTION. WHOA.
I GOT A BLEEDER HERE.

1683
00:58:42,853 --> 00:58:43,888
WHOA, LOOK AT IT SQUIRT.

1684
00:58:43,888 --> 00:58:45,557
OH. I DID THAT WRONG.
WHOOPS.

1685
00:58:45,557 --> 00:58:46,925
OH, YEAH.
KEEP THOSE COMING.

1686
00:58:46,925 --> 00:58:48,960
KEEP THEM COMING.
HO, HO.

1687
00:58:48,960 --> 00:58:50,962
CLAMP.

1688
00:58:50,962 --> 00:58:52,363
CLAMP.

1689
00:58:52,363 --> 00:58:55,132
CLAMP.

1690
00:58:55,132 --> 00:58:56,167
CLAMP.

1691
00:58:56,167 --> 00:59:00,103
CLAMP!

1692
00:59:00,103 --> 00:59:01,838
WIPE MY BROW.

1693
00:59:01,838 --> 00:59:06,277
NOW KISS ME HARD.
THROUGH THE MASK.

1694
00:59:06,277 --> 00:59:07,278
CLAMP.

1695
00:59:07,278 --> 00:59:08,713
CLAMP.

1696
00:59:10,648 --> 00:59:12,050
SPONGE.

1697
00:59:12,050 --> 00:59:13,217
BOX-END WRENCH.

1698
00:59:13,217 --> 00:59:17,722
BUTTERFLY SCREW.

1699
00:59:17,722 --> 00:59:18,923
NUMBER 23 SCALPEL.

1700
00:59:18,923 --> 00:59:23,928
NOT THE 23 SCALPEL.
YOU’RE MAD, DOCTOR.

1701
00:59:23,928 --> 00:59:28,532
AH, THERE WE GO. I’LL BE
THROUGH HER GOWN IN NO TIME.

1702
00:59:28,532 --> 00:59:31,468
BROW.

1703
00:59:31,468 --> 00:59:33,370
NOW TELL ME I’M THE BEST.

1704
00:59:33,370 --> 00:59:37,775
SPONGE.

1705
00:59:37,775 --> 00:59:39,143
THERE. GOT THE BUBBLES.

1706
00:59:39,143 --> 00:59:40,778
THE GLAND.

1707
00:59:40,778 --> 00:59:43,247
HMM?

1708
00:59:43,247 --> 00:59:44,448
[WHISPERS]
THE MIRACLE GLAND.

1709
00:59:44,448 --> 00:59:45,950
OH.

1710
00:59:45,950 --> 00:59:47,718
THIS IS THE MOST
WONDERFUL SCIENTIF--

1711
00:59:47,718 --> 00:59:48,887
HEY, WAIT A MINUTE.

1712
00:59:48,887 --> 00:59:51,155
THAT’S AN UNCLE JOSH’S
PORK RIND.

1713
00:59:51,155 --> 00:59:52,957
THE BUNNY GLAND.

1714
00:59:52,957 --> 00:59:57,395
[DRAMATIC MUSIC]

1715
00:59:57,395 --> 00:59:59,763
NICE MUSIC.

1716
01:00:02,533 --> 01:00:03,668
UGH.

1717
01:00:03,668 --> 01:00:07,938
THIS BROWN ’N SERVE IS ALIVE!
ALIVE!

1718
01:00:07,938 --> 01:00:10,040
ALL RIGHT.

1719
01:00:13,243 --> 01:00:14,545
SUTURE.

1720
01:00:14,545 --> 01:00:17,082
NO, WAIT.
THIS THING LOOKS DELICIOUS.

1721
01:00:17,082 --> 01:00:19,983
BUTTER. LOG CABIN.

1722
01:00:19,983 --> 01:00:22,753
YEAH, WE SHOULD REALLY
PUT SCUZZY PORT IN HERE
WHILE WE’RE AT IT.

1723
01:00:22,753 --> 01:00:24,755
YEP.

1724
01:00:24,755 --> 01:00:25,790
[SNIFFS]

1725
01:00:25,790 --> 01:00:26,992
IT SMELLS LIKE AN OPEN GLAND.

1726
01:00:26,992 --> 01:00:27,992
[KNOCKS]

1727
01:00:27,992 --> 01:00:29,760
YES?

1728
01:00:29,760 --> 01:00:31,862
- IT’S MARK.
- ARE YOU COOKING IN THERE?

1729
01:00:31,862 --> 01:00:34,765
OPEN THE DOOR, GRACE.
I’VE GOT TO SEE YOU.

1730
01:00:34,765 --> 01:00:37,768
WAIT. LET ME WRAP MYSELF
IN GAUZE.

1731
01:00:37,768 --> 01:00:41,738
WHAT IS IT?

1732
01:00:41,738 --> 01:00:43,273
I WANNA GET YOU AWAY
FROM THIS HOUSE.

1733
01:00:43,273 --> 01:00:45,743
OH, HOW MANY TIMES
HAS SHE HEARD THAT?

1734
01:00:45,743 --> 01:00:47,145
DANGER? WHY?

1735
01:00:47,145 --> 01:00:49,080
DR. CONWAY ISN’T THE KIND
OF A MAN YOU THINK HE IS.

1736
01:00:49,080 --> 01:00:50,113
HE’S AN ELF.

1737
01:00:50,113 --> 01:00:51,148
I DON’T UNDERSTAND.

1738
01:00:51,148 --> 01:00:52,883
I JUST CHECKED
NATALIE’S ROOM.

1739
01:00:52,883 --> 01:00:54,485
HER CLOTHES ARE ALL THERE,
BUT SHE’S GONE.

1740
01:00:54,485 --> 01:00:55,487
SHE’S BEEN GONE
FOR QUITE A WHILE.

1741
01:00:55,487 --> 01:00:57,088
I DON’T LIKE IT, GRACE.

1742
01:00:57,088 --> 01:00:58,322
CONWAY’S A MADMAN.

1743
01:00:58,322 --> 01:00:59,357
I’M AFRAID HE’S DONE
SOMETHING TO HER.

1744
01:00:59,357 --> 01:01:01,525
HOW CAN YOU SAY THAT?

1745
01:01:01,525 --> 01:01:03,862
WELL, THAT COULD
HAVE GONE BETTER.

1746
01:01:03,862 --> 01:01:07,165
I’M REALLY OUT OF PRACTICE.

1747
01:01:07,165 --> 01:01:09,967
WHAT?

1748
01:01:09,967 --> 01:01:11,968
IN EIGHT HOURS
WE’LL KNOW THE ANSWER.

1749
01:01:11,968 --> 01:01:13,470
WHAT DO YOU SAY
WE GO TO THE SWAMP

1750
01:01:13,470 --> 01:01:14,538
AND HAVE COCKTAILS.

1751
01:01:14,538 --> 01:01:15,873
GRACE, HE’S GOT
SOME FANTASTIC IDEA

1752
01:01:15,873 --> 01:01:17,908
HE CAN WORK MIRACLES
TO KEEP PEOPLE YOUNG FOREVER.

1753
01:01:17,908 --> 01:01:19,277
IT’S CALLED PORCELANA.

1754
01:01:19,277 --> 01:01:20,745
HE ACTUALLY TOLD ME HE WANTS
TO USE US AS GUINEA PIGS.

1755
01:01:20,745 --> 01:01:22,913
HE’S EVEN BEEN TALKING
ABOUT SACRIFICES FOR SCIENCE.

1756
01:01:22,913 --> 01:01:24,148
NOW WITH A MIND THAT WARPED,

1757
01:01:24,148 --> 01:01:25,750
THERE’S NO TELLING
WHAT HE’S THINKING.

1758
01:01:25,750 --> 01:01:28,887
I WON’T BELIEVE THAT.
THE DOCTOR’S TRYING TO HELP ME.

1759
01:01:28,887 --> 01:01:30,153
TO HELP MYSELF.

1760
01:01:30,153 --> 01:01:31,688
I CAN’T ACCEPT
WHAT YOU’RE SAYING, MARK.

1761
01:01:31,688 --> 01:01:33,858
YOU’VE GOT TO ACCEPT IT.
YOUR WHOLE LIFE DEPENDS ON IT.

1762
01:01:33,858 --> 01:01:35,225
LOOK, FIRST THING
IN THE MORNING,

1763
01:01:35,225 --> 01:01:37,328
I WANT YOU TO GO AND SEE CONWAY
AND GET YOUR RELEASE.

1764
01:01:37,328 --> 01:01:38,595
I DON’T CARE
WHAT YOU TELL HIM,

1765
01:01:38,595 --> 01:01:41,698
BUT SOMEHOW CONVINCE HIM
YOU HAVE TO GO HOME.

1766
01:01:41,698 --> 01:01:44,168
I’M HERE UNDER
MY OWN DOCTOR’S ADVICE.

1767
01:01:44,168 --> 01:01:46,537
YOUR DOCTOR’S
CLAUS VON BULOW.

1768
01:01:46,537 --> 01:01:47,572
DON’T YOU UNDERSTAND?

1769
01:01:47,572 --> 01:01:48,538
YOU HAVE TO GET OUT
OF THIS HOUSE

1770
01:01:48,538 --> 01:01:49,640
BEFORE IT’S TOO LATE.

1771
01:01:49,640 --> 01:01:50,975
YOU’D BETTER
GET OUT OF THIS ROOM

1772
01:01:50,975 --> 01:01:52,577
BEFORE DOCTOR CONWAY
FINDS YOU HERE.

1773
01:01:52,577 --> 01:01:54,212
I DON’T THINK HE’D APPROVE.

1774
01:01:54,212 --> 01:01:55,345
GRACE--

1775
01:01:55,345 --> 01:01:57,215
I’M GOING TO CALL
THE HOUSE MOTHER.

1776
01:01:57,215 --> 01:02:01,318
STRANGE PLACE
FOR A HUMMINGBIRD FEEDER.

1777
01:02:01,318 --> 01:02:03,487
GET SOME DUCT TAPE.

1778
01:02:06,357 --> 01:02:08,625
THING ON. THIS THING ON.

1779
01:02:08,625 --> 01:02:12,130
THAT THING.
THEN THAT OTHER THING ON.

1780
01:02:12,130 --> 01:02:14,198
OKAY, LET’S SEE.
GARAGE LIGHTS ON,

1781
01:02:14,198 --> 01:02:17,235
KITCHEN LIGHTS ON.

1782
01:02:17,235 --> 01:02:18,468
READY.
[SUSTAINED TONE]

1783
01:02:18,468 --> 01:02:20,538
OH, THEY TURNED ON
THE EMERGENCY BROADCAST SYSTEM.

1784
01:02:20,538 --> 01:02:22,907
HMM.

1785
01:02:22,907 --> 01:02:23,942
14.

1786
01:02:23,942 --> 01:02:24,975
- 26.
- SKIDOO!

1787
01:02:24,975 --> 01:02:26,143
50%.

1788
01:02:26,143 --> 01:02:27,812
EIGHT ACRES.

1789
01:02:27,812 --> 01:02:28,847
50%.

1790
01:02:28,847 --> 01:02:31,282
- READING?
- 12 HECTARES.

1791
01:02:31,282 --> 01:02:32,883
26 1/4.

1792
01:02:32,883 --> 01:02:33,918
ONE CUBIT.

1793
01:02:33,918 --> 01:02:34,952
26 1/4.

1794
01:02:34,952 --> 01:02:36,387
50%.

1795
01:02:36,387 --> 01:02:37,555
- HUT, HUT.
- 50%.

1796
01:02:37,555 --> 01:02:40,558
- READING?
- PLUS 2.4.

1797
01:02:40,558 --> 01:02:42,727
INCREASE 2%.

1798
01:02:42,727 --> 01:02:44,195
A QUART OF 2%.

1799
01:02:44,195 --> 01:02:46,197
- INCREASE 2%.
- READING?

1800
01:02:46,197 --> 01:02:48,598
- PLUS 2.48.
- MINUS THREE.

1801
01:02:48,598 --> 01:02:50,835
INCREASE SLOWLY TO 55.

1802
01:02:50,835 --> 01:02:52,237
IS HE READING POETRY AGAIN?

1803
01:02:52,237 --> 01:02:53,703
INCREASE SLOWLY TO 55.

1804
01:02:53,703 --> 01:02:55,205
HE’S MAKING IT UP
AS HE GOES ALONG.

1805
01:02:55,205 --> 01:02:56,440
I THINK SO.

1806
01:02:56,440 --> 01:02:59,010
HEY.

1807
01:02:59,010 --> 01:03:00,612
- TEN.
- ARE WE NOT MEN?

1808
01:03:00,612 --> 01:03:02,280
- NINE.
- A BAJILLION.

1809
01:03:02,280 --> 01:03:04,048
- EIGHT.
- 20. - 50%.

1810
01:03:04,048 --> 01:03:05,483
- SEVEN.
- ELEVEN.

1811
01:03:05,483 --> 01:03:06,483
AVOGADRO’S NUMBER.

1812
01:03:06,483 --> 01:03:07,852
BOOGAH, BOOGAH,
BOOGAH, BOOGAH.

1813
01:03:07,852 --> 01:03:08,887
NEWMAN!

1814
01:03:08,887 --> 01:03:10,955
FIVE...FOUR...

1815
01:03:10,955 --> 01:03:11,988
BOOGER.

1816
01:03:11,988 --> 01:03:16,593
THREE...TWO...ONE...

1817
01:03:16,593 --> 01:03:17,628
ZERO!

1818
01:03:17,628 --> 01:03:19,097
OOH, IT’S GREAT!

1819
01:03:19,097 --> 01:03:21,265
HUH?

1820
01:03:21,265 --> 01:03:23,767
MOM?

1821
01:03:23,767 --> 01:03:28,505
WHAT’S ALL THE RACKET?

1822
01:03:28,505 --> 01:03:31,242
[GROANING]

1823
01:03:31,242 --> 01:03:32,343
HER THERMOMETER POPPED UP.

1824
01:03:32,343 --> 01:03:33,377
SHE’S DONE.

1825
01:03:33,377 --> 01:03:35,613
OH. SHE’S DELICIOUS.

1826
01:03:41,152 --> 01:03:43,187
OH, GREAT. THEY’VE MOVED
THE MOVIE INTO THE BASEMENT.

1827
01:03:43,187 --> 01:03:45,222
THEY’RE REALLY REACHING NOW.

1828
01:03:45,222 --> 01:03:49,193
HERE IN THE WINE CELLARS
OF ERNEST AND JULIO GALLO--

1829
01:03:49,193 --> 01:03:50,360
ALL THE BEST.

1830
01:03:50,360 --> 01:03:54,965
UH, THIS’LL BE
THE BOYS ROOM OVER HERE.

1831
01:03:54,965 --> 01:03:56,433
EIGHT HOURS ON THE DOT.

1832
01:03:56,433 --> 01:03:58,535
WELL, GOODNIGHT.

1833
01:03:58,535 --> 01:03:59,570
THIS IS IT.

1834
01:03:59,570 --> 01:04:01,472
UH-HUH. NOW LET’S, UH--
HMM.

1835
01:04:01,472 --> 01:04:02,507
DOOR’S KINDA TOUGH.

1836
01:04:02,507 --> 01:04:04,875
IT, UH, OH, SEE?
IT PULLS OUT.

1837
01:04:04,875 --> 01:04:08,145
I’M SORRY.

1838
01:04:08,145 --> 01:04:11,848
OH, CRAP. AGAIN?

1839
01:04:11,848 --> 01:04:12,983
- UGH.
- NO.

1840
01:04:12,983 --> 01:04:14,552
NO, IT CAN’T BE.

1841
01:04:14,552 --> 01:04:16,620
YES, IT CAN.

1842
01:04:23,727 --> 01:04:26,030
- EW.
- ICK.

1843
01:04:29,033 --> 01:04:32,102
OH, NO.
SHE LOOKS LIKE ME.

1844
01:04:32,102 --> 01:04:33,837
HOW COULD THIS HAVE HAPPENED?

1845
01:04:33,837 --> 01:04:35,405
I TOOK EVERY PRECAUTION.

1846
01:04:35,405 --> 01:04:36,840
I WASHED MY HANDS--

1847
01:04:36,840 --> 01:04:39,410
MEDICAL SCHOOL.
THAT’S IT. MEDICAL SCHOOL.

1848
01:04:39,410 --> 01:04:43,213
CRIPES. I’VE TURNED HER
INTO A SLEESTAK!

1849
01:04:43,213 --> 01:04:46,817
PUT THAT SIDE
AGAINST THE WALL.

1850
01:04:46,817 --> 01:04:48,485
WELL, DEAR,
I’VE GOT SOME BAD NEWS.

1851
01:04:48,485 --> 01:04:52,557
YOUR MODELING CAREER
IS DOWN THE TOILET.

1852
01:04:52,557 --> 01:04:55,827
UGH.

1853
01:04:55,827 --> 01:04:56,827
[NERVOUS LAUGH]

1854
01:04:56,827 --> 01:04:58,963
UH, MIND IF I SKIP DINNER?

1855
01:04:58,963 --> 01:05:01,898
I’M A BIT OFF MY FOOD.

1856
01:05:01,898 --> 01:05:04,368
WELL, MAY I SAY
HOW SORRY I AM

1857
01:05:04,368 --> 01:05:06,770
AND SMALL MISTAKE
WITH YOUR CHART.

1858
01:05:06,770 --> 01:05:09,640
UH, LOOK ON THE BRIGHT SIDE.
UGH.

1859
01:05:09,640 --> 01:05:11,275
DON’T BE DISCOURAGED, CHARLES.

1860
01:05:11,275 --> 01:05:12,410
YOU’LL SUCCEED.

1861
01:05:12,410 --> 01:05:14,512
ALL THESE YEARS
OF STUDY AND HARD WORK

1862
01:05:14,512 --> 01:05:15,847
CAN’T GO UNREWARDED.

1863
01:05:15,847 --> 01:05:19,317
YEAH. SURE. WHATEVER.

1864
01:05:19,317 --> 01:05:20,752
ICK.

1865
01:05:20,752 --> 01:05:23,553
UGH.

1866
01:05:23,553 --> 01:05:25,355
[DOOR OPENS]

1867
01:05:25,355 --> 01:05:27,692
GOOD MORNING, GRACE, MARK.

1868
01:05:27,692 --> 01:05:29,393
GOOD MORNING, DOCTOR.

1869
01:05:29,393 --> 01:05:30,393
DOC.

1870
01:05:30,393 --> 01:05:32,028
I’M GOING ON UPSTAIRS.

1871
01:05:32,028 --> 01:05:34,932
PAUL BUNYAN,
WHERE’S YOUR BLUE OX?

1872
01:05:34,932 --> 01:05:36,667
WILL YOU COME INTO
THE COMMON ROOM, MY DEAR?

1873
01:05:36,667 --> 01:05:40,070
I’D LIKE TO TALK TO YOU.

1874
01:05:40,070 --> 01:05:41,572
NICE.

1875
01:05:41,572 --> 01:05:44,042
MY DEAR, YOU’RE TO BE
CONGRATULATED.

1876
01:05:44,042 --> 01:05:45,677
YOUR CONDITION HAS IMPROVED.

1877
01:05:45,677 --> 01:05:46,943
IF YOU CONTINUE
IN THIS MANNER,

1878
01:05:46,943 --> 01:05:48,778
YOU’LL BE ENTIRELY WELL
IN NO TIME.

1879
01:05:48,778 --> 01:05:50,313
I HOPE SO.

1880
01:05:50,313 --> 01:05:51,815
COME AND SIT DOWN.

1881
01:05:51,815 --> 01:05:54,918
ETHAN ALLEN.

1882
01:05:54,918 --> 01:05:56,387
TELL ME, GRACE...

1883
01:05:56,387 --> 01:05:58,055
DO YOU CARE
HOW YOUR SKIN LOOKS?

1884
01:05:58,055 --> 01:05:59,323
LOOK OUT FOR THE SNACK BOWL!
OH.

1885
01:05:59,323 --> 01:06:00,825
WHAT DOES A YOUNG COUPLE
TALK ABOUT

1886
01:06:00,825 --> 01:06:01,992
WHEN THEY WALK
IN THE GARDEN?

1887
01:06:01,992 --> 01:06:04,395
I’M AFRAID A LITTLE
TOO OLD TO REMEMBER.

1888
01:06:04,395 --> 01:06:07,565
MANY THINGS.
MOSTLY ABOUT NATALIE.

1889
01:06:07,565 --> 01:06:09,867
REALLY?
WELL, WHAT ABOUT HER?

1890
01:06:09,867 --> 01:06:12,135
MARK SEEMS WORRIED
ABOUT HER.

1891
01:06:12,135 --> 01:06:13,437
WHY?

1892
01:06:13,437 --> 01:06:15,873
HE SEEMS TO THINK
SHE’S ILL OR SOMETHING.

1893
01:06:15,873 --> 01:06:17,173
NONSENSE, MY DEAR.

1894
01:06:17,173 --> 01:06:19,477
SHE MADE A PERFECT RECOVERY
AND I RELEASED HER.

1895
01:06:19,477 --> 01:06:21,278
I DROVE HER TO THE TRAIN
THIS MORNING MYSELF.

1896
01:06:21,278 --> 01:06:22,312
SHE LEFT RATHER EARLY,

1897
01:06:22,312 --> 01:06:24,148
SO SHE ASKED ME
TO MAKE HER GOODBYES.

1898
01:06:24,148 --> 01:06:25,315
I’M SO HAPPY FOR HER.

1899
01:06:25,315 --> 01:06:27,652
SHE LOOKS LIKE
IRENE RYAN, BUT...

1900
01:06:27,652 --> 01:06:30,120
GRACE, YOU’VE MADE
SUCH FINE PROGRESS.

1901
01:06:30,120 --> 01:06:32,990
I’D HATE TO HAVE ANYTHING
STAND IN YOUR WAY.

1902
01:06:32,990 --> 01:06:35,927
LOOK, JOHN,
JUST PICK A SEAT AND SIT DOWN.

1903
01:06:35,927 --> 01:06:37,260
...LIMIT YOUR ASSOCIATION
WITH MARK.

1904
01:06:37,260 --> 01:06:38,695
WHY?

1905
01:06:38,695 --> 01:06:40,732
WELL, NO MATTER
HOW I PHRASE IT,

1906
01:06:40,732 --> 01:06:42,065
IT’LL SOUND HARSH
TO YOU, BUT...

1907
01:06:42,065 --> 01:06:43,267
I’M A NAZI.

1908
01:06:43,267 --> 01:06:44,835
OOH, THAT DOES SOUND HARSH,
DOESN’T IT?

1909
01:06:44,835 --> 01:06:45,870
DANGEROUS?

1910
01:06:45,870 --> 01:06:47,605
YES.
VERY DANGEROUS.

1911
01:06:47,605 --> 01:06:49,307
THERE’S NO TELLING
WHAT HE MIGHT DO.

1912
01:06:49,307 --> 01:06:50,842
I DON’T UNDERSTAND.

1913
01:06:50,842 --> 01:06:51,875
MY DEAR.

1914
01:06:51,875 --> 01:06:53,410
YEAH, COME ON.
SCOOCH OVER.

1915
01:06:53,410 --> 01:06:54,612
YEAH. THAT’S BETTER.

1916
01:06:54,612 --> 01:06:57,147
OH, JUST GET IT OVER WITH
AND SIT ON MY LAP.

1917
01:06:57,147 --> 01:06:59,683
HE’S SUFFERING AN ADVANCED
PERSECUTION COMPLEX.

1918
01:06:59,683 --> 01:07:01,385
ANY INCIDENT MIGHT PROVOKE HIM

1919
01:07:01,385 --> 01:07:03,187
INTO COMMITTING
AN ACT OF VIOLENCE.

1920
01:07:03,187 --> 01:07:04,922
I’M WATCHING HIM CAREFULLY
AND TRYING TO HELP HIM.

1921
01:07:04,922 --> 01:07:06,590
BET HIS BREATH IS TERRIBLE.

1922
01:07:06,590 --> 01:07:08,425
HOW CAN I HELP?

1923
01:07:08,425 --> 01:07:10,693
BY AVOIDING
ANY UNNECESSARY CONVERSATION.

1924
01:07:10,693 --> 01:07:13,297
THEN HE’LL BE FREE
OF ANY ENTANGLING EMOTIONS

1925
01:07:13,297 --> 01:07:16,100
WHICH MIGHT HARM HIM.

1926
01:07:16,100 --> 01:07:17,602
I’LL DO AS YOU ASK, DOCTOR.

1927
01:07:17,602 --> 01:07:19,170
GOOD.

1928
01:07:19,170 --> 01:07:21,438
WE MUST LOOK
AFTER YOU TOO, DOCTOR.

1929
01:07:21,438 --> 01:07:23,307
YOU’RE SO GOOD TO ME,
DR. CONWAY.

1930
01:07:23,307 --> 01:07:26,510
I’LL SCRATCH YOUR EYES OUT.
[HISSES]

1931
01:07:26,510 --> 01:07:27,945
ONE SO LOVELY AS YOU

1932
01:07:27,945 --> 01:07:30,647
SHOULD HAVE THE UNDERSTANDING
AND PROTECTION OF A FRIEND.

1933
01:07:30,647 --> 01:07:32,950
BUT ABOVE ALL,

1934
01:07:32,950 --> 01:07:36,353
YOU MUST DISREGARD ANYTHING
MARK MAY TELL YOU.

1935
01:07:36,353 --> 01:07:38,155
I UNDERSTAND, DOCTOR.

1936
01:07:38,155 --> 01:07:40,523
NOW, I’M JUST GOING
TO SIT ON THE OTTOMAN,

1937
01:07:40,523 --> 01:07:41,558
THEN I’LL BE DONE.

1938
01:07:41,558 --> 01:07:44,060
I’M GLAD OTHERS THINK FOR ME.

1939
01:07:44,060 --> 01:07:46,330
JUST A LITTLE BIT NERVOUS.

1940
01:07:46,330 --> 01:07:48,198
LITTLE BIT JUMPY.

1941
01:07:48,198 --> 01:07:50,935
LIGHT. LIGHT. PLEASE.

1942
01:07:50,935 --> 01:07:55,472
HE LOOKS LIKE THE CAT
THAT ATE THE CANARY.

1943
01:07:55,472 --> 01:07:59,810
HERE. USE MY RONSON.
WORKS EVERY TIME.

1944
01:07:59,810 --> 01:08:01,945
[COUGHS]

1945
01:08:01,945 --> 01:08:03,213
OH, AND SHE JUST
PUTS IT OUT.

1946
01:08:03,213 --> 01:08:04,248
WHAT’S THE POINT OF THAT?

1947
01:08:04,248 --> 01:08:05,783
LEAVE THAT GIRL ALONE.

1948
01:08:05,783 --> 01:08:07,017
WHAT DOES THAT MEAN?

1949
01:08:07,017 --> 01:08:08,252
GRACE. LEAVE HER ALONE.

1950
01:08:08,252 --> 01:08:10,788
YOU’RE SOUNDING
LIKE A JEALOUS WOMAN.

1951
01:08:10,788 --> 01:08:12,557
THAT’S EXACTLY WHAT I AM,
CHARLES.

1952
01:08:12,557 --> 01:08:13,790
I LOVE YOU.

1953
01:08:13,790 --> 01:08:15,993
AND I’M NOT GONNA HAVE ANYTHING
COME BETWEEN US.

1954
01:08:15,993 --> 01:08:17,762
- SHARON.
- THIS IS NEW.

1955
01:08:17,762 --> 01:08:19,563
SHARON,
TWO PEOPLE STRIVING

1956
01:08:19,563 --> 01:08:21,165
FOR SUCH A GREAT SCIENTIFIC
ACHIEVEMENT

1957
01:08:21,165 --> 01:08:22,600
SHOULD NOT BE QUARRELING.

1958
01:08:22,600 --> 01:08:24,100
NOTHING SHOULD EVER
COME BETWEEN US.

1959
01:08:24,100 --> 01:08:25,602
EXCEPT MY HAND PUPPET.

1960
01:08:25,602 --> 01:08:26,970
CHARLES.

1961
01:08:26,970 --> 01:08:28,372
YES?

1962
01:08:28,372 --> 01:08:30,573
WHY CAN’T SHE BE
OUR NEXT SUBJECT?

1963
01:08:30,573 --> 01:08:32,042
SHE’S ALMOST
A PERFECT SPECIMEN,

1964
01:08:32,042 --> 01:08:33,510
AND YOU SAID WE NEEDED
A GOOD SUBJECT

1965
01:08:33,510 --> 01:08:35,045
FOR OUR NEXT EXPERIMENT.

1966
01:08:35,045 --> 01:08:38,048
- NOT YET.
- WHY NOT?

1967
01:08:38,048 --> 01:08:39,583
IT ISN’T THE RIGHT TIME.

1968
01:08:39,583 --> 01:08:41,718
BUT BE ASSURED,
WHEN THE TIME COMES,

1969
01:08:41,718 --> 01:08:44,053
I SHALL NOT HESITATE.

1970
01:08:44,053 --> 01:08:45,890
OKAY, RIGHT TIME NOW?

1971
01:08:45,890 --> 01:08:47,858
IS IT TIME YET?

1972
01:08:47,858 --> 01:08:49,593
NOW LET’S JOIN OUR FRIENDS

1973
01:08:49,593 --> 01:08:50,962
IN ANOTHER PART
OF THE HOUSE.

1974
01:08:50,962 --> 01:08:53,463
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC]

1975
01:08:53,463 --> 01:08:56,733
SLOW, SLOW, PLINK, PLINK.

1976
01:08:56,733 --> 01:09:01,538
SLOW.

1977
01:09:01,538 --> 01:09:02,573
MY DINNER WITH ANDRE

1978
01:09:02,573 --> 01:09:07,110
HAD MORE LOCATIONS
THAN THIS FILM.

1979
01:09:07,110 --> 01:09:08,245
NICE REC ROOM.

1980
01:09:08,245 --> 01:09:10,180
NO WAY. FOOSBALL.
THEY GOT EVERYTHING.

1981
01:09:10,180 --> 01:09:12,750
WOW. BUMPER POOL.

1982
01:09:15,518 --> 01:09:20,357
ADOLPH HITLER ON VIBES.

1983
01:09:20,357 --> 01:09:22,727
♪ DO DO ♪

1984
01:09:22,727 --> 01:09:27,130
SLOW, SLOW, PLINK, PLINK.

1985
01:09:30,633 --> 01:09:32,202
A SUB BASEMENT.

1986
01:09:32,202 --> 01:09:34,972
I COULD PUT A WORKSHOP
DOWN HERE.

1987
01:09:34,972 --> 01:09:36,540
YOU KNOW, AS LONG AS
I’M DOWN HERE,

1988
01:09:36,540 --> 01:09:38,275
- I’LL BRING UP
SOME CORN RELISH.
- OH YEAH.

1989
01:09:38,275 --> 01:09:40,077
MAYBE SOME OF THAT
BREAD AND BUTTER PICKLE STUFF

1990
01:09:40,077 --> 01:09:41,612
AND WATERMELON RIND PICKLES.

1991
01:09:41,612 --> 01:09:42,880
OH, I LOVE THOSE.
THOSE ARE REALLY GOOD.

1992
01:09:42,880 --> 01:09:45,815
AND SOME
PICKLED EGGS, MAYBE.

1993
01:09:45,815 --> 01:09:47,150
MRS. BATES?

1994
01:09:47,150 --> 01:09:50,220
- MRS. BATES?
- NORMAN?

1995
01:09:50,220 --> 01:09:52,422
YOU KNOW, I THINK HE’S LOOKING
FOR DAVE LENNOX.

1996
01:09:52,422 --> 01:09:54,692
OH, OF COURSE,
THAT WOULD FOLLOW.

1997
01:09:54,692 --> 01:09:56,693
LOOKS KIND OF LIKE
DAVID JANSSEN.

1998
01:09:56,693 --> 01:09:59,363
RAH, CAN’T GET
THE DOOR OPEN.

1999
01:09:59,363 --> 01:10:03,067
OH, SAM, YOU’RE IN THERE.

2000
01:10:03,067 --> 01:10:04,868
HMM.

2001
01:10:04,868 --> 01:10:06,537
WELL, I HAD ONE OF THESE
WHEN I WAS A KID.

2002
01:10:06,537 --> 01:10:09,940
IT’S A GRANDPA, I THINK.

2003
01:10:09,940 --> 01:10:11,708
D’AH, HERMAN,
TURN THE LIGHT OFF.

2004
01:10:11,708 --> 01:10:15,545
I’M RESTING.

2005
01:10:15,545 --> 01:10:16,880
[SERVO MIMICS PENGUIN]

2006
01:10:16,880 --> 01:10:20,017
MAN, THOSE MINNESOTANS
ARE SO STOIC.

2007
01:10:21,885 --> 01:10:23,353
WELL, I THOUGHT
THAT WOULD SCARE ME

2008
01:10:23,353 --> 01:10:24,655
A LOT WORSE THAN IT DID.

2009
01:10:24,655 --> 01:10:26,290
I WAS PRETTY COOL
THROUGH THAT.

2010
01:10:26,290 --> 01:10:28,358
I’LL PROBABLY
HAVE BAD DREAMS.

2011
01:10:31,462 --> 01:10:33,197
WELL...

2012
01:10:33,197 --> 01:10:35,565
OH, GOOD THING THERE’S
A DISSOLVE IN THE STAIRCASE.

2013
01:10:35,565 --> 01:10:38,635
MAKES IT EASIER.

2014
01:10:38,635 --> 01:10:41,005
[SERVO HUMS]

2015
01:10:41,005 --> 01:10:44,708
UH, WE KNOCK IN THIS MOVIE.

2016
01:10:44,708 --> 01:10:46,110
WHAT DO YOU WANT?

2017
01:10:46,110 --> 01:10:48,178
- TWO GUESSES.
- I’M SORRY TO
BREAK IN LIKE THIS

2018
01:10:48,178 --> 01:10:49,480
BUT IT’S MY
ONLY CHANCE TO PROVE

2019
01:10:49,480 --> 01:10:51,748
- I’M TELLING YOU THE TRUTH.
- PLEASE GET OUT.

2020
01:10:51,748 --> 01:10:53,350
BUT YOU DON’T UNDERSTAND
I’M TRYING TO HELP YOU?

2021
01:10:53,350 --> 01:10:54,618
LOOK, I’VE GOT
POSITIVE PROOF.

2022
01:10:54,618 --> 01:10:56,787
PROOF YOU’LL
HAVE TO BELIEVE.

2023
01:10:56,787 --> 01:10:58,622
PLEASE LEAVE ME ALONE.

2024
01:10:58,622 --> 01:11:01,625
LOOK, I DON’T HAVE TIME
TO ARGUE WITH YOU.

2025
01:11:01,625 --> 01:11:03,393
HERE, PUT ON THIS ROBE
AND COME WITH ME.

2026
01:11:03,393 --> 01:11:07,063
♪ WHILE STROLLING
THROUGH PARK ONE DAY ♪

2027
01:11:07,063 --> 01:11:08,332
BEFORE THIS NIGHT’S OVER,

2028
01:11:08,332 --> 01:11:11,402
YOU’RE GONNA BE
CONVINCED I’M RIGHT.

2029
01:11:15,472 --> 01:11:17,975
[CROW SIGHS]

2030
01:11:17,975 --> 01:11:20,110
WHAT IS THIS, A THREE STOOGES
ALL OF A SUDDEN?

2031
01:11:20,110 --> 01:11:21,612
[SERVO MIMICS MOE HOWARD]

2032
01:11:21,612 --> 01:11:24,582
THERE WAS A MAN HERE
NOT TEN MINUTES AGO.

2033
01:11:24,582 --> 01:11:25,915
MARK, PLEASE TAKE ME
BACK UPSTAIRS.

2034
01:11:25,915 --> 01:11:27,117
I TELL YOU,
HE WAS RIGHT HERE.

2035
01:11:27,117 --> 01:11:28,685
MARK, THIS IS
GETTING BORING.

2036
01:11:28,685 --> 01:11:30,320
- MARK, PLEASE.
- NO, GRACE.

2037
01:11:30,320 --> 01:11:32,188
NOT UNTIL WE FIND THAT GUY.

2038
01:11:37,127 --> 01:11:38,962
COVER YOUR SHAME.

2039
01:11:42,165 --> 01:11:44,200
OH, YOU KNOW, I DO LOVE
THESE FANTA-SUITES.

2040
01:11:44,200 --> 01:11:47,537
SAY, ARE WE IN THE JUNGLE ROOM
OR THE TARZAN ROOM?

2041
01:11:47,537 --> 01:11:50,640
WELL, YOU GOTTA ADMIT,
IT’S REALLY CREEPY DOWN HERE.

2042
01:11:50,640 --> 01:11:52,042
CREEPY CREEPY.

2043
01:11:52,042 --> 01:11:53,477
CREEPARELLY.

2044
01:11:53,477 --> 01:11:55,145
CREEPAROONY.

2045
01:11:55,145 --> 01:11:57,113
CREEPA-DEEPA-DEEP.

2046
01:11:57,113 --> 01:11:58,882
OH-- EW.

2047
01:12:01,318 --> 01:12:05,122
NATALIE! IT’S NATALIE!

2048
01:12:05,122 --> 01:12:08,025
SISSY SPACEK!

2049
01:12:08,025 --> 01:12:11,428
WOW, NOW I REALLY AM
HOTTER THAN HER.

2050
01:12:11,428 --> 01:12:12,797
YEAH, THAT’S NATALIE.

2051
01:12:12,797 --> 01:12:14,398
- NATALIE WEIRD.
- IT’S HORRIBLE.

2052
01:12:14,398 --> 01:12:16,967
- [NATALIE GROANS]
- SHE’S BEEN JERKED.

2053
01:12:16,967 --> 01:12:19,603
EASY NOW, YOU’VE GOTTA
TAKE A HOLD OF YOURSELF.

2054
01:12:19,603 --> 01:12:21,438
[SOBS]

2055
01:12:21,438 --> 01:12:22,740
I’M SORRY YOU HAD
TO SEE HER LIKE THIS,

2056
01:12:22,740 --> 01:12:26,477
BUT NOW MAYBE
YOU’LL BELIEVE ME.

2057
01:12:26,477 --> 01:12:28,812
- HOW COULD HE?
- WELL, ’CAUSE HE HAD SOME

2058
01:12:28,812 --> 01:12:30,647
EXTRA MOZZARELLA LYING
AROUND, YOU KNOW?

2059
01:12:30,647 --> 01:12:33,317
[SERVO CHUCKLES]
GONNA MAKE SOME GARLIC FACE.

2060
01:12:33,317 --> 01:12:35,652
EW.

2061
01:12:35,652 --> 01:12:37,553
YEAH, UH, CLOSE THE DOOR.

2062
01:12:37,553 --> 01:12:38,755
IT’LL KEEP HER FRESH.

2063
01:12:38,755 --> 01:12:40,023
AT LEAST KEEP THE ODOR IN.

2064
01:12:40,023 --> 01:12:42,392
WHOO.

2065
01:12:42,392 --> 01:12:44,193
OH, I’M REALLY TIRED.
GOOD NIGHT.

2066
01:12:44,193 --> 01:12:46,930
- [SERVO SNORES]
- OH, NATALIE!

2067
01:12:46,930 --> 01:12:48,765
GRACE.

2068
01:12:48,765 --> 01:12:50,400
GRACE, WE HAVEN’T TIME
TO THINK ABOUT THAT NOW.

2069
01:12:50,400 --> 01:12:51,902
WE’VE GOTTA FIGURE SOME WAY
TO GET YOU OUT OF THIS HOUSE.

2070
01:12:51,902 --> 01:12:53,237
- HOW ABOUT THE FRONT DOOR?
- HEY...

2071
01:12:53,237 --> 01:12:55,638
- I’M SO AFRAID.
- I KNOW.

2072
01:12:55,638 --> 01:12:57,573
NOW, LISTEN.
WHEN I GO OUT OF THIS ROOM,

2073
01:12:57,573 --> 01:12:59,510
YOU LOCK THE DOOR AND DON’T
OPEN IT FOR ANYBODY

2074
01:12:59,510 --> 01:13:01,745
UNTIL I GET BACK--
YOU UNDERSTAND? NOT FOR ANYBODY.

2075
01:13:01,745 --> 01:13:03,147
I WON’T, MARK.

2076
01:13:03,147 --> 01:13:04,948
- OKAY.
- I’LL LOOK LIKE ME.

2077
01:13:04,948 --> 01:13:06,583
OH, WE’D BETTER GO.

2078
01:13:06,583 --> 01:13:08,485
- LOCK THE DOOR.
- LOCK YOUR CAR,

2079
01:13:08,485 --> 01:13:10,653
TAKE YOUR KEYS.

2080
01:13:22,132 --> 01:13:23,733
[SERVO HUMS]

2081
01:13:23,733 --> 01:13:25,702
WHAT IN THE-- OH, YOU GUYS.

2082
01:13:25,702 --> 01:13:27,737
- WE’RE ZANY.
- WHICH RESULTS IN CREATIVITY.

2083
01:13:27,737 --> 01:13:28,972
YEAH, WE THOUGHT
WE COULD SHAKE OFF

2084
01:13:28,972 --> 01:13:30,740
OUR OWN CABIN FEVER
BY PLAYING A LITTLE GAME.

2085
01:13:30,740 --> 01:13:32,508
YEAH, BUT MOST OF OUR GAMES
ARE MISSING THEIR PIECES.

2086
01:13:32,508 --> 01:13:34,645
SO WE COMBINED THEM
TO MAKE OUR OWN GAME

2087
01:13:34,645 --> 01:13:36,247
BASED ON THIS WEEK’S MOVIE.

2088
01:13:36,247 --> 01:13:37,580
WANNA HELP US PLAY A GAME?

2089
01:13:37,580 --> 01:13:38,948
SURE, WHAT CAN I DO?

2090
01:13:38,948 --> 01:13:40,883
WELL, WE’RE ALL SET UP.
YOU COULD READ THE DIRECTIONS.

2091
01:13:40,883 --> 01:13:42,887
OH, THESE? OKAY. ALL RIGHT.

2092
01:13:42,887 --> 01:13:44,922
OH, I CAN TELL
YOU GUYS PUT THESE--

2093
01:13:44,922 --> 01:13:47,892
IT’S KIND OF AN AMALGAM OF
A BUNCH OF DIFFERENT
INSTRUCTIONS.

2094
01:13:47,892 --> 01:13:49,860
OKAY, GOT YOU.

2095
01:13:49,860 --> 01:13:52,728
EQUIPMENT-- GAME BOARD
SHOWING THE MANY ROOMS

2096
01:13:52,728 --> 01:13:54,932
OF JOHN CARRADINE’S
UNEARTHLY MANSION.

2097
01:13:54,932 --> 01:13:56,400
- DID THAT.
- LOOKS GOOD.
- ALL DONE.

2098
01:13:56,400 --> 01:13:58,035
OKAY, EACH PLAYER CHOOSES

2099
01:13:58,035 --> 01:13:59,268
A COLOR, TOKEN, OR MARKER.

2100
01:13:59,268 --> 01:14:01,103
OH-OH-OH, I’M THE SHOE!
I’M ALWAYS THE SHOE.

2101
01:14:01,103 --> 01:14:03,140
- DIBS ON THE SHOE.
- OKAY, YOU’RE THE SHOE.

2102
01:14:03,140 --> 01:14:04,373
I GET THE IRON, I DON’T
WANT THE PIG THIS TIME.

2103
01:14:04,373 --> 01:14:06,443
- OKAY, YOU’RE THE IRON.
- AH, LUCKY IRON.

2104
01:14:06,443 --> 01:14:08,812
AND I’LL BE PLAYING
MY CAPTAIN KIRK KING

2105
01:14:08,812 --> 01:14:11,582
FROM MY FRANKLIN MINT
COLLECTION CHESS SET.

2106
01:14:11,582 --> 01:14:13,483
- OH, I FORGOT ABOUT THAT ONE.
- THE ONLY PIECE YOU GOT.

2107
01:14:13,483 --> 01:14:15,018
OKAY, WHAT’S NEXT? UH...

2108
01:14:15,018 --> 01:14:16,287
FIRSTIES, WE ROLL
FOR FIRSTIES.

2109
01:14:16,287 --> 01:14:18,922
OKAY, RIGHT.
EACH PLAYER ROLLS THE DICE

2110
01:14:18,922 --> 01:14:22,860
IN THE TOR JOHNSON
POP-O-MATIC.

2111
01:14:22,860 --> 01:14:25,395
AFTER THE FIRST PLAYER
HAS BEEN SELECTED,

2112
01:14:25,395 --> 01:14:27,463
BUT BEFORE YOU REMOVE
HIS PITUITARY GLAND,

2113
01:14:27,463 --> 01:14:29,132
THE PLAYER TO HIS OR HER LEFT

2114
01:14:29,132 --> 01:14:31,435
LOSES ONE TURN
AND THEN PRECEDES TO GO.

2115
01:14:31,435 --> 01:14:34,572
[TALK OVER EACH OTHER]

2116
01:14:34,572 --> 01:14:36,307
EACH PLAYER STARTS OUT
WITH A BILLION DOLLARS

2117
01:14:36,307 --> 01:14:37,440
AND HALF A DOZEN HOTELS.

2118
01:14:37,440 --> 01:14:39,108
BUT IMMEDIATELY LOSES THEM

2119
01:14:39,108 --> 01:14:41,110
WHEN THEY DUMP IVANA
FOR MARLA.

2120
01:14:41,110 --> 01:14:43,747
YEAH, OKAY, OKAY,
LET’S GO, LET’S GO.

2121
01:14:43,747 --> 01:14:46,015
THE PLAYER LANDING
ON A PLOT STOPPER SQUARE

2122
01:14:46,015 --> 01:14:47,817
MUST GO BACK TO THE BEGINNING
OF THE MOVIE

2123
01:14:47,817 --> 01:14:50,287
OR PLAY THE ORGAN
FOR FIVE MINUTES.

2124
01:14:50,287 --> 01:14:52,588
ALL PLAYERS MUST STAY WITHIN
THE BOUNDARIES OF THE HOUSE.

2125
01:14:52,588 --> 01:14:54,257
PLAYERS GOING
OUTSIDE THE HOUSE

2126
01:14:54,257 --> 01:14:56,193
OR IN ANY WAY SUGGESTING
ANOTHER LOCATION

2127
01:14:56,193 --> 01:14:58,662
PUT THE FILM OVER BUDGET
AND MUST FORFEIT ONE TURN

2128
01:14:58,662 --> 01:15:01,198
AND PAY THE PLAYER
TO HIS OR HER RIGHT.

2129
01:15:01,198 --> 01:15:03,033
THE SUM NOT EQUAL
TO NET POINTS MADE

2130
01:15:03,033 --> 01:15:05,002
- ON THE BACK END OF THE DEAL.
- OKAY, WE KNOW!

2131
01:15:05,002 --> 01:15:06,837
OKAY! LET’S ROLL! ROLL!
HERE WE GO! POP-O-MATIC!

2132
01:15:06,837 --> 01:15:08,572
NO, HOLD ON, PLAYERS CAUGHT

2133
01:15:08,572 --> 01:15:10,040
ON THE STAIRWAY
LOSE ONE TURN.

2134
01:15:10,040 --> 01:15:11,742
- UH-HUH?
- PLAYERS CAUGHT IN
A MEANINGLESS TWO-SHOT

2135
01:15:11,742 --> 01:15:13,477
WITH JOHN CARRADINE
LOSE ONE TURN.

2136
01:15:13,477 --> 01:15:16,313
- PLAYERS WHO LOSE ONE TURN--
- [ALL] LOSE ONE TURN.

2137
01:15:16,313 --> 01:15:18,615
- OKAY! HERE WE GO!
- [TALK OVER EACH OTHER]

2138
01:15:18,615 --> 01:15:21,385
WAIT A SECOND-- PLAYERS WHO
LOSE THE BREAKFAST ARGUMENT

2139
01:15:21,385 --> 01:15:23,487
WITH THE PALOOKA ADVANCE
TO THE WOMAN’S BEDROOM.

2140
01:15:23,487 --> 01:15:25,988
PALOOKAS MAKING ADVANCES
ON THE WOMAN LOSE ONE TURN.

2141
01:15:25,988 --> 01:15:27,723
THANK YOU, JOEL
YOU KNOW, WE WROTE THESE RULES,

2142
01:15:27,723 --> 01:15:28,992
SO WE KNOW THEM.
WE CAN JUST GET TO THEM

2143
01:15:28,992 --> 01:15:31,228
- AS WE GO, SO LET’S GO!
- OKAY, HOLD ON--

2144
01:15:31,228 --> 01:15:32,795
- DIALOGUE CARDS.
- AW, THIS IS GONNA
TAKE TEN MINUTES.

2145
01:15:32,795 --> 01:15:34,297
PLAYERS LANDING
ON THE DIALOGUE BOX

2146
01:15:34,297 --> 01:15:35,798
MUST DRAW ONE CARD.

2147
01:15:35,798 --> 01:15:38,302
PLAYERS MUST THEN
READ A PASSAGE OF DIALOGUE.

2148
01:15:38,302 --> 01:15:39,703
YEAH, BUT YOU DON’T NEED
TO DO THAT, ’CAUSE--

2149
01:15:39,703 --> 01:15:41,305
LET’S DO THAT
WHEN WE GET TO IT--

2150
01:15:41,305 --> 01:15:43,873
- WE’LL LAND ON THAT SQUARE--
- IT’S GONNA BE A HALF HOUR.

2151
01:15:43,873 --> 01:15:45,208
ALL RIGHT, OKAY, HOLD ON.

2152
01:15:45,208 --> 01:15:47,277
HERE IT IS. HERE WE GO.

2153
01:15:47,277 --> 01:15:48,778
AS JOHN CARRADINE.

2154
01:15:48,778 --> 01:15:50,413
LET’S SEE HERE.

2155
01:15:50,413 --> 01:15:52,748
I’M GLAD TO HEAR
YOU’RE WILLING TO HELP.

2156
01:15:52,748 --> 01:15:54,083
YOU’RE A CLEVER YOUNG MAN.

2157
01:15:54,083 --> 01:15:56,453
I’VE DECIDED YOU CAN BE
OF ASSISTANCE TO ME.

2158
01:15:56,453 --> 01:15:57,887
- PRETTY GOOD CARRADINE.
- YEAH.

2159
01:15:57,887 --> 01:15:59,823
I’M REAL HANDY TO HAVE AROUND,
ESPECIALLY IF YOU NEED

2160
01:15:59,823 --> 01:16:01,492
SOMEONE TO BANDAGE
A GUNSHOT WOUND.

2161
01:16:01,492 --> 01:16:02,927
- JOHN CARRADINE.
- OKAY, GAME-TIME.
- JOEL.

2162
01:16:02,927 --> 01:16:04,227
THAT’S NOT EXACTLY
WHAT I HAD IN MIND.

2163
01:16:04,227 --> 01:16:05,895
JOEL, COME ON,
WE WANNA PLAY!

2164
01:16:05,895 --> 01:16:07,230
- --THAT WE’D HAVE
A LITTLE TALK--
- HEY, JOEL,

2165
01:16:07,230 --> 01:16:08,665
THE COMMERCIAL SIGN LIGHT
IS FLASHING.

2166
01:16:08,665 --> 01:16:10,433
- YOU TALK AND I’LL--
- LET’S JUST PLAY THE GAME!

2167
01:16:10,433 --> 01:16:11,835
WHAT COULD BE SO WRONG
WITH JUST--

2168
01:16:11,835 --> 01:16:13,637
OH, LET’S JUST LEAVE.

2169
01:16:13,637 --> 01:16:14,972
--TO A PROJECT THAT MOST
SCIENTISTS HAVE CONSIDERED--

2170
01:16:14,972 --> 01:16:16,573
PLEASE, MISTER,
CAN WE HAVE OUR BALL BACK?

2171
01:16:16,573 --> 01:16:18,108
BEYOND THE REALM
OF POSSIBILITY.

2172
01:16:18,108 --> 01:16:20,277
BELIEVE ME,
IT’S NOT IMPOSSIBLE

2173
01:16:20,277 --> 01:16:21,578
TO THE TRUE SCIENTIST.

2174
01:16:24,347 --> 01:16:25,882
HEY, WHY DIDN’T
YOU GUYS WAIT?

2175
01:16:25,882 --> 01:16:28,018
’CAUSE YOU WERE JUST
READING DIRECTIONS.

2176
01:16:28,018 --> 01:16:32,455
HMM, MISSING
A BALUSTRADE THERE.

2177
01:16:32,455 --> 01:16:35,225
TOR LIKE NEW LUNCH BOX.

2178
01:16:35,225 --> 01:16:36,693
TOR’S WEARING
A WOODEN KIMONO.

2179
01:16:36,693 --> 01:16:38,762
HEY.

2180
01:16:38,762 --> 01:16:41,197
HEY, TOR, HOW COME
YOU’RE COFFIN SO BAD?

2181
01:16:41,197 --> 01:16:42,498
- [BOTS LAUGH]
- NUDGE NUDGE.

2182
01:16:42,498 --> 01:16:43,933
THAT’S A GREAT-- AHH.

2183
01:16:43,933 --> 01:16:45,635
I LOVE THAT.

2184
01:16:48,172 --> 01:16:50,940
TOR DEEP INTO RECYCLING.

2185
01:16:50,940 --> 01:16:52,775
TISKET, TASKET.

2186
01:16:52,775 --> 01:16:54,712
GREEN YELLOW CASKET!

2187
01:16:54,712 --> 01:16:56,112
PUN!

2188
01:16:56,112 --> 01:16:57,947
[SERVO CHUCKLES]

2189
01:16:59,883 --> 01:17:02,552
DID I JUST SEE
A CASKET GO BY?

2190
01:17:02,552 --> 01:17:04,320
HEY, I CAN’T BELIEVE IT--
THEY’RE OUTSIDE!

2191
01:17:04,320 --> 01:17:08,125
- YEP.
- WHOA. WHOA!

2192
01:17:08,125 --> 01:17:10,460
UNDER THE SPREADING
CHESTNUT TREE,

2193
01:17:10,460 --> 01:17:14,197
THE VILLAGE SMITHY STANDS.

2194
01:17:14,197 --> 01:17:17,333
HE’S WEARING BIRKI’S!

2195
01:17:17,333 --> 01:17:18,968
[CROW GROANS]

2196
01:17:18,968 --> 01:17:20,370
MULCH GOOD FOR GARDEN.

2197
01:17:20,370 --> 01:17:22,238
- RICH COMPOST.
- D’UH, ONE.

2198
01:17:22,238 --> 01:17:24,440
D’UH, TWO.

2199
01:17:28,178 --> 01:17:29,545
I DON’T LIKE
THIS PLACE, SEE?

2200
01:17:29,545 --> 01:17:32,515
YEAH, GIVES ME
THE CREEPS, SEE?

2201
01:17:32,515 --> 01:17:34,250
YEAH, THIS PLACE
GIVES ME THE WILLIES.

2202
01:17:34,250 --> 01:17:37,287
- I’M GONNA BLOW!
- [DOG BARKS]

2203
01:17:37,287 --> 01:17:40,523
UH, TWO-- OH,
DOG MAKE ME LOSE COUNT.

2204
01:17:45,628 --> 01:17:48,798
♪ MR. LOBO RISIN’ ♪

2205
01:17:48,798 --> 01:17:50,500
[SERVO MIMICS GUITAR]

2206
01:17:50,500 --> 01:17:52,135
[DOG BARKS]

2207
01:17:52,135 --> 01:17:53,337
[CROW MIMICS
POPEYE CHUCKLE]

2208
01:17:53,337 --> 01:17:54,738
HE DIDN’T NOTICE ME’SKA.

2209
01:17:54,738 --> 01:17:56,573
HUH, I’LL JUST GO OUT
AND FINISH HIS JOBSK FOR HIM.

2210
01:17:56,573 --> 01:17:58,208
YEAH, HE WON’T KNOW
WHO DID IT, THEN.

2211
01:17:58,208 --> 01:18:00,343
YEAH, BACK OFF, YOU MUTT.

2212
01:18:04,748 --> 01:18:07,683
D’AH, KITTY!

2213
01:18:07,683 --> 01:18:09,318
[DOG WHINES]

2214
01:18:09,318 --> 01:18:12,922
SIT.

2215
01:18:12,922 --> 01:18:15,258
[SERVO HUMS SCORE]

2216
01:18:24,533 --> 01:18:26,937
HEY, ABE VIGODA!

2217
01:18:26,937 --> 01:18:28,905
YEAH.

2218
01:18:28,905 --> 01:18:30,840
I’M FEELING MUCH BETTER.

2219
01:18:30,840 --> 01:18:32,475
[SERVO GASPS]

2220
01:18:32,475 --> 01:18:35,112
WELL, WHAT DO YOU KNOW?
I AM ANN B. DAVIS.

2221
01:18:38,915 --> 01:18:40,517
THAT SURE WAS SWELL.

2222
01:18:40,517 --> 01:18:41,785
MAN, THIS JOINT HAS CLASS.

2223
01:18:41,785 --> 01:18:44,187
YEAH.

2224
01:18:44,187 --> 01:18:46,188
D’AH, BACK TO WORK.

2225
01:18:46,188 --> 01:18:48,392
UH...

2226
01:18:48,392 --> 01:18:50,993
UH, ONE.

2227
01:18:50,993 --> 01:18:52,862
D’UH, TWO.

2228
01:18:52,862 --> 01:18:54,230
ALAS, POOR YORICK.

2229
01:18:54,230 --> 01:18:55,865
I KNEW HIM, HORATIO.

2230
01:18:55,865 --> 01:18:57,700
D’UH, TWO.

2231
01:18:57,700 --> 01:18:59,268
THIS IS WHAT HAPPENS
WHEN YOU SIGN

2232
01:18:59,268 --> 01:19:01,337
- WITH WILLIAM MORRIS.
- TWO.

2233
01:19:01,337 --> 01:19:04,507
MAN, THIS IS THE LIFE.

2234
01:19:04,507 --> 01:19:07,643
[KNOCK ON DOOR]

2235
01:19:07,643 --> 01:19:10,847
- WHO IS IT?
- MARK. OPEN UP.

2236
01:19:10,847 --> 01:19:14,050
- IT’S JOHN "BOWZER" BAUMAN.
- YEAH.

2237
01:19:14,050 --> 01:19:16,687
WHY-- WHY,
I OUGHTA POP YOU ONE!

2238
01:19:16,687 --> 01:19:17,920
- WHAT DO YOU WANT?

2239
01:19:17,920 --> 01:19:19,188
DANNY, LET’S GET
ONE THING STRAIGHT.

2240
01:19:19,188 --> 01:19:20,657
- I DIDN’T COME HERE--
- YOU MUTTONHEAD.

2241
01:19:20,657 --> 01:19:22,225
YOU’RE IN A JAM, AND I WANNA
GET YOU OUT OF IT.

2242
01:19:22,225 --> 01:19:23,560
- GIVE ME THE STRAIGHT POOP.
- I DON’T NEED ANY HELP.

2243
01:19:23,560 --> 01:19:24,828
- YES, YOU DO,
NOW LISTEN TO ME.
- YEAH,

2244
01:19:24,828 --> 01:19:26,095
WHAT’S WITH THE GRABBIN’?
WHAT GIVES?

2245
01:19:26,095 --> 01:19:27,430
--CRAZY EXPERIMENTS HERE.
HE PLANS TO USE

2246
01:19:27,430 --> 01:19:28,898
- ALL OF US AS GUINEA PIGS.
- YOU’RE COCKEYED!

2247
01:19:28,898 --> 01:19:30,267
I DON’T BELIEVE IT.
ALL RIGHT, DON’T.

2248
01:19:30,267 --> 01:19:32,835
BUT STOP AND THINK, DANNY.
FOR ONCE, REALLY THINK.

2249
01:19:32,835 --> 01:19:34,337
WHAT’S BECOME OF NATALIE?
WHERE IS SHE?

2250
01:19:34,337 --> 01:19:35,672
AH, YOU’RE LOCO,
YOU’RE SCREWY!

2251
01:19:35,672 --> 01:19:37,473
NOW, IF I HAD TIME,
I’D TAKE YOU DOWNSTAIRS.

2252
01:19:37,473 --> 01:19:38,875
AND SHOW YOU-- I’VE SEEN HER.
SHE’S IN THE CELLAR,

2253
01:19:38,875 --> 01:19:40,943
AND I’VE SEEN WHAT
CONWAY’S DONE TO HER.

2254
01:19:40,943 --> 01:19:42,212
HE’S TURNED HER INTO A--

2255
01:19:42,212 --> 01:19:43,547
WELL, A GOD-KNOWS-WHAT.
SHE’S ALL TWISTED.

2256
01:19:43,547 --> 01:19:44,815
HER FACE LOOKS LIKE SOMETHING
OUT OF A NIGHTMARE.

2257
01:19:44,815 --> 01:19:46,382
YEAH, REAL SAD-SACK,
YOU KNOW?

2258
01:19:46,382 --> 01:19:47,717
WHY WOULD HE DO
A THING LIKE THAT TO NATALIE?

2259
01:19:47,717 --> 01:19:48,952
- HE’S A MADE MAN.
- WHO KNOWS WHY?

2260
01:19:48,952 --> 01:19:50,353
NOTHING MATTERS TO CONWAY
BUT HIS CRAZY IDEAS.

2261
01:19:50,353 --> 01:19:52,155
- AND BELIEVE ME, DANNY--
- HE’S HOODOO, I TELL YA!

2262
01:19:52,155 --> 01:19:53,823
--ONLY A SAMPLE OF WHAT
HE’LL DO TO YOU, ME,

2263
01:19:53,823 --> 01:19:55,225
OR ANYBODY ELSE
HE GETS HIS HANDS ON.

2264
01:19:55,225 --> 01:19:56,727
YEAH, YEAH, HE’S ROTTEN.

2265
01:19:56,727 --> 01:19:58,162
- ALL RIGHT.
- COME ON, LET’S BLOW.

2266
01:19:58,162 --> 01:20:00,163
ALL RIGHT, WELL,
WHAT CAN WE DO ABOUT IT?

2267
01:20:00,163 --> 01:20:01,565
YOU CAN SAVE YOUR NECK--
YOU CAN GET OUT OF THIS HOUSE

2268
01:20:01,565 --> 01:20:03,032
BEFORE IT’S TOO LATE.
BEFORE CONWAY TURNS YOU

2269
01:20:03,032 --> 01:20:04,400
INTO SOME KIND
OF A HORRIBLE FREAK.

2270
01:20:04,400 --> 01:20:06,068
- HOW?
- SKIP THE PATTER
AND GRAB YOUR SKIVVIES.

2271
01:20:06,068 --> 01:20:07,437
- I’VE ALREADY TRIED.
- I KNOW.

2272
01:20:07,437 --> 01:20:08,905
BUT DON’T WORRY ABOUT THAT.
YOU DO WHAT I TELL YOU,

2273
01:20:08,905 --> 01:20:10,407
- YOU’LL GET OUT ALL RIGHT.
- YEAH, JUST TALK FAST, SEE?

2274
01:20:10,407 --> 01:20:11,942
IT’S 12:45.

2275
01:20:11,942 --> 01:20:13,177
YOU GO TO BED
AND PRETEND YOU’RE ASLEEP.

2276
01:20:13,177 --> 01:20:14,577
AT EXACTLY 2:00,
YOU COME DOWNSTAIRS.

2277
01:20:14,577 --> 01:20:15,912
GRACE AND I’LL
MEET YOU THERE.

2278
01:20:15,912 --> 01:20:17,480
YEAH, SURE THING, SHUT-EYE.
THAT’S THE TICKET.

2279
01:20:17,480 --> 01:20:19,315
OKAY. 2:00. I’LL BE THERE.

2280
01:20:19,315 --> 01:20:21,017
JAKE, I’LL HIT THE SACK
AND CATCH SOME Z’S.

2281
01:20:21,017 --> 01:20:23,353
- YOU BE ON TIME.
- YEAH YEAH, I’LL BE THERE.

2282
01:20:26,623 --> 01:20:28,992
YOU KNOW, STAMPS ARE FUN.

2283
01:20:31,093 --> 01:20:33,530
HMM, WHO’S PLAYING
MY HAMMOND?

2284
01:20:40,037 --> 01:20:42,605
HUH, FAUCET’S DRIPPING.

2285
01:20:42,605 --> 01:20:43,807
YOU’RE NOT ABOUT TO START

2286
01:20:43,807 --> 01:20:46,877
KNOCKING AGAIN, ARE YOU?

2287
01:20:46,877 --> 01:20:48,312
YEAH, I’LL MAKE LIKE
I’M SAWIN’ LOGS.

2288
01:20:48,312 --> 01:20:50,047
[JOEL SNORES]

2289
01:20:55,818 --> 01:20:57,853
HE EVEN SLEEPS CRABBY.

2290
01:21:06,028 --> 01:21:07,297
CHRIS ISAAK!

2291
01:21:07,297 --> 01:21:08,965
♪♪ [SERVO MIMICS ISAAK]

2292
01:21:15,805 --> 01:21:17,040
UH, NOTHING, DEAR.

2293
01:21:17,040 --> 01:21:20,777
JUST CHECKING THE JOISTS.

2294
01:21:20,777 --> 01:21:22,378
OKAY, WATCH THE LADY.

2295
01:21:22,378 --> 01:21:23,547
WE’RE GONNA
SWITCH ’EM AROUND.

2296
01:21:23,547 --> 01:21:26,148
WATCH!

2297
01:21:26,148 --> 01:21:28,050
KINDA HIGH
FOR A BATHTUB DRAIN.

2298
01:21:28,050 --> 01:21:30,220
MM-HMM.

2299
01:21:30,220 --> 01:21:32,722
[CROW AS BASIL FAWLTY]
MANUEL? POLLY?

2300
01:21:34,925 --> 01:21:36,192
MAN, STAIRS.

2301
01:21:36,192 --> 01:21:37,793
THIS MOVIE WOULD’VE BEEN
A LOT SHORTER

2302
01:21:37,793 --> 01:21:39,228
IF THEY FILMED IT
IN A RAMBLER.

2303
01:21:39,228 --> 01:21:41,330
MM-HMM.

2304
01:21:45,668 --> 01:21:47,203
HE SHOULD JUST
DRINK A GLASS OF MILK

2305
01:21:47,203 --> 01:21:50,240
- AND GO TO BED.
- YEAH.

2306
01:21:50,240 --> 01:21:52,908
♪ TAKE SOMINEX TONIGHT
AND SEE... ♪

2307
01:21:56,947 --> 01:21:59,648
SOMEBODY’S KNOCKING AGAIN--
I HATE THAT.

2308
01:22:03,387 --> 01:22:06,155
LOOK, HE’S MORE CONFUSED
THAN WE ARE.

2309
01:22:06,155 --> 01:22:08,658
I GOTTA BACK UP
AND READ THE SCRIPT.

2310
01:22:10,360 --> 01:22:13,797
MAN, IT’S LIKE VAUDEVILLE
IN SLOW-MOTION.

2311
01:22:13,797 --> 01:22:15,632
WELL, LET’S SEE, SCENE 13--

2312
01:22:15,632 --> 01:22:18,200
OH, LET’S STOP FOR THE DAY.
I’M POOPED.

2313
01:22:22,338 --> 01:22:23,807
- [ALL GASP]
- DON’T DO THAT!

2314
01:22:23,807 --> 01:22:27,077
I’M A HORROR MOVIE,
AND YOU SNEAK UP ON ME!

2315
01:22:27,077 --> 01:22:28,812
HAVE YOU JUST
BEEN DOWNSTAIRS?

2316
01:22:28,812 --> 01:22:30,880
NO, I’VE BEEN IN MY ROOM, WHY?

2317
01:22:30,880 --> 01:22:32,648
- ARE YOU SURE?
- OF COURSE.

2318
01:22:32,648 --> 01:22:34,217
IS THERE SOMETHING
WRONG, CHARLES?

2319
01:22:34,217 --> 01:22:35,818
SOMEONE STOLE
THE STRAWBERRIES.

2320
01:22:35,818 --> 01:22:37,453
NOTHING.

2321
01:22:37,453 --> 01:22:39,022
NOTHING AT ALL.

2322
01:22:39,022 --> 01:22:41,523
CHARLES, I’M WORRIED ABOUT YOU.
YOU’VE BEEN WORKING TOO HARD.

2323
01:22:41,523 --> 01:22:43,760
LOOK AT THE COLLAR
ON ANNE BOLEYN, HERE.

2324
01:22:43,760 --> 01:22:46,462
YES, PLEASE LEAVE ME ALONE.

2325
01:22:46,462 --> 01:22:47,863
WHY DON’T YOU
TRY TO GET SOME REST?

2326
01:22:47,863 --> 01:22:49,665
- YOU’LL FEEL SO MUCH BETTER.
- AND WE CAN FILM IT.

2327
01:22:49,665 --> 01:22:51,167
PERHAPS YOU’D LIKE
A GLASS OF WARM MILK.

2328
01:22:51,167 --> 01:22:54,103
I’M NOT A CHILD.
I WON’T BE PAMPERED
OR MOTHERED.

2329
01:22:54,103 --> 01:22:56,773
I’D LIKE STRAWBERRY QUIK
AND SOME COOKIES, THOUGH.

2330
01:22:56,773 --> 01:22:59,542
I NEED NOTHING THAT
I DO NOT WISH TO NEED.

2331
01:22:59,542 --> 01:23:01,077
GOOD NIGHT, SHARON.

2332
01:23:01,077 --> 01:23:04,447
YOU WANNA UNPACK THAT ONE
FOR US, GRANDPA?

2333
01:23:04,447 --> 01:23:05,782
WHERE’S THAT MUG?

2334
01:23:05,782 --> 01:23:08,017
IT’S BLACKER THAN
A PARSON’S HAT DOWN HERE.

2335
01:23:08,017 --> 01:23:09,818
JEEPERS.

2336
01:23:09,818 --> 01:23:12,055
YEAH, KEEP THAT MUG OF SHINE
IF YOU DON’T SHOW.

2337
01:23:14,157 --> 01:23:17,393
AND THE DOLLY, MAN,
SHE WAS POURED INTO THAT DRESS.

2338
01:23:17,393 --> 01:23:19,028
I TIRE OF GUTTER LINGO.

2339
01:23:19,028 --> 01:23:21,597
- HMM.
- WHAT TIME IS IT?

2340
01:23:21,597 --> 01:23:23,933
HUH, MUST BE ALMOST TIME
FOR HIS MEDS.

2341
01:23:27,803 --> 01:23:30,673
HEY, IT’S THE STIFF
AND HIS DOLLY.

2342
01:23:30,673 --> 01:23:31,808
YEAH.

2343
01:23:31,808 --> 01:23:33,743
GOOD BOY, DANNY.

2344
01:23:33,743 --> 01:23:36,578
NOW, LISTEN, YOU AND GRACE
TAKE THE MAIN ROAD INTO TOWN.

2345
01:23:36,578 --> 01:23:38,448
REMEMBER, STAY IN THE SHADOWS
TILL YOU’RE CLEAR OF THE HOUSE.

2346
01:23:38,448 --> 01:23:40,750
I’LL TAKE THE LOW ROAD
AND BE IN SCOTLAND BEFORE YOU.

2347
01:23:40,750 --> 01:23:43,352
- --TO MOVE
AS FAST AS YOU CAN.
- WHAT ABOUT YOU, MARK?

2348
01:23:43,352 --> 01:23:45,020
WELL, I’LL MAKE SURE
CONWAY DOESN’T FOLLOW.

2349
01:23:45,020 --> 01:23:46,923
- I’LL CATCH UP TO YOU LATER.
- YOU SURE YOU’LL BE OKAY?

2350
01:23:46,923 --> 01:23:48,658
YEAH, YEAH, I’LL BE FINE.
NOW, GET OUT OF HERE.

2351
01:23:48,658 --> 01:23:49,925
- OH, AND DANNY?
- YEAH?

2352
01:23:49,925 --> 01:23:51,693
- TAKE GOOD CARE OF HER, HUH?
- YEAH, OKAY.

2353
01:23:51,693 --> 01:23:53,362
YEAH, SHE’S A REAL SWEET KID,
YOU KNOW?

2354
01:23:53,362 --> 01:23:54,797
D’OH.

2355
01:23:54,797 --> 01:23:57,200
- WELL.
- SO, A MAKE-OUT PARTY?

2356
01:23:57,200 --> 01:23:58,568
HOW COME I’M NOT INVITED?

2357
01:23:58,568 --> 01:24:00,603
--REPAY MY HOSPITALITY?

2358
01:24:00,603 --> 01:24:03,473
LOBO? SHARON? THANK YOU.

2359
01:24:03,473 --> 01:24:04,773
- NO, THANK YOU.
- OH NO, THANK YOU.

2360
01:24:04,773 --> 01:24:06,308
OH, NO THANK YOU--
WOULD YOU JUST?!

2361
01:24:06,308 --> 01:24:07,643
--VERY CLEVER,
BUT I CAN’T ENJOY

2362
01:24:07,643 --> 01:24:09,912
WATCHING MY
KINDNESSES ABUSED.

2363
01:24:09,912 --> 01:24:11,280
I SUPPOSE I SHOULD’VE
TURNED YOU OVER

2364
01:24:11,280 --> 01:24:13,382
TO THE POLICE
IN THE FIRST PLACE.

2365
01:24:13,382 --> 01:24:14,650
WOULD IT SURPRISE YOU ALL
TO KNOW

2366
01:24:14,650 --> 01:24:16,585
THAT MARK IS
AN ESCAPED KILLER?

2367
01:24:16,585 --> 01:24:18,788
AND A THIEF TO WHOM
I OFFERED SANCTUARY?

2368
01:24:18,788 --> 01:24:22,292
- THAT WOULDN’T SURPRISE ME.
- IT’S TRUE.

2369
01:24:22,292 --> 01:24:24,160
AND AS FOR YOU, ESMERALDA--

2370
01:24:24,160 --> 01:24:25,595
THE FACT THAT
YOU TURNED AGAINST ME

2371
01:24:25,595 --> 01:24:26,863
IS THE GREATEST SHOCK OF ALL.

2372
01:24:26,863 --> 01:24:28,698
THAT COULD’VE BEEN
A CONVINCING STORY, DOC,

2373
01:24:28,698 --> 01:24:29,898
BUT NOW IT’S TOO LATE.

2374
01:24:29,898 --> 01:24:32,835
HEY, IT’S BOB AND CAROL
AND TOR AND ALICE.

2375
01:24:32,835 --> 01:24:35,338
TAKE THEM AWAY.
DOWNSTAIRS, LOBO.

2376
01:24:35,338 --> 01:24:37,173
SHARON, SEE THAT THEY’RE SECURE,
AND THEN JOIN ME UPSTAIRS.

2377
01:24:37,173 --> 01:24:39,975
HEY, BALDY, GET THE GAT
OUTTA MY BACKSIDE.

2378
01:24:42,145 --> 01:24:43,480
NOT YOU, MY DEAR.

2379
01:24:43,480 --> 01:24:45,815
I HAVE SOMETHING SPECIAL
PLANNED FOR YOU.

2380
01:24:49,118 --> 01:24:51,353
UPSTAIRS.

2381
01:24:51,353 --> 01:24:54,290
SLOWLY, WALK REAL SLOW.

2382
01:24:54,290 --> 01:24:55,692
THAT’S IT.

2383
01:25:02,798 --> 01:25:04,867
HEY, WE’RE WATCHING
DOWN BY LAW ALL OF A SUDDEN.

2384
01:25:04,867 --> 01:25:07,103
KEEP THEM HERE TILL I COME BACK.
UNDERSTAND?

2385
01:25:07,103 --> 01:25:08,538
YES, I KEEP THEM HERE

2386
01:25:08,538 --> 01:25:10,005
TILL THEY GET BACK.

2387
01:25:12,975 --> 01:25:15,245
DANNY, TAKE A LOOK AT THIS.

2388
01:25:15,245 --> 01:25:18,447
♪ TAKE A LOOK
AT THESE HANDS ♪

2389
01:25:18,447 --> 01:25:20,683
NIGHT, MOTHER.

2390
01:25:20,683 --> 01:25:22,785
OH, ICK.

2391
01:25:22,785 --> 01:25:27,023
THANKS FOR SHOWING ME THAT.

2392
01:25:27,023 --> 01:25:28,825
FOLLOW MY PLAY.

2393
01:25:28,825 --> 01:25:30,227
I’VE GOT AN IDEA.

2394
01:25:30,227 --> 01:25:31,493
WATCH YOURSELF.

2395
01:25:31,493 --> 01:25:33,228
SURE THING--
TIME FOR THE OLD DIPSY-DOODLE.

2396
01:25:33,228 --> 01:25:34,697
ROUTINE 55.

2397
01:25:34,697 --> 01:25:36,833
SEEN THE SLEEPING BEAUTY
IN THERE?

2398
01:25:36,833 --> 01:25:38,702
YOU KNOW, JUST LIKE
IN THE STORYBOOK.

2399
01:25:38,702 --> 01:25:39,968
WITH A GIRL WHO’S REAL PRETTY,

2400
01:25:39,968 --> 01:25:42,005
- LIKE NATALIE.
- YEAH, REAL ATTRACTIVE GAL.

2401
01:25:42,005 --> 01:25:43,472
PUT HER INTO A DRESS, YEAH.

2402
01:25:43,472 --> 01:25:46,242
SHE HAD A SPELL PUT ON HER BY
THIS GIANT IN A CASTLE.

2403
01:25:46,242 --> 01:25:47,543
- UH-HUH?
- A GIANT?

2404
01:25:47,543 --> 01:25:50,180
NOW, THIS GIANT,
HE’S GOT A BULL.

2405
01:25:50,180 --> 01:25:52,815
AND THE BULL’S NAME
IS FERDINAND.

2406
01:25:52,815 --> 01:25:54,350
FERDINAND?

2407
01:25:54,350 --> 01:25:56,685
- YEAH--
- TOR’S HOOKED ON PHONICS!

2408
01:25:56,685 --> 01:25:58,655
--HE DOESN’T LIKE
THE BEAUTIFUL RED CAPE

2409
01:25:58,655 --> 01:26:00,190
THAT THE GIANT HAS.

2410
01:26:00,190 --> 01:26:01,690
SO HE TRIES TO GET IT.

2411
01:26:01,690 --> 01:26:03,793
BUT THE GIANT,
HE JUST TAKES THE CAPE,

2412
01:26:03,793 --> 01:26:05,362
AND HE WAVES IT
RIGHT IN FRONT OF THE BULL.

2413
01:26:05,362 --> 01:26:07,363
OH, HE’S A TOR-EADOR.

2414
01:26:07,363 --> 01:26:09,098
D’OH!

2415
01:26:09,098 --> 01:26:10,967
AND HE RUSHES
RIGHT AT THE CAPE.

2416
01:26:10,967 --> 01:26:12,668
THE GIANT,
HE JUST TAKES THE CAPE,

2417
01:26:12,668 --> 01:26:13,903
- HE THROWS IT OVER THE BULL!
- WAIT!

2418
01:26:13,903 --> 01:26:16,172
DO OTHER VOICES.

2419
01:26:16,172 --> 01:26:17,673
OH.

2420
01:26:17,673 --> 01:26:20,210
YOU KNOW, THAT STORY’S GOT
A BETTER PLOT THAN THIS MOVIE.

2421
01:26:20,210 --> 01:26:21,777
YEAH.

2422
01:26:21,777 --> 01:26:22,978
OH, NO WOUND, HUH?

2423
01:26:22,978 --> 01:26:24,780
HEY, WE NEED A WOUND--
MAKE-UP!

2424
01:26:27,850 --> 01:26:30,420
WAIT, WAIT,
DON’T LEAVE TOR HANGING.

2425
01:26:30,420 --> 01:26:32,755
WHAT HAPPENS TO FERDINAND?

2426
01:26:32,755 --> 01:26:34,257
- EXTRAORDINARY.
- YEAH, ALL RIGHT.

2427
01:26:34,257 --> 01:26:35,458
GO AHEAD, I’LL FOLLOW YOU.

2428
01:26:35,458 --> 01:26:36,960
ARE YOU SURE
YOU CAN MAKE IT ALONE?

2429
01:26:36,960 --> 01:26:38,862
YEAH, YEAH, SURE, I’M SWELL.
NOW SCRAM!

2430
01:26:38,862 --> 01:26:40,095
OH-- OW.

2431
01:26:40,095 --> 01:26:41,463
SHE’S WELL UNDER.
PREPARE HER.

2432
01:26:41,463 --> 01:26:43,365
HEY, THEY’RE GONNA GIVE HER
A NOSE LIKE LATOYA.

2433
01:26:43,365 --> 01:26:45,000
SAY.

2434
01:26:45,000 --> 01:26:47,037
YOU MEAN, LIKE MICHAEL.

2435
01:26:47,037 --> 01:26:48,370
WHAT’S THE DIF?

2436
01:26:51,273 --> 01:26:52,475
STAY RIGHT THERE, CONWAY.

2437
01:26:52,475 --> 01:26:54,410
YOU THINK THAT GUN
IS REALLY NECESSARY?

2438
01:26:54,410 --> 01:26:56,112
YEAH, FINISHES THE ENSEMBLE.

2439
01:26:56,112 --> 01:26:57,613
--MUCH EASIER IF
YOU PUT THE GUN AWAY.

2440
01:26:57,613 --> 01:27:01,617
MAYBE SO, BUT YOU KEEP
YOUR HANDS ON TOP OF THE DESK.

2441
01:27:01,617 --> 01:27:04,087
VERY WELL, MARK.

2442
01:27:04,087 --> 01:27:05,688
WAIT A MINUTE--
PRETTY GIRL, YOUNG GIRL,

2443
01:27:05,688 --> 01:27:07,157
OLD MAN, MAN WITH A GUN!

2444
01:27:07,157 --> 01:27:09,358
THE SITUATION SEEMS
TO HAVE ALTERED SLIGHTLY.

2445
01:27:09,358 --> 01:27:11,160
MORE THAN SLIGHTLY.
I’VE GOT THE GUN.

2446
01:27:11,160 --> 01:27:12,495
WARM GUN. MAKES ME HAPPY.

2447
01:27:12,495 --> 01:27:13,730
--HOW LONG DO YOU THINK
YOU COULD GO ON

2448
01:27:13,730 --> 01:27:15,332
DESTROYING PEOPLE
BEFORE SOMEBODY STOPPED YOU?

2449
01:27:15,332 --> 01:27:18,133
OH, I DON’T KNOW.
20, 30 YEARS?

2450
01:27:18,133 --> 01:27:19,968
--THIS FROM YOU, A KILLER.

2451
01:27:19,968 --> 01:27:21,837
A MAN HUNTED BY THE POLICE.

2452
01:27:21,837 --> 01:27:24,573
I WAS ABOUT TO GIVE THE WORLD
THE GIFT OF ETERNAL LIFE.

2453
01:27:24,573 --> 01:27:26,608
TEACH THE WORLD TO SING
IN PERFECT HARMONY!

2454
01:27:26,608 --> 01:27:28,010
--MUTILATED
INNOCENT HUMAN BEINGS

2455
01:27:28,010 --> 01:27:29,445
YOU TRANSFORMED THEM INTO
CREATURES SO HIDEOUS

2456
01:27:29,445 --> 01:27:32,548
- THEY’D BE BETTER OFF DEAD?
- OUI. I DID ZAT.

2457
01:27:32,548 --> 01:27:33,950
WHO ARE YOU TO QUESTION
THE USEFULNESS

2458
01:27:33,950 --> 01:27:35,752
OF MY EXPERIMENTS
IN RELATION TO THE FUTURE?

2459
01:27:35,752 --> 01:27:36,987
WHO ARE YOU TO JUDGE?
I WAS IN

2460
01:27:36,987 --> 01:27:39,288
STAGECOACH AND
GRAPES OF WRATH!

2461
01:27:39,288 --> 01:27:40,957
A HAPPY WORLD
ABOUT TO THROWN OPEN

2462
01:27:40,957 --> 01:27:42,558
TO A HUMANITY
THAT WOULDN’T DIE.

2463
01:27:42,558 --> 01:27:44,260
AND NOT YOU OR ANYONE ELSE
CAN STOP ME.

2464
01:27:44,260 --> 01:27:45,428
SAVE THAT FOR THE JURY.

2465
01:27:45,428 --> 01:27:48,263
AH, SAVE IT FOR
THE FINAL SCENE.

2466
01:27:48,263 --> 01:27:50,433
- OH, BUT OF COURSE.
- YOU’RE A BAILIFF.

2467
01:27:50,433 --> 01:27:52,668
I MUST ADMIT,
YOU TOOK ME IN COMPLETELY.

2468
01:27:52,668 --> 01:27:55,638
A POLICEMAN.
I NEVER THOUGHT.

2469
01:27:55,638 --> 01:27:56,973
YOU WEREN’T SUPPOSED TO.

2470
01:27:56,973 --> 01:27:58,540
LET’S GO.

2471
01:27:58,540 --> 01:28:01,510
NO, I SUPPOSE
I HAVE NO CHOICE.

2472
01:28:01,510 --> 01:28:03,478
NOW, HOW OFTEN ARE YOU GONNA
NEED A BUTTON LIKE THAT?

2473
01:28:03,478 --> 01:28:05,047
WELL, I GOT
AN ESPRESSO MACHINE.

2474
01:28:05,047 --> 01:28:07,350
I DON’T USE IT MUCH,
BUT IT’S NICE TO HAVE.

2475
01:28:07,350 --> 01:28:10,387
YOU GOT A POINT THERE.

2476
01:28:10,387 --> 01:28:12,088
OH, NOW WHERE’D HE GET
HIS FLASHLIGHT?

2477
01:28:12,088 --> 01:28:13,388
FOR CRYIN’ OUT LOUD.

2478
01:28:13,388 --> 01:28:15,792
A FOUR TRACK,
A WAFFLE IRON, AND SAUSAGES?

2479
01:28:15,792 --> 01:28:18,828
THEY’RE RECORDING BREAKFAST?

2480
01:28:18,828 --> 01:28:20,363
[SERVO YAWNS]

2481
01:28:20,363 --> 01:28:21,797
GET ME THE SHERIFF’S
OFFICE, QUICK.

2482
01:28:21,797 --> 01:28:23,967
THERE’S AN OUTSIDE.
THERE’S AN OUTSIDE.

2483
01:28:23,967 --> 01:28:25,468
HELLO, CASEY,
THIS IS A CODE THREE.

2484
01:28:25,468 --> 01:28:28,070
- LIEUTENANT HOUSTON.
- JIM? JIM-- JIMMY?

2485
01:28:28,070 --> 01:28:30,373
PUT YOUR MOTHER ON-- NO-NO,
DON’T HANG UP, JIMMY, NO!

2486
01:28:30,373 --> 01:28:32,175
YEAH, THEY KNOW WHERE I AM.
NOW GET ’EM ROLLING!

2487
01:28:32,175 --> 01:28:35,545
I’M GONNA ELOPE WITH MYSELF.
I LOVE ME.

2488
01:28:40,817 --> 01:28:43,052
[SERVO HUMS WITH SCORE]

2489
01:28:43,052 --> 01:28:44,520
VAN DAMME AND VAN DAMME

2490
01:28:44,520 --> 01:28:46,222
IN VAN DAMME YANKEES!

2491
01:28:46,222 --> 01:28:47,823
OOH.

2492
01:28:47,823 --> 01:28:49,025
[CROW HUMS]

2493
01:28:49,025 --> 01:28:50,993
IT’S CONFUSE-O-VISION AGAIN.

2494
01:28:50,993 --> 01:28:53,062
WHOO. IT’S WORKING.

2495
01:28:53,062 --> 01:28:54,663
♪ THERE’S A SCIENTIST
ON A SPREE ♪

2496
01:28:54,663 --> 01:28:57,300
♪ AND HE’S SKINNY
AS CAN BE ♪

2497
01:29:08,077 --> 01:29:09,545
OH, NUTS!

2498
01:29:09,545 --> 01:29:13,682
LOBO HAS THE KEYS!

2499
01:29:13,682 --> 01:29:16,585
OH, GO ON INSIDE
AND GET A COAT HANGER.

2500
01:29:16,585 --> 01:29:18,087
COME ON.

2501
01:29:18,087 --> 01:29:19,855
I HAVE NO IDEA WHERE
ANY OF THESE PEOPLE ARE.

2502
01:29:19,855 --> 01:29:21,457
WHAT’S GOING ON?

2503
01:29:21,457 --> 01:29:22,658
ONE ADAM TWELVE.

2504
01:29:22,658 --> 01:29:25,193
MOVIE NEEDS RESUSCITATION,
SEE THE MOVIE.

2505
01:29:25,193 --> 01:29:27,097
- REAGAN!
- YEAH.

2506
01:29:27,097 --> 01:29:28,663
WHAT’S THE PITCH, MARK?
IT’S CONWAY.

2507
01:29:28,663 --> 01:29:30,165
HE WAS OUT THERE SOMEWHERE.
I LOST HIM.

2508
01:29:30,165 --> 01:29:31,533
- NO ONE OUTSIDE.
- WE’D BETTER SPLIT UP.

2509
01:29:31,533 --> 01:29:33,502
- KENNEDY, YOU GO THAT WAY.
- AND STAY OFF THE SAUCE!

2510
01:29:33,502 --> 01:29:34,770
I’M GONNA CHECK THAT HOUSE.

2511
01:29:34,770 --> 01:29:36,305
ALL RIGHT, GOOD DEAL.
COME ON-- LET’S GO.

2512
01:29:39,542 --> 01:29:42,043
COME ON, OTIS,
YOU KNOW HOW TO DO THAT.

2513
01:29:42,043 --> 01:29:44,547
OTIS, COME ON.

2514
01:29:48,450 --> 01:29:50,285
AH, WELL, THERE’S, UM...

2515
01:29:50,285 --> 01:29:52,588
AH, THE KEY TO THE PLOT.

2516
01:29:52,588 --> 01:29:56,358
WHY IS THAT MIRROR
AT BELLY-BUTTON LEVEL?

2517
01:29:56,358 --> 01:29:58,127
IT’S A NAVEL-GAZER.

2518
01:29:58,127 --> 01:30:00,863
NO.

2519
01:30:00,863 --> 01:30:02,298
YOU’RE DEAD.

2520
01:30:02,298 --> 01:30:05,167
HERMAN! I’M NOT DEAD...

2521
01:30:05,167 --> 01:30:08,737
[SERVO MUMBLES]

2522
01:30:08,737 --> 01:30:12,408
WELL, THANK YOU,
I DIDN’T GET YOU ANYTHING.

2523
01:30:12,408 --> 01:30:13,542
I KNOW YOU’RE DEAD.

2524
01:30:13,542 --> 01:30:16,078
I TOLD EVERYBODY.

2525
01:30:16,078 --> 01:30:18,882
UH-OH.

2526
01:30:21,317 --> 01:30:23,820
THAT’S FOR THE BACH.

2527
01:30:23,820 --> 01:30:28,357
[DEFLATING SOUND]

2528
01:30:28,357 --> 01:30:29,758
DYING IS EASY.

2529
01:30:29,758 --> 01:30:31,960
COMEDY IS HARD.

2530
01:30:31,960 --> 01:30:34,930
I’LL SAY.

2531
01:30:34,930 --> 01:30:37,233
LET’S DANCE, I’LL LEAD.

2532
01:30:37,233 --> 01:30:39,035
DIP-- OOPS.

2533
01:30:39,035 --> 01:30:43,538
BLAME IT ON THE BOSSA NOVA.

2534
01:30:43,538 --> 01:30:45,273
LOBO.

2535
01:30:45,273 --> 01:30:47,042
UH...

2536
01:30:47,042 --> 01:30:49,478
REAGAN.

2537
01:30:49,478 --> 01:30:51,513
WELL, IT LOOKS LIKE
SOMEBODY SAVED THIS--

2538
01:30:51,513 --> 01:30:52,715
YEAH, BRING IN THE MEAT BAG.

2539
01:30:52,715 --> 01:30:55,050
PUT THIS PALOOKA
IN THE CHILLER.

2540
01:30:55,050 --> 01:30:56,585
WHO’S THIS GUY?

2541
01:30:56,585 --> 01:30:58,187
FELLA NAMED JEDROW.

2542
01:30:58,187 --> 01:31:00,657
CONWAY TRIED
TO BURY HIM ALIVE.

2543
01:31:00,657 --> 01:31:02,258
YOU KNOW, IT’S IRONIC.
I PULLED HIM OUT OF HIS GRAVE,

2544
01:31:02,258 --> 01:31:03,525
AND HE ENDS UP LIKE THIS.

2545
01:31:03,525 --> 01:31:05,728
I CAN SENSE THE IRONY.

2546
01:31:05,728 --> 01:31:07,630
WELL, AND THIS IS
CONWAY’S ASSISTANT.

2547
01:31:07,630 --> 01:31:09,132
YEAH, THE MILKMAN FOUND HER.

2548
01:31:09,132 --> 01:31:11,500
--WHAT DID YOU DO
WITH MS. THOMAS?

2549
01:31:11,500 --> 01:31:15,137
SHE’S IN THE LAB.

2550
01:31:15,137 --> 01:31:19,408
GEORGE,
GET THE CUFFS ON HIM.

2551
01:31:19,408 --> 01:31:21,110
CAPTAIN, YOU’D BETTER
COME DOWN TO THE CELLAR.

2552
01:31:21,110 --> 01:31:23,112
- NO!
- NO, NO, NOT THE CELLAR.

2553
01:31:23,112 --> 01:31:24,647
--YOU’D NEVER BELIEVE IT.

2554
01:31:24,647 --> 01:31:25,848
OKAY, LET’S GO.

2555
01:31:25,848 --> 01:31:30,553
WIPE THAT CHOCOLATE MILK
OFF YOUR LIP.

2556
01:31:30,553 --> 01:31:32,388
MY, OH MY, WHAT A--

2557
01:31:32,388 --> 01:31:33,957
OH, FORGET IT.

2558
01:31:33,957 --> 01:31:35,925
GRACE?

2559
01:31:35,925 --> 01:31:37,360
GRACE, WAKE UP.

2560
01:31:37,360 --> 01:31:38,727
COME ON.

2561
01:31:38,727 --> 01:31:40,328
SNAP OUT OF IT NOW,
COME ON.

2562
01:31:40,328 --> 01:31:42,332
GRACE BEFORE EVERY MEAL.

2563
01:31:42,332 --> 01:31:44,633
AMEN!

2564
01:31:44,633 --> 01:31:45,902
OH, IT’S A TEST PATTERN.

2565
01:31:45,902 --> 01:31:49,472
THEY TEMPORARILY
LOST THEIR SIGNAL.

2566
01:31:49,472 --> 01:31:51,407
LISTEN, IT’S ALL RIGHT.
EVERYTHING’S ALL RIGHT NOW.

2567
01:31:51,407 --> 01:31:52,675
THERE’S NOTHING MORE
TO WORRY ABOUT.

2568
01:31:52,675 --> 01:31:57,078
SLEEP!

2569
01:31:57,078 --> 01:31:58,882
OOPS.

2570
01:31:58,882 --> 01:32:01,483
I’VE CHECKED HIM.
HE’S DEAD.

2571
01:32:01,483 --> 01:32:03,118
THIS WAY, SIR.

2572
01:32:03,118 --> 01:32:04,320
SEE, THERE’S ONE IN HERE.

2573
01:32:04,320 --> 01:32:05,588
AND THEN I FOUND
ANOTHER ONE IN HERE.

2574
01:32:05,588 --> 01:32:06,855
THIS PLACE IS JUST
CRAWLING WITH STUFF

2575
01:32:06,855 --> 01:32:09,725
YOU WOULDN’T BELIEVE.

2576
01:32:09,725 --> 01:32:11,560
TAKE A DEEP BREATH.

2577
01:32:11,560 --> 01:32:13,495
[SCREAMS, GRUNTS]

2578
01:32:13,495 --> 01:32:17,367
HEY, THERE’S ANOTHER
MOVIE IN HERE.

2579
01:32:17,367 --> 01:32:19,135
OH, IT’S THE CAST
FOR QUEST FOR FIRE.

2580
01:32:19,135 --> 01:32:20,770
THEY SAVED
THE BEST FOR LAST.

2581
01:32:20,770 --> 01:32:24,840
WOW, BRIAN BOSWORTH
AND BEN DAVIDSON!

2582
01:32:24,840 --> 01:32:27,042
IAN ANDERSON-- AQUALUNG!

2583
01:32:27,042 --> 01:32:28,912
- OH.
- WOW.

2584
01:32:28,912 --> 01:32:30,078
DOCTOR, WHAT’RE
WE GONNA DO WITH THEM?

2585
01:32:30,078 --> 01:32:31,180
GET MICHAEL JACKSON
ON THE PHONE.

2586
01:32:31,180 --> 01:32:33,782
HE MAY WANNA BUY
ONE OF THESE GUYS.

2587
01:32:33,782 --> 01:32:35,852
WELL, IT’S A GOOD THING
WE HAVE INSTITUTIONS

2588
01:32:35,852 --> 01:32:38,320
THAT CAN TAKE GOOD CARE OF THEM
FOR THE REST OF THEIR LIVES.

2589
01:32:38,320 --> 01:32:43,325
THE BIRTH OF THE
WORLD WRESTLING FEDERATION.

2590
01:32:43,325 --> 01:32:45,527
OKAY, SO WHO
MUCKS OUT THE CAGES?

2591
01:32:45,527 --> 01:32:47,797
- [CREATURE SNORTS]
- EW.
- WHO?

2592
01:32:47,797 --> 01:32:49,932
- GOOD LORD.
- LIGHT A MATCH.

2593
01:32:49,932 --> 01:32:52,000
- YEAH, REALLY.
- --IF THEY DO LIVE FOREVER?

2594
01:32:52,000 --> 01:32:53,835
UH, LET’S JUST PRETEND
WE DIDN’T SEE THIS.

2595
01:32:53,835 --> 01:32:56,505
THINK OF THE PAPERWORK.

2596
01:32:56,505 --> 01:32:57,840
THAT SMELLED LIKE
A MONKEY HOUSE,

2597
01:32:57,840 --> 01:33:00,843
AND THEN I KNEW FOR SURE
THAT IT WAS-- OH.

2598
01:33:00,843 --> 01:33:02,110
LIEUTENANT, WHO IS THIS?
MY NEW GAL!

2599
01:33:02,110 --> 01:33:04,147
- LIEUTENANT?
- CAPTAIN REAGAN,

2600
01:33:04,147 --> 01:33:05,480
THIS IS MS. GRACE THOMAS.

2601
01:33:05,480 --> 01:33:07,248
SHE WAS ONE OF CONWAY’S
PATIENTS.

2602
01:33:07,248 --> 01:33:09,185
GRACE THOMAS?

2603
01:33:09,185 --> 01:33:10,853
HOW GLAD I AM TO SEE YOU,
YOUNG LADY.

2604
01:33:10,853 --> 01:33:12,288
YOU HAD US DRAGGING THE BAY
FOR TWO DAYS.

2605
01:33:12,288 --> 01:33:14,257
WE ALMOST HAD YOU
MARKED OFF AS A SUICIDE.

2606
01:33:14,257 --> 01:33:15,590
- SUICIDE?
- YEAH.

2607
01:33:15,590 --> 01:33:18,193
THAT’S A GOOD WAY
TO EXPLAIN HER DISAPPEARANCE.

2608
01:33:18,193 --> 01:33:19,728
CAPTAIN, YOU’D BETTER
GET AT A PICKUP

2609
01:33:19,728 --> 01:33:22,398
- ON A DR. LOREN WRIGHT.
- GOT MY OWN PICKUP RIGHT HERE.

2610
01:33:22,398 --> 01:33:23,932
--BROUGHT THE OTHERS, TOO.

2611
01:33:23,932 --> 01:33:25,702
YEAH, I’LL GET OUT
A CALL RIGHT AWAY.

2612
01:33:25,702 --> 01:33:28,137
COME ON, MILLER,
WE HAVE A LOT OF WORK TO DO.

2613
01:33:31,507 --> 01:33:32,942
LIFE’S FUNNY, HUH?

2614
01:33:32,942 --> 01:33:34,443
LIEUTENANT HOUSTON?

2615
01:33:34,443 --> 01:33:37,178
- MARK.
- OH, LIEUTENANT MARK.

2616
01:33:37,178 --> 01:33:38,813
WILL YOU PLEASE
TAKE ME HOME?

2617
01:33:38,813 --> 01:33:41,650
YEAH. YEAH,
OF COURSE I WILL.

2618
01:33:41,650 --> 01:33:44,553
THAT’S PART OF MY JOB.

2619
01:33:44,553 --> 01:33:47,990
I SEE.

2620
01:33:47,990 --> 01:33:49,658
- HEY.
- HEY.

2621
01:33:49,658 --> 01:33:51,527
- [SERVO SMOOCHES]
- HOW ABOUT BREAKFAST?

2622
01:33:53,728 --> 01:33:54,997
SHOULD I CALL YOU

2623
01:33:54,997 --> 01:33:57,400
OR JUST ROLL OVER
AND NUDGE YOU?

2624
01:33:57,400 --> 01:34:00,435
HI, I-- [MUFFLED VOICE]

2625
01:34:00,435 --> 01:34:03,305
- HE’S OFF THE RAMP.
WE HAVE LIFT-OFF!
- LET’S GO! LET’S GO!

2626
01:34:03,305 --> 01:34:05,073
- WHOO!
- YES! BROUGHT TO YOU
BY THE PEOPLE

2627
01:34:05,073 --> 01:34:07,777
OF CARTOON-HOUSE.

2628
01:34:19,755 --> 01:34:21,523
HOLY BUCKETS,
WHAT A COCK-AND-BULL

2629
01:34:21,523 --> 01:34:23,658
HOODOO PICTURE SHOW
THAT WAS, EH FELLAS?

2630
01:34:23,658 --> 01:34:25,493
BOY, THOSE OLD MOSS-BACKS

2631
01:34:25,493 --> 01:34:26,995
GIVE ME THE JIM-JAM
SOMETHIN’ AWFUL.

2632
01:34:26,995 --> 01:34:28,630
YEAH, I’D GIVE THAT
HONK UP THE NIXIE,

2633
01:34:28,630 --> 01:34:30,365
BUT HEY, WE’RE REALLY
FOOTIN’ IT ON THE LINGO.

2634
01:34:30,365 --> 01:34:31,700
YEAH, WE CAN CHIP PEG AWAY

2635
01:34:31,700 --> 01:34:33,235
WITH A PEDDLER’S FRENCH,
EH PAL OF MINE?

2636
01:34:33,235 --> 01:34:35,805
YEAH, WE’RE GOIN’ HI-HAT
IN A BIG WAY, FELLAS.

2637
01:34:35,805 --> 01:34:37,840
- HOT, SWEET, AND FILTHY!
- YEAH, OKAY.

2638
01:34:37,840 --> 01:34:39,208
NOW ZIP IT,
YOU MUTTONHEADS.

2639
01:34:39,208 --> 01:34:40,843
WE GOT A BUG-LETTER
TO SLING.

2640
01:34:40,843 --> 01:34:42,343
MAN, AIN’T THAT JAKE!

2641
01:34:42,343 --> 01:34:44,780
YEAH, LET’S PUT IT--
BOOST IT, CAMBOT, OKAY?

2642
01:34:44,780 --> 01:34:46,782
HOO, OKAY, HERE WE GO.

2643
01:34:46,782 --> 01:34:50,018
IT SAYS HERE,
"DEAR JOEL AND DA BOTS--"

2644
01:34:50,018 --> 01:34:51,787
- [BOTS] HEY, DAT’S ME!
- RIGHT, BUTTON IT.

2645
01:34:51,787 --> 01:34:53,288
OKAY, BUTTON IT, YOU GUMS.

2646
01:34:53,288 --> 01:34:55,623
OKAY, SAYS HERE,
I HAVE A COUPLE OF QUESTIONS

2647
01:34:55,623 --> 01:34:57,158
ABOUT TOM SERVO.

2648
01:34:57,158 --> 01:34:58,560
- EH!
- FIRST,

2649
01:34:58,560 --> 01:35:00,997
WHY CAN’T WE
SEE THROUGH TOM’S HEAD

2650
01:35:00,997 --> 01:35:03,798
WHEN YOU GUYS
ARES WATCHIN’ THE MOVIE?

2651
01:35:03,798 --> 01:35:06,135
EVEN THOUGH HIS HEAD
IS TRAMSPARENT?

2652
01:35:06,135 --> 01:35:08,670
- HUH.
- HMM, AND SECOND?

2653
01:35:08,670 --> 01:35:10,405
HOW CAN TOM
EVEN WATCH THE MOVIE

2654
01:35:10,405 --> 01:35:12,542
WHEN HE DOESN’T HAVE
ANY PEEPERS?

2655
01:35:12,542 --> 01:35:14,343
WELL, DON’T THAT
BEAT THE DUTCH.

2656
01:35:14,343 --> 01:35:16,678
YEAH, YEAH,
I THINK OLD LAUGHIN’ BOY

2657
01:35:16,678 --> 01:35:18,280
IS PULLING A FAST ONE ON US
IS WHAT I THINK.

2658
01:35:18,280 --> 01:35:20,382
HEY, WHAT GIVES,
I AIN’T NO BAD PILL!

2659
01:35:20,382 --> 01:35:22,283
HONEST, FELLAS,
YOU’VE BEEN DONE UP BROWN!

2660
01:35:22,283 --> 01:35:24,453
AH, CUT WITH THE BABY ACT.
COME ON, CLOD.

2661
01:35:24,453 --> 01:35:26,322
SO, DIS MUG WAS GONNA
GIVE US THE BOOST, HUH?

2662
01:35:26,322 --> 01:35:28,423
GONNA CUT UP WITH DIDDY-O’S
WITH HIS OLD PALLIES.

2663
01:35:28,423 --> 01:35:29,558
- NO, NO!
- WHY, I OUGHTA--

2664
01:35:29,558 --> 01:35:31,293
HEY, CROW, ROUTINE 27.

2665
01:35:31,293 --> 01:35:33,562
[ALL SHOUT]

2666
01:35:33,562 --> 01:35:35,865
WE’RE JUST PULLIN’ YOUR PANTS,
GUMPY, TAKE IT EASY.

2667
01:35:35,865 --> 01:35:37,332
YEAH, BOY OH BOY, WE REALLY

2668
01:35:37,332 --> 01:35:38,533
HAD YOU BY
THE FAT END, PALLY.

2669
01:35:38,533 --> 01:35:40,468
D’AH, YOU SAPS.

2670
01:35:40,468 --> 01:35:42,137
HEY, HEY, FOOT IT, BOYS.

2671
01:35:42,137 --> 01:35:43,772
HIS NIBS IS CALLIN’
ON THE OTHER LINE.

2672
01:35:43,772 --> 01:35:45,808
SO WHAT’S IT TO YOU,
EINSTEIN?

2673
01:35:45,808 --> 01:35:47,743
LOOK, YOU BOMBASTIC
BISCUIT BOY,

2674
01:35:47,743 --> 01:35:50,312
ANYMORE OF THIS FAUX
DEAD END KIDS PATOIS

2675
01:35:50,312 --> 01:35:51,580
AND I’LL TEACH YOU
THE REAL MEANING

2676
01:35:51,580 --> 01:35:53,315
OF LEXIPHANICISM

2677
01:35:53,315 --> 01:35:55,117
- OR WHAT--
- HEY, BOSS, THIS IS GOOD GRUB.

2678
01:35:55,117 --> 01:35:56,685
THAT PADRE,
HE’S NOT A HALF-BAD EGG.

2679
01:35:56,685 --> 01:35:58,387
YOU KNOW, I COULD REALLY GET
INTO EATING GRUB LIKE THIS

2680
01:35:58,387 --> 01:35:59,888
IF I COULD BE
A JUNIOR G-MAN.

2681
01:35:59,888 --> 01:36:03,158
FRANK, WHY MUST YOU ALWAYS
GO ON WITH YOUR LITTLE--

2682
01:36:03,158 --> 01:36:04,893
HEY, BOSS,
DO YOUR LEO GORCEY.

2683
01:36:04,893 --> 01:36:06,762
- COME ON, YOU DO A GREAT
- I’M NOT GOING TO DO MY LEO--

2684
01:36:06,762 --> 01:36:08,663
HE DOES A GREAT LEO--
DO YOUR LEO GORCEY, C’MON.

2685
01:36:08,663 --> 01:36:10,298
- COME ON. COME ON.
- NO, FRANK, FRANK,

2686
01:36:10,298 --> 01:36:13,368
ONCE AGAIN, I’M GOING
TO HAVE TO KILL YOU.

2687
01:36:13,368 --> 01:36:15,070
YOU WANNA RUN THAT BY ME
ONE MORE TIME?

2688
01:36:15,070 --> 01:36:17,973
RUN THAT BY YOU
ONE MORE TIME?

2689
01:36:17,973 --> 01:36:20,175
YEAH, YOU KNOW, KILL!

2690
01:36:20,175 --> 01:36:23,145
BOOST, ICE, WACK, SCRAG,

2691
01:36:23,145 --> 01:36:25,580
DOUSE, STIFLE, 86.

2692
01:36:25,580 --> 01:36:27,817
UH, SLIP THE ROSCOE, CHILL.

2693
01:36:27,817 --> 01:36:30,820
DUST, YANK,
TOSS A LITTLE KICKSHAW.

2694
01:36:30,820 --> 01:36:33,588
ROGER.

2695
01:36:33,588 --> 01:36:36,192
♪♪ [THEME]

2696
01:37:35,383 --> 01:37:36,918
TIME FOR GO TO BED.
